<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.01.170      Personal obligation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.01.180      Enforcement power.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>I.
GENERAL PROVISIONS</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.01.010 
Definitions.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  For the purpose of all business license ordinances the
words and phrases used herein, unless the context otherwise indicates, shall
have the following meanings:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A. 
&quot;Certificate&quot; means any certificate or renewal of certificate issued
pursuant to any business license ordinance;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B. 
&quot;Director&quot; means for taxicabs and for-hire drivers and vehicles the
manager of the records and licensing services division, department of executive
services or designee.  For all other business licenses, permits or
certificates, &quot;director&quot; means the manager of the department of local
services, permitting division or designee;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C. 
&quot;License&quot; means any license or renewal of license issued pursuant to
any business license ordinance;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D. 
&quot;Licensee&quot; means any person to whom a license or renewal of license
has been issued pursuant to any business license ordinance;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E. 
&quot;Permit&quot; means any permit or renewal of permit issued pursuant to any
business license ordinance;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F. 
&quot;Person&quot; means any individual, partnership, firm, joint stock
company, corporation, association, trust, estate or other legal entity;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            G. 
&quot;Registrant&quot; means any person to whom a registration or renewal of
registration has been issued pursuant to any business license ordinance;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            H. 
&quot;Registration&quot; means any registration or renewal of registration
issued pursuant to any business license ordinance.  (Ord. 18791 § 44, 2018: 
Ord. 18728 § 1, 2018:  Ord. 17420 § 10, 2012:  Ord. 15971 § 46, 2007:  Ord.
14199 § 114, 2001:  Ord. 1888 Art. I § 2, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.01.030  Additional
rules and regulations.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The director is authorized to make
and enforce rules and regulations, not inconsistent with any business license
ordinance, and it is unlawful to violate or fail to comply with any of the
rules and regulations.  All such rules and regulations as promulgated by the
director shall be reduced to writing and mailed to each licensee or permit
holder.  The licensee or permittee shall distribute such rules and regulations to
the licensee or permit holder's registrants or employees.  (Ord. 18728 § 2, 2018: 
Ord. 1888 Art. I. § 4, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.01.040  Authority
to suspend or revoke licenses, registration or permits.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
The director shall have the right to suspend or revoke any business license,
registration or permit issued upon a showing of violation of any of the
provisions of any business license ordinance; provided, however, that such
suspension or revocation shall not relieve the licensee, registrant or permit
holder of the other penalties otherwise provided for in any business license
ordinance.  (Ord. 1888 Art. V § 1, 1974: Ord. 997 § 1, 1971).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>II.
LICENSING PROVISIONS</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.01.050  License,
registration or permit fee &#8209; refunds.</span></b><span style='font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Any application
or issuance or renewal of a license, registration or permit pursuant to any
business license ordinance shall not be accepted by the director unless
accompanied by the appropriate license, registration or permit fee.  In the
event an application for a license, registration or permit fee is refused, the
amount tendered as the license, registration or permit fee shall not be
returned to the applicant but shall go to the county to defray the cost of
examination or investigation, or both; provided, however, that this section
shall not apply to the fee paid for a novelty amusement device operator's
license.  (Ord. 1888 Art. II § 1, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.01.060  Form
of license, registration, permit or certificate.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
All licenses, registrations, permits or certificates, issued pursuant to any
business license ordinance, shall be in a form prescribed by the director. 
(Ord. 1888 Art. II § 2, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.01.070  Posting
of license, registration, permit or certificate.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
Any license, registration, permit or certificate, issued pursuant to any
business license ordinance, shall be posted in a conspicuous place in the place
of business of the licensee, registrant, permit or certificate holder.  (Ord.
1888 Art. II § 3, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.01.080  Change
of address.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Any person licensed, registered or permitted pursuant
to any business license ordinance shall notify the director of any change in address
or business name, or in the officers, directors or partners of the person,
within fourteen days of any such change.  (Ord. 18728 § 3, 2018:  Ord. 1888
Art. II § 4, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.01.090  License,
registration, permit or certificate not an endorsement.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
No license, registration, permit or certificate, issued pursuant to any
business license ordinance, shall be an endorsement of such business licensed,
registered, permitted or certificated under any business license ordinance. 
(Ord. 1888 Art. II § 5, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.01.100  Enforcement
agreements with other municipalities.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The director is
authorized to enter into agreements with any or all other municipal
corporations in King County for the licensing and enforcement of local
ordinances relating to businesses or entertainments licensed, registered or
permitted pursuant to any business license ordinance; provided, that any
municipal corporation entering into such an agreement shall enact an ordinance
substantially similar to the applicable King County business license
ordinance.  (Ord. 1888 Art. II § 6, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>III.
ENFORCEMENT, PROCEDURE AND</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>PENALTY
PROVISIONS</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.01.110  Inspections
- right of entry.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The
director is authorized to make such inspections and take such action as may be
required to enforce any business license ordinance.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  Whenever
necessary to make an inspection to enforce any of the provisions of any
business license ordinance, or whenever the director has reasonable cause to
believe that a licensee, registrant or permit holder is operating in violation
of any business license ordinance, the director may enter such licensee's,
registrant's or permit holder's place of business or entertainment, which is
licensed, registered or permitted pursuant to any business license ordinance,
at all reasonable times to inspect the same or perform any duty imposed on the
director by any business license ordinance; provided, that, 1. if the place of
business or entertainment is occupied, the director shall first present proper
credentials and demand entry; and 2. if the place of business or entertainment
is unoccupied, the director shall first make a reasonable effort to locate the
licensee, registrant or permit holder or other person or persons having charge
or control of the place of business or entertainment and demand entry.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  No person
shall fail or neglect, after proper demand, to admit the director, while acting
within the scope of the director's employment, to any place of business or
entertainment licensed, registered or permitted pursuant to any business
license ordinance, or to interfere with the director while in the performance
of the director's duty.  (Ord. 18728 § 4, 2018:  Ord. 1888 Art. III § 1, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.01.120  Duties
of the director.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The director is authorized and directed to enforce the
terms and provisions of all business license ordinances.  If it is determined,
by means of investigation or inspection, that any person has violated or failed
to comply with any provision of any business license ordinance, then the
director shall issue a notice and order recording such findings, specifying
therein the particulars of any such violation or failure to comply.  (Ord. 1888
Art. III § 2, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.01.130 
Notice and order.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The
director shall issue a notice and order, pursuant to K.C.C. 6.01.120, directed
to the person whom the director has determined to be in violation of any of the
terms and provisions of any business license ordinance.  The notice and order
shall contain:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  The
street address, when available, and a legal description sufficient for
identification of the premises upon which the violation occurred;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  A
statement that the director has found the conduct of the person to be in
violation of any business license ordinance, with a brief and concise
description of the conditions found to render the person in violation of the business
license ordinance;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  A
statement of any action required to be taken as determined by the director.  If
the director has determined to assess a civil penalty, the order shall require
that the penalty shall be paid within a time certain from the date of the order
as determined by the director to be reasonable;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  A
statement of any action taken by the director; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              5.  Statements
advising that:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                a.(1)  the
person may appeal from the notice and order of any action of the director
arising under K.C.C. chapter 6.64, for-hire transportation, to the office of
the hearing examiner in accordance with K.C.C. 20.22.080; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                  (2)  the
person may appeal from the notice and order any action of the director, other
than those arising under K.C.C. chapter 6.64, to the office of the hearing
examiner, but only if the appeal is made in writing as provided in this chapter
and filed with the director within seven days from the date of service of such
notice and order;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                b.  the
failure to appeal will constitute a waiver of all right to an administrative
hearing and determination of the matter.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The notice
and order, and any amended or supplemental notice and order, shall be served
upon the person either personally or by mailing a copy of the notice and order
by certified mail, postage prepaid, return receipt requested to the person at the
person’s address as it appears on the license, registration or permit.  Service
by certified mail in the manner provided in this section shall be effective on
the date of mailing.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  Proof of
service of the notice and order shall be made at the time of service by a
written declaration under penalty of perjury executed by the person effecting
service, declaring the time, date, and manner in which service was made.  (<span
style='color:black'>Ord. 18230 § 78, 2016:  </span>Ord. 1888 Art. III § 3,
1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.01.140  Civil
penalty.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  In addition to or as an alternative to any other
penalty provided herein or by law any person who violates any provision of any
business license ordinance shall be subject to a civil penalty in an amount not
to exceed two hundred fifty dollars per violation to be directly assessed by
the director.  The director, in a reasonable manner, may vary the amount of the
penalty assessed to consider the appropriateness of the penalty to the size of
the business of the violator; the license, registration or permit fee required
of the violator; the gravity of the violation; the number of past and present
violations committed and the good faith of the violator in attempting to
achieve compliance after notification of the violation.  All civil penalties
assessed will be enforced and collected in accordance with the procedure
specified in this chapter. (Ord. 1888 Art.  III § 4, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.01.150 
Appeals.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The office
of the hearing examiner is designated to hear appeals by parties aggrieved by
actions of the director pursuant to any business license ordinance.  For
appeals under K.C.C. chapter 6.65 the office of the hearing examiner is
designated to hear such appeals unless a different party is designated by the
director.  The examiner may adopt reasonable rules or regulations for
conducting its business.  Copies of all rules and regulations adopted by the examiner
shall be delivered to the director, who shall make them freely accessible to
the public.  All decisions and findings of the examiner shall be rendered to
the appellant in writing, with a copy to the director.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  For-hire
transportation appeals under K.C.C. chapter 6.64 shall be filed in accordance
with K.C.C. 20.22.080 and the hearing process conducted in accordance with
K.C.C. chapter 20.22.  Appeals under K.C.C. chapter 6.65 shall be filed in
accordance with K.C.C. 6.65.450 and the hearing process conducted in accordance
with that same section.  Subsections C. through H. of this section do not apply
to this subsection B.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  Any person
entitled to service under K.C.C. 6.01.130 may appeal any notice and order or
any action of the director by filing at the office of the director within seven
days from the date of service of such order, a written appeal containing;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  A
heading in the words:  &quot;Before the Office of the Hearing Examiner&quot;;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  A
caption reading:  &quot;Appeal of ..........&quot; giving the names of all
appellants participating in the appeal;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  A brief
statement setting forth the legal interest of each of the appellants in the
business or entertainment involved in the notice and order;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  A brief
statement in concise language of the specific order or action protested,
together with any material facts claimed to support the contentions of the
appellant;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              5.  A brief
statement in concise language of the relief sought, and the reasons why it is
claimed the protested order or action should be reversed, modified, or
otherwise set aside;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              6.  The
signatures of all parties named as appellants, and their official mailing
addresses; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              7.  The
verification (by declaration under penalty of perjury) of at least one
appellant as to the truth of the matters stated in the appeal.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  As soon as
practicable after receiving the written appeal, the examiner shall fix a date,
time, and place for the hearing of the appeal.  The date shall be neither less
than ten days nor more than sixty days from the date the appeal was filed with
the director.  Written notice of the time and place of the hearing shall be
given at least ten days before the date of the hearing to each appellant by the
examiner either by causing a copy of the notice to be delivered to the
appellant personally or by mailing a copy thereof, postage prepaid, addressed
to the appellant at the appellant’s address shown on the appeal.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  At the
hearing the appellant shall be entitled to appear in person, be represented by
counsel, and offer such evidence as is pertinent and material to the action of
the director.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F.  Only those
matters or issues specifically raised by the appellant in the written notice of
appeal shall be considered in the hearing of the appeal.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            G.  Failure of
any person to file an appeal in accordance with this section shall constitute a
waiver of the person's right to an administrative hearing and adjudication of
the notice and order, or any portion thereof.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            H. 
Enforcement of any notice and order of the director shall be stayed during the
pendency of an appeal therefrom that is properly and timely filed.  (Ord. 19940
§ 2, 2025:  Ord. 19700 § 58, 2024:  Ord. 19030 § 2, 2019:  Ord. 18728 § 5, 2018: 
<span style='color:black'>Ord. 18230 § 79, 2016: </span> Ord. 1888 Art. III §
5, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.01.160 
Violations &#8209; misdemeanor.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Any person violating or
failing to comply with any of the provisions of any business license ordinance
shall be deemed guilty of a misdemeanor and upon conviction thereof shall be
punished by a fine in any sum not to exceed two hundred fifty dollars or by
imprisonment in the King County jail for a period not to exceed ninety days.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>(Ord. 1888 Art. III § 6,
1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.01.170 
Personal obligation.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The civil penalty is a personal obligation of the
licensee, registrant or permit holder.  The prosecuting attorney, on behalf of
King County, may collect the civil penalty by use of all appropriate legal
remedies.  (Ord. 1888 Art. III § 7, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.01.180 
Enforcement power.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The director is authorized to take such lawful action,
including the writing and issuance of misdemeanor citations, as may be required
to enforce the provisions of any business license ordinance codified in this
title.  (Ord. 4514 § 1, 1979).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc319998435"></a><a name="_Toc28263349">6.04      AMUSEMENT
DEVICES</a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>I.
 NOVELTY AMUSEMENT DEVICES</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.010      Definitions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.020      License required &#8209;
Operation near schools prohibited.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.030      Operation without licenses
prohibited.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.040      License Fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.060      Novelty amusement device
vendor's license.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.070      Application procedure.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.090      Financial interest prohibited.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.100      Denial of licenses.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.110      Suspension or revocation of
licenses.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.120      Effective date.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.130      Renewal of license,
registration or permit &#8209; Late penalty.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.140      Violation &#8209; Misdemeanor.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.150      Civil penalty.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.160      Additional enforcement.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>II.
 SHUFFLEBOARDS</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.170      Shuffleboard defined.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.180      License required - fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.190      Display, removal and transfer
of license.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.200      Information required on
application for license - qualifications required of applicant.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.210      Renewal of license,
registration or permit - late penalty.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.220      Penalty for violation - confiscation
of shuffleboard.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.230      Civil penalty.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.240      Additional enforcement.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>I.
NOVELTY AMUSEMENT DEVICES*</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Prior resolution history:
Res. 11956, as amended by Res. 12715, 16484 and 3561. Gambling devices unlawful
&#8209; See K.C.C. 12.56.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.010 
Definitions.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A. 
&quot;Financial interest&quot; means any direct or indirect ownership of the
premises of business located therein through corporate stock ownership,
partnership, trust or otherwise.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  &quot;Novelty
amusement device&quot; includes any coin&#8209;operated or remote controlled
machine, device, contrivance, apparatus or appliance, mechanical, electrical or
hand propelled, designed to be used in whole or in part as an instrument or
instrumentality for engaging in the use and exercise of skill by one or more
persons in playing a game for the amusement and entertainment of the player or
players and which is maintained commercially for such purpose.  Such novelty
amusement device shall not be used for the purpose of awarding any money or
object of value to the player or players, and shall not contain any mechanism
which varies the chance of winning free games or the number of free games which
may be won, depending on the number of coins inserted into the device; provided
that in no event shall a machine be licensed which is so designed and equipped
as to render it of practical utility only as a device to be used for gambling.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  &quot;Novelty
amusement device distributor&quot; means any person who leases or rents to, or
places with others, any novelty amusement device for use, play or operation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  &quot;Novelty
amusement device owner&quot; means any person who owns a novelty amusement
device and operates the device on premises owned or leased by said person.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  &quot;Novelty
amusement device vendor&quot; means any person who engages in the business of
selling, exchanging or offering or exhibiting for sale or exchange, more than
three novelty amusement devices in a year period.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F.  &quot;Substantial
connection&quot; means:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  In a
sole proprietorship, the individual owns, operates, manages or conducts,
directly or indirectly, the applicant; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  In a
partnership, the individual shares in any potential profits of the applicant;
or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  In a
corporation, if the individual is an officer, director or a holder (directly or
beneficially) of more than ten percent of any class of stock; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  The
individual furnishes more than ten percent of the capital of such applicant,
whether in cash, goods or services.  (Ord. 2287 § 1, 1975:  Ord. 69 § 1, 1969).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.020  License
required &#8209; Operation near schools prohibited.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
No novelty amusement device shall be operated or kept for operation in King
County outside of the limits of incorporated cities and towns unless licenses
for the operation thereof have been taken out as hereinafter required;
provided, however, that in no event shall any novelty amusement device be
operated within five hundred feet of any elementary, middle, junior high or
high school.  (Ord. 1684 § 1, 1973: Ord. 69 § 2, 1969).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.030  Operation
without licenses prohibited.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No owner, operator or
other person in charge of any place of business shall operate, or permit to be
in such place of business for operation, any novelty amusement device unless
such device is licensed pursuant to Sections 6.04.040 and 6.04.080.  (Ord. 2287
§ 2, 1975: Ord. 69 § 3, 1969).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.040  License
Fee.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The license fee for each amusement device shall be $100
per year.  License fees for less than one year shall be prorated.  The fee for
such license or portion thereof shall be payable on January 1st of each year. 
(Ord. 10170 § 1, 1991:  Ord. 6260 § 2, 1982).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.060  Novelty
amusement device vendor's license.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  No person
shall engage in the business of selling or offering or exhibiting for sale more
than three novelty amusement devices in a year without a novelty amusement
device vendor's license.  However, the requirement for such a license shall not
exist where the director determines the intent of the seller, offeror or
exhibitor is not to engage in this business.  In determining this intent the
director shall consider and weigh in a reasonable manner the following factors,
to include but not be limited by:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            1.  Nature of
the sale;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            2.  Parties to
the sale;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            3.  Frequency
of sales in the past;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4.  Volume of
the sale;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            5.  Bargaining
position of the parties to the sale;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.  Position
of the parties after the sale;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            7.  Effect of
the license requirement on the parties;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            8.  Good faith
of the parties; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            9.  Protection
of buyer regarding servicing and maintenance of the device(s) if bond is not
required.  The fee for such license shall be five hundred dollars per year
payable on January 1 of each year or portion thereof.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  Each
applicant for a novelty amusement device vendor's license shall file with the
director a surety bond in a form approved by the director, executed by a surety
company authorized to do business in this state running to the county of King,
state of Washington in the sum of ten thousand dollars conditioned that the
applicant&#8209;vendor will furnish parts and repairs to any person to whom the
applicant-vendor may sell any novelty amusement device for a period of two
years after the sale.  The bond shall state that it is for the use or benefit
of the vendee who may have a cause of action against the vendor on the bond by
reason of breach of the condition.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  The
director shall deny the application for a license if the applicant fails to
satisfy the surety bond requirement.  (Ord. 18728 § 6, 2018:  Ord. 2287 § 6,
1975).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.070  Application
procedure.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No license or renewal of any license provided for by
this chapter shall be issued or renewed except upon written application to the
director, signed and sworn to by the person who intends to utilize the
license.  Such application shall contain the following information:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The
business name, business address and telephone number of the applicant;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  In
relation to each natural person having a substantial connection with such
business:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            1.  True name
and any other name by which commonly known,</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            2.  Residence
address and telephone number,</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            3.  Date and
place of birth,</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4.  Length of
residence in King County; if less than one year then the prior address outside
King County,</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            5.  Nature of
relationship to business,</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.  Within ten
years of date of application, has pleaded guilty to or been convicted of
violating any ordinance, resolution or law other than traffic offenses, of any
jurisdiction.  If so, full circumstances thereof including but not limited to
date, court and case disposition;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  In
relation to each corporation or partnership having a substantial connection
with such applicant:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            1.  Name of
the corporation or partnership,</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            2.  Name of
registered agent and address of registered office,</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            3.  Primary
office address, if different from above,</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            4.  Date and
place of incorporation or organization,</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            5.  Date and
place of filing of articles,</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6. Nature of
relationship to applicant,</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            7.  Names and
residence addresses of all officers, directors, limited or general partners,
and holders (directly or beneficially) of more than ten percent of any class of
stock;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  Such other
information as the director may reasonably require to determine the
advisability of license issuance.  (Ord. 2287 § 7, 1975).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.090  Financial
interest prohibited.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No holder of a novelty amusement device distributor's
license shall have any financial interest in the premises whereon said
distributor leases, rents or places a novelty amusement device.  (Ord. 2287 §
8, 1975).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.100  Denial
of licenses.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> The director may deny issuance of any license under this
chapter if the applicant or any of its officers, directors or partners have:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Made any
false statement in the application;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  Committed
any act, while unlicensed, for which a license is required under the provisions
of this chapter;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  Committed
any act resulting in a conviction within ten years of a felony or a crime
involving moral turpitude which is reasonably related to the license applied
for;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  Been
refused a license or had a license revoked under the provisions of this
chapter; provided however, that any applicant denied a license may reapply
after six months, if the basis for denial no longer exists;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  Not
resided in the state of Washington for at least five years prior to an
application for a novelty amusement device distributor's license;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F.  Failed to
comply with the building, zoning and fire codes of King County.  (Ord. 2287 §
9, 1975).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.110  Suspension
or revocation of licenses.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The director may suspend or revoke
any license under this chapter if the applicant or any of its officers,
directors or partners have:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Committed
any act which is a ground for denial of any license under this chapter;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  Violated
any of the provisions of this chapter.  (Ord. 2287 § 10, 1975).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.120  Effective
date.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The provisions of this chapter shall not become
effective until January 1, 1975; provided however, that any person desiring to
apply for a novelty amusement device owner's license may do so and may be
granted such license upon compliance with the provisions of this chapter; and
further provided, that any person holding a license in 1974 pursuant to King
County Code Section 6.04.030, who applied for such license after June 30, 1974,
shall be credited by the county for the 1975 license year in the amount of two
thousand five hundred dollars.  (Ord. 2287 § 11, 1975).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.130  Renewal
of license, registration or permit &#8209; Late penalty.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
A late penalty shall be charged on all applications for renewal of a license,
registration or permit received later than ten working days after the
expiration date of such license, registration or permit as set forth in the
respective resolution or ordinance establishing the expiration date of such
license, registration or permit.  The amount of such penalty is fixed as
follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            For a license,
registration or permit requiring a fee of fifty cents or more, but less than
fifty dollars &#8209; twenty percent of the required fee;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            For a license,
registration or permit requiring a fee of fifty cents or more, but less than
one thousand dollars &#8209; ten percent of the required fee;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            For a license,
registration or permit requiring a fee of one thousand dollars or more &#8209;
five percent of the required fee.  (Ord. 1888 Art. IV § 3, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.140  Violation
&#8209; Misdemeanor.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Any violation of this article constitutes a misdemeanor
and the punishment shall be as provided by the laws of the state of
Washington.  (Ord. 126 (part), 1969:  Ord. 69 § 17, 1969).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.150  Civil
penalty.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  In addition to or as an alternative to any other
penalty provided herein or by law any person who violates any provision of any
business license ordinance shall be subject to a civil penalty in an amount not
to exceed two hundred fifty dollars per violation to be directly assessed by
the director.  The director, in a reasonable manner, may vary the amount of </span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>the penalty assessed to
consider the appropriateness of the penalty to the size of the business of the
violator; the gravity of the violation; the number of past and present
violations committed and the good faith of the violator in attempting to
achieve compliance after notification of the violation.  All civil penalties
assessed will be enforced and collected in accordance with the procedure
specified under this title.  (Ord. 1888 Art. IV § 1, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.160  Additional
enforcement.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Notwithstanding the existence or use of any other
remedy the director may seek legal or equitable relief to enjoin any acts or
practices which constitute or will constitute a violation of any business
license ordinance or other regulations herein adopted.  (Ord. 1888 Art. IV § 2,
1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>II.
SHUFFLEBOARDS</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.170  Shuffleboard
defined.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  For the purpose of this chapter,
&quot;shuffleboard&quot; means any game consisting of a raised table or
platform in the shape of an elongated rectangle that is supported on legs or a
frame, that has surfaces with scoring areas and that is played by a hand-propelled
ball, disk, puck or similar object and for which the winner or score is
calculated by the resulting positions of such ball, disk, puck or similar
object.  Shuffleboards owned by establishment owners may be coin operated under
the control of the establishment owner or designee and subject to inspection by
the director.  An establishment owner may own the shuffleboard to be used only
on those premises.  The establishment owner shall be required to pay a location
license fee.  (Ord. 18728 § 7, 2018:  Ord. 1176 § 1, 1972:  Res. 12714 § 1,
1951).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.180  License
required - fee.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No shuffleboard shall be operated or kept for operation
in King County outside of the limits of incorporated cities and towns unless a
license for the operation thereof has been taken out as hereinafter provided,
and the license fee for each shuffleboard shall be $50.00 per year.  (Ord.
10170 § 2, 1991:  Ord. 1982 § 1, 1974: Res. 12714 § 2, 1951).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.190  Display,
removal and transfer of license.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Licenses shall be
furnished in a form suitable to be attached to the shuffleboard licensed
thereby.  No such license shall be removed or detached from one shuffleboard
and transferred to another.  (Ord. 1888 Art. V § 6, 1974:  Res. 12714 § 3,
1951).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.200  Information
required on application for license - qualifications</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> <b>required
of applicant.</b>  The licenses set forth in this article shall be issued only
upon written application therefor, which application shall be presented to the
director, upon forms provided by the director, and must state the names and
residences of the owners and parties who operate, maintain or offer for use or
play any such shuffleboard, the location where each of the same is to be
operated, maintained or offered for use or play, and the number of shuffleboards
at each location, and the license shall only be issued to applicants of good
moral character and financial responsibility.  If the applicant is a partnership,
each partner must possess the above qualifications.  If applicant is a
corporation, the corporation must be licensed to do business in the state of
Washington, and its officers, manager and/or agents must possess the
qualifications set forth in this section. (Ord. 18728 § 8, 2018:  Ord. 1888
Art. V § 7, 1974:  Res. 12714 § 4, 1951).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.210  Renewal
of license, registration or permit - late penalty.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
A late penalty shall be charged on all applications for renewal of a license,
registration or permit received later than ten working days after the
expiration date of such license, registration or permit, as set forth in the
respective resolution or ordinance establishing the expiration date of such
license, registration or permit.  The amount of such penalty is fixed as
follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  For a
license, registration or permit requiring a fee of fifty cents or more, but
less than fifty dollars, twenty percent of the required fee;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  For a
license, registration or permit requiring a fee of fifty dollars or more, but
less than one thousand dollars, ten percent of the required fee;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  For a
license, registration or permit requiring a fee of one thousand dollars or
more, five percent of the required fee.  (Ord. 1888 Art. IV § 3, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.220  Penalty
for violation - confiscation of shuffleboard.</span></b><span style='font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Any person
violating any of the terms of this article shall, upon conviction thereof, be
fined in the sum of not less than fifty dollars nor more than three hundred
dollars or imprisoned in the county jail for not more than ninety days, or
both, and any shuffleboard being operated, maintained, kept or displayed in
violation of this article shall, in the discretion of the court before which
the violation is prosecuted, be confiscated by King County.  (Res. 12714 § 7,
1951).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.230  Civil
penalty.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  In addition to or as an alternative to any other
penalty provided herein or by law, any person who violates any provision of any
business license ordinance shall be subject to a civil penalty in an amount not
to exceed two hundred fifty dollars per violation, to be directly assessed by
the director.  The director, in a reasonable manner, may vary the amount of the
penalty assessed to consider the appropriateness of the penalty to the size of
the business of the violator; the gravity of the violation; the number of past
and present violations committed; and the good faith of the violator in
attempting to achieve compliance after notification of the violation.  All
civil penalties assessed will be enforced and collected in accordance with the
procedure specified under this title.  (Ord. 1888 Art. IV § 1, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.04.240  Additional
enforcement.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Notwithstanding the existence or use of any other
remedy, the director may seek legal or equitable relief to enjoin any acts or
practices which constitute or will constitute a violation of any business
license ordinance or other regulations herein adopted.  (Ord. 1888 Art IV § 2,
1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc319998436"></a><a name="_Toc28263350">6.08      AMUSEMENT
PLACES</a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.08.010      Definitions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.08.020      License required &#8209; fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.08.021      License investigation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.08.022      Standards for denial of
license.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.08.030      Due date for license fees.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.08.042      License applications – public
amusement/entertainment license.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.08.043      License display.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.08.070      Business hours.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.08.080      Outdoor sports exempt from
code.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.08.090      Race tracks and dragstrips.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.08.100      Standards for public
amusement/entertainment license suspension or revocation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.08.120      Penalty for violation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.08.130      Civil penalty.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.08.140      Additional enforcement.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.08.150      Limitation of liability.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.08.010  Definitions.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
For the purpose of this chapter, &quot;public place of amusement,&quot;
&quot;public amusement/entertainment,&quot; and &quot;public
entertainment&quot; mean an amusement, diversion, entertainment, show,
performance, exhibition, display or like activities, for the use or benefit of
a member or members of the public, or advertised for the use or benefit of a
member of the public, held, conducted, operated or maintained for a profit,
direct or indirect, but not including adult entertainment businesses.  (Ord.
13548 § 29, 1999:  Ord. 9915 § 9, 1991:  Ord. 7216 § 2, 1985:  Ord. 5410 § 1,
1981:  Ord. 5304 § 1, 1981:  Ord. 4206 § 3, 1979).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.08.020  License
required &#8209; fee.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> A public place of amusement shall not be operated or
maintained in King County, outside the limits of incorporated cities and towns,
unless the owner or lessee thereof has obtained a license from the director, as
follows:</span></p>

<table class=MsoNormalTable border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0
 style='margin-left:23.4pt;border-collapse:collapse;border:none'>
 <tr>
  <td width=288 colspan=2 valign=top style='width:3.0in;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;
  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Type of Entertainment</span></b></p>
  </td>
  <td width=24 colspan=2 valign=top style='width:.25in;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;
  border-left:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=276 valign=top style='width:207.0pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;
  border-left:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
  font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Fee</span></b></p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td width=288 colspan=2 valign=top style='width:3.0in;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;
  border-top:none;padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
  letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Miscellaneous (Includes, but is not limited to):</span></p>
  <p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
  letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Live Entertainment; music (other than mechanical);
  boxing or wrestling exhibition skating; video arcades; pool halls; bowling
  alleys; public more of miscellaneous race tracks, dragstrips, automobile or
  otherwise.</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=24 colspan=2 valign=top style='width:.25in;border-top:none;
  border-left:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;
  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
  letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>
  </td>
  <td width=276 valign=top style='width:207.0pt;border-top:none;border-left:
  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;
  padding:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt'>
  <p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
  letter-spacing:-.1pt'>$200.00 per year, 100.00 per 6 mos. or 50.00 per one
  night (covers one or skating rinks; shooting galleries; entertainment).</span></p>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
  <td width=288 colspan=2 valign=top style='width:3.0in;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;
