letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.040      Interpretation of franchise
terms.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:112.5pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-112.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.050      Applications for franchise,
renewal, modification or transfer.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:112.5pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-112.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.060      Franchise renewal.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:112.5pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-112.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.070      Notices.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:112.5pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-112.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.080      Insurance requirements.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:112.5pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-112.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.090      Liability and indemnification.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:112.5pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-112.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.100      Security fund or letter of
credit.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:112.5pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-112.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.110      Liquidated damages.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:1.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-112.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              6.27A.120      Nondiscrimination. </span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:112.5pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-112.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.130      Privacy.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:112.5pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-112.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.140      Rates.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:112.5pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-112.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.150      Customer service standards.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:112.5pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-112.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.160      Technical standards.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:112.5pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-112.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.170      Minimum facilities and
services.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:112.5pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-112.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.180      Local origination.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:112.5pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-112.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.190      Reports and records.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:112.5pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-112.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.200      Performance evaluation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:112.5pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-112.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.210      Revocation, expiration or
abandonment.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:112.5pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-112.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.220      Continuity of service
mandatory.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:112.5pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-112.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.230      Enforcement remedies.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:112.5pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-112.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.240      Notice and order procedure.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:112.5pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-112.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.250      Municipal cable system
ownership authorized.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:112.5pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-112.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.260      Administration.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:112.5pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-112.5pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.270      Applicability to current
franchise agreements.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>CROSS REFERENCE:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Public, educational and
government access (CTV) television channels:  K.C.C. chapter 2.59.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.010  Definitions.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
For the purpose of this chapter, the following terms, phrases, words and their
derivations shall have the meanings given herein.  When not inconsistent with
the context, words used in the present tense include the future, words in the
plural number include the singular number, and words in the singular number
include the plural number.  The words &quot;shall&quot; and &quot;will&quot;
are mandatory, and &quot;may&quot; is permissive.  Words not defined herein
shall be given the meaning set forth in the Cable Act.  Words not defined in
this chapter or the Cable Act shall be given their common and ordinary meaning.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  &quot;Abandonment&quot;
means failure by the franchisee to operate the entire cable system for ten
consecutive days without just cause.  Just cause shall include circumstances
beyond the franchisee's control, such as natural disasters and material
breakdown of the system that is not the result of the franchisee's fault or
negligence.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  &quot;Access
channel&quot; means any channel or bandwidth on a cable system set aside for
public, educational and/or governmental use.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  &quot;Basic
cable service&quot; means any service tiers which include the retransmission of
local television broadcast signals.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  &quot;Bulk
rate&quot; means a rate charged to an owner of a structure or parcel of land
containing multiple dwelling units in return for the provision of cable service
to those units.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  &quot;Cable
Act&quot; means the Cable Communications Policy Act of 1984, codified at 47
U.S.C. Secs. 521 et seq., and as hereafter may be amended.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F.  &quot;Cable
manager&quot; means the director of the department of information technology or
the director's designee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            G.  &quot;Cable
office&quot; means the cable section of the department of information
technology.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            H.  &quot;Cable
rules&quot; means rules promulgated by the director of the department of
information technology or the director's designee for the purpose of
administering the terms and requirements of this chapter.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            I.  &quot;Cable
service&quot; means the transmission of video or other service over a cable
system to subscribers together with any subscriber interaction provided in
connection with such service.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            J.  &quot;Cable
system&quot; means a facility, consisting of a set of closed transmission paths
and associated signal generation, reception and control equipment that is
designed to provide cable service that includes video programming and that is
provided to subscribers within King County.  A cable system does not include:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  a
facility that serves only to retransmit the television signals of one or more
television broadcast stations;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  a
facility that serves only subscribers in one or more multiple unit dwellings
under common ownership, control, or management, unless such facility uses any
public right-of-way;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  a
facility of a common carrier that is subject, in whole or in part, to the
provisions of Title II of the Communications Act of 1934, codified at 47 U.S.C.
Sec 201 et seq., except that such facility will be considered a cable system to
the extent it is used in the transmission of video programming directly to
subscribers; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  any
facilities of any electric utility used solely for operating its electric
utility systems.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            K.  &quot;Channel&quot;
means a portion of the electromagnetic frequency spectrum which is used in a
cable system and which is capable of delivering a television channel, as
television channel is defined by the FCC by regulation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            L.  &quot;Commercial
rate&quot; means a rate charged to a business in return for the provision of
cable service to that business.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            M.  &quot;Disabled
subscriber&quot; means a subscriber with a physical or mental impairment that
substantially limits one or more of the major life activities of such
individual.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            N.  &quot;Equitable
price&quot; means the price that a willing buyer would pay to a willing seller
for a going concern, less any value attributed to the franchise itself, less
the amount of harm to the community, and less any expenses incurred by the
county as result of the actions giving rise to the revocation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            O.  &quot;Fair
market price&quot; means the price that a willing buyer would pay to a willing
seller for a going concern, less any value attributed to the franchise itself.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            P.  &quot;FCC&quot;
means the Federal Communications Commission and any legally appointed,
designated or elected agent or successor.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Q.  &quot;Franchise&quot;
means the right granted by the county to a franchisee to construct,
reconstruct, repair, maintain and operate a cable system over, on, along, or
under any public rights-of-way within all or specified areas within
unincorporated areas of the county.  The term does not include any license or
permit required by other laws, ordinances or rules of the county for the
privilege of transacting and carrying on a business within the county, or for
construction, reconstruction, repair or maintenance on, over or under or use of
any public rights-of-way.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            R.  &quot;Franchise
agreement&quot; means a document entered into between the county and a
franchisee that sets forth the terms and conditions under which the franchise
will be exercised.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            S.  &quot;Franchisee&quot;
means any person granted a franchise pursuant to this chapter who has entered
into a franchise agreement with King County.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            T.  &quot;Gross
revenues&quot; means the annual gross revenue of the franchisee from all
sources in the operation of the cable communications system, excluding any bad
debt, sales tax, excise tax, or other taxes collected for direct pass-through
to local, state or federal government.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            U.  &quot;Installation&quot;
means the connection and/or activation of the system from feeder cable to
subscriber terminals.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            V.  &quot;Institutional
network&quot; means a voice, data and/or video communications system, whether
physically integrated with a cable system or not, that is constructed, operated
or maintained by a franchisee, whose transmissions are principally available to
persons other than cable television subscribers.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            W.  &quot;Interconnect
means&quot; the sharing of video, audio and/or data transmissions between two
or more cable systems, institutional networks and/or users.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            X.  &quot;Minority
persons&quot; means African-Americans, Hispanics, Mexican-Americans,
Asian-Americans, Pacific Islanders, American Indians and Alaska Natives.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Y.  &quot;Person&quot;
means any individual, corporation, partnership, limited partnership,
association, joint venture, organization, or any other legal entity of any
kind, and any lawful trustee, successor, assignee, transferee or personal
representative thereof.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Z.  &quot;Public
rights-of-way&quot; means the surface of and the space along, above and below
any street, road, highway, freeway, lane, sidewalk, alley, court, boulevard,
parkway, drive, utility easement and road right-of-way now or hereafter held or
administered by the county.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            AA.  &quot;Senior
citizen subscriber&quot; means a subscriber sixty-five years of age or over.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            BB.  &quot;Subscriber&quot;
means any person who legally receives cable service delivered over the cable
system.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            CC.  &quot;Transfer&quot;
means any transaction in which:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  an
ownership or other interest in a franchisee is transferred from one person to
another person so that control of the franchisee is transferred, or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  the
rights held by the franchisee under a franchise agreement are transferred or
assigned, in whole or in part, to another person.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Provided, the
transfer of ownership or other interest in a franchisee between members of the
same immediate family shall not be a transfer for the purpose of this chapter
so long as the county is notified of the fact of the transfer of ownership or
other interest no later than fourteen (14) days prior to the transfer of
ownership or other interest, except where the transfer of ownership or other
interest occurs due to death or disability, in which case the county shall be
notified within fourteen (14) days after the transfer of ownership or other
interest.  The franchisee shall insure that its insurance coverage and all
other commitments continue in force without interruption and provide evidence
of the same to the county.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            For the
purposes of this provision, a transfer shall be deemed to be between members of
the same family if the transferee is the spouse, parent, sibling, adopted or
natural child or other lineal descendant of the transferor, or if the
transferee is a trust established for the benefit of such a person or for the
benefit of the transferor.  If the ownership or other interest in the
franchisee is held by the trustee of a trust, then a transfer shall be deemed
to be between members of the same family if the transferee is the spouse,
parent, sibling, adopted or natural child or other lineal descendant of any
other beneficiary of the trust, or any trust created for the benefit of such a
person.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Provided
further that, the transfer of ownership or other interest in a franchisee in
connection with an internal reorganization or internal merger to a direct or
indirect parent, subsidiary or affiliated entity under common control with the
franchisee shall not be a transfer for the purpose of this chapter so long as:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  the
county is notified of the proposed transfer no later than thirty (30) days
prior to the transfer of ownership or other interest;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  the
transferee shall insure that insurance coverage and all other commitments under
the franchise agreement continue in force and without interruption and provide
evidence to the same of the county no later than thirty (30) days prior to the
proposed transfer; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  there is
no increased risk of liability to the county or nonperformance of the terms of
the franchise agreement.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            DD.  &quot;Two-way
capability&quot; means the capacity for two-way transmission, over the cable
system.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            EE.  &quot;Video
programming vendor&quot; means a person engaged in the production, creation, or
wholesale distribution of video programming for sale.  (Ord. 17142 § 18, 2011: 
Ord. 14199 § 117, 2001:  Ord. 10731 § 1, 1993:  Ord. 10159 § 3, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.020  Grant
of authority.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Franchise and permits required.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  A
franchise authorizes the use of the county's public rights-of-way and
compatible utility easements, as defined in the Cable Act, to construct,
reconstruct, repair and maintain a cable system and/or institutional network.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  No person
shall construct or operate a cable system in the county without a franchise
granted by the county and a franchise agreement executed with the county.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  A
franchisee must obtain any permits and pay any permit fees required by the
county for use of the public rights-of-way.  Such permits shall be obtained by
and issued to a franchisee prior to any construction, reconstruction, repair or
maintenance activity on any public rights-of-way.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  A
franchisee, in consideration of its use of the public rights-of-way, must pay
to the county quarterly a franchise fee equal to five percent of the
franchisee's gross revenues.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  A
franchisee is at all times subject to and must comply with all generally
applicable federal, state and local laws, ordinances, codes, rules, regulations
and orders.  A franchisee shall at all times be subject to the exercise of the
police power of the county.  (10159 § 4, 1991)</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.030  Franchises
and franchise agreements.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The county
may grant one or more franchises to serve all or a specified portion of
unincorporated areas of the county.  Any new franchise, renewal, transfer or
modification shall be granted by ordinance and shall be for a term not to
exceed fifteen years from the date the franchise is fully executed.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  Any
franchise granted shall be nonexclusive, and does not expressly or implicitly
preclude the issuance of other franchises, or affect the county's right to use
or authorize the use of its public rights-of-way to other persons as it
determines appropriate.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  In
evaluating an application for a new franchise or a transfer of a franchise, the
county may consider, among other things, the following factors:  the
applicant's technical, financial, and legal qualifications to construct and
operate the proposed system; the nature of the proposed facilities, equipment,
and services; the applicant's record and experience in constructing and
operating cable systems and providing cable service in other communities, if
any; the capability of the county's public rights-of-way to accommodate the
proposed system; the potential disruption to existing users of the county's
public rights-of-way and the resulting inconvenience to the public caused by
the construction or operation of the proposed system; and whether the proposal
will meet reasonably anticipated community cable-related needs and interests
and serve the public interest.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  The terms,
conditions and provisions of a fully executed franchise agreement, together
with all applicable laws, ordinances, codes, rules, regulations and orders,
enacted now or in the future, shall define the rights and obligations of the
franchisee and the county relating to the franchise.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  The county
may modify franchises consistent with its police powers as follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  at the
time of renewal, transfer, or other disposition;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  when the
franchisee's service area is altered, provided the franchisee is given thirty
(30) days written notice of the proposed modification and is provided an
opportunity to present arguments against the modification, or alternatives in
lieu of if;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  upon
giving thirty days written notice to the franchisee of the proposed
modification, provided the franchisee is given an opportunity to present
arguments against the modification or alternative in lieu of it;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  upon
request of the franchisee under the circumstances provided in the Cable Act; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              5.  when the
franchise and/or franchise agreement is inconsistent with governing laws or
statutes.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F.  Except as
expressly provided to the contrary, all costs incurred by an applicant or
franchisee in complying with this chapter, the cable rules, a franchise,
applicable law, or any action thereunder shall be the sole responsibility of
the applicant or franchisee and shall not be charged to the county.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            G.  The notice
requirements contained in RCW 36.55.040 shall apply to this section.  (Ord.
10159 § 5, 1991)</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.035  Specific
acts prohibited.  </span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>No cable operator or holder of a franchise to provide
cable services or other multichannel video programming distributor providing or
intending to provide services in King County shall:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Engage in
unfair methods of competition or unfair or deceptive acts or practices.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  Monopolize
or attempt to monopolize or combine or conspire with any other person or
persons to monopolize any part of the production, control or sale of cable
services, video programming or equipment.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  Lease or
make a sale or contract for the sale of goods or services used in the provision
of multichannel video programming in King County when the purpose or effect of
such lease, sale, or contract may be to:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  substantially
lessen competition, or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  tend to
create a monopoly; or </span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  hinder
significantly or prevent any multichannel video programming distributor from
providing video programming to subscribers or consumers when the purpose or
effect is to substantially lessen competition or to tend to create a monopoly.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  Require a
financial interest in a program service as a condition of carriage on one or
more of its systems when the purpose or effect is to substantially lessen
competition or to tend to create a monopoly.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E. Coerce a
video programming vendor to provide, or retaliate against such a vendor for
failing to provide, exclusive rights against other multichannel video
programming distributors as a condition of carriage on a system when the
purpose or effect is to substantially lessen competition or to tend to create a
monopoly.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F.  Engage in
conduct the effect of which is to unreasonably restrain the ability of a video
programming vendor to compete fairly by discriminating in video programming
distribution on the basis of affiliation or nonaffiliation of vendors in the
selection, terms, or conditions for carriage of video programming provided by
such vendors when the purpose or effect is to substantially lessen competition
or to tend to create a monopoly.  (Ord. 10731 § 2, 1993).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.040  Interpretation
of franchise terms.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  All franchise agreements shall include the following
provision:  The provisions of the cable ordinance and the cable rules shall
apply to the franchise agreement as if fully set forth in the franchise
agreement, and the express terms of this chapter and the cable rules will
prevail over conflicting or inconsistent provisions in the franchise agreement
unless the franchise agreement expresses an explicit intent to waive a
requirement of this chapter and/or the cable rules.  (Ord. 10159 § 6, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.050  Applications
for franchise, renewal, modification or transfer.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  All
applications for the following must be filed in writing with the clerk of the
county council:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  grant of
a new franchise;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  renewal
of a franchise under the franchise renewal procedures set forth in the Cable
Act and this chapter;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  modification
of a franchise agreement; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  transfer
of a franchise.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  An
applicant shall demonstrate in its application compliance with all requirements
of this chapter, the cable rules, and applicable federal, state and local law.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  An
application for a new franchise or renewal of an existing franchise must
contain, at a minimum, the following:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  information
regarding the characteristics and location of the proposed system;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  the
applicant's technical and financial ability to construct and operate the
proposed system;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  a
proposal for the provision of public, educational and/or governmental
(&quot;PEG&quot;) access channels, and equipment and facilities relating to
such channels sufficient to meet community needs and interest; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  a
proposal to meet future cable-related community needs and interests.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  If the
county issues a request for franchising proposals or a request for
refranchising proposals, an application must comply with the requirements of
such request.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  An
application for approval of a transfer of a franchise must contain, at minimum,
information regarding the applicant's technical and financial ability to
construct and operate the system and a statement that the proposed transferee
will comply with the transferor's franchise agreement, this chapter, the cable
rules and applicable law.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F.  An
application for a new franchise must be accompanied by a $5,000 deposit to
cover the costs incurred by the county to review and process the application. 
This deposit shall be made payable to the county and delivered to the clerk of
the council.  (Ord. 10159 § 7, 1991)</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.060  Franchise
renewal.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Franchises
may be renewed using either the formal process specified in the Cable Act and
in subsection B. of this section or the informal process specified in
subsection C. of this section.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The
following procedure shall be used for all formal renewals effected under the
Cable Act:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  During
the six-month period that begins with the thirty-sixth month before the
expiration of a franchise, the county may on its own initiative, and shall at
the request of the franchisee, commence proceedings that afford the public in
the franchise area appropriate notice and participation to identify the future
cable-related community needs and interests and to review the franchisee's performance
under the franchise;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Upon
completion of the proceeding, the franchisee may, on its own initiative or at
the request of the county, submit a proposal for renewal.  All such proposals
must meet the requirements of this chapter.  If the county requests a renewal
proposal, it shall establish a date when the renewal proposal shall be due,
which shall not be less than thirty days after the request is made;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  Upon
submittal of a completed proposal for renewal by the due date, the county shall
notify the public of the proposal and, during the four-month period, which
begins on the date of submission of the cable operator's proposal under
subsection B.2. [of this section], the county shall issue a preliminary
assessment that the franchise should not be renewed or the county shall grant
the renewal.  The county's failure to make a preliminary assessment or to grant
the renewal within the four-month period shall be deemed to be a preliminary
assessment that the franchise should not be renewed and shall entitle the
franchisee to the procedure in subsection B.4. of this section;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.a.  Whenever
a preliminary assessment is made that a franchise should not be renewed, the
county may on its own, and shall at the request of the franchisee, commence an
administrative proceeding by the hearing examiner under K.C.C. 20.22.040, after
providing notice to the public and the franchisee, to consider whether:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                  (1)  the
franchisee has substantially complied with the material terms of the existing
franchise and with applicable law;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                  (2)  the
quality of the franchisee's service, including signal quality, response to
consumer complaints and billing practices, but without regard to the mix,
quality or level of cable services or other services provided over the system,
has been reasonable in light of community needs;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                  (3)  the
franchisee has the financial, legal and technical ability to provide the
services, facilities and equipment as set forth in the franchisee's proposal;
and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                  (4)  the
franchisee's proposal is reasonable to meet the future cable-related community
needs and interests, taking into account the cost of meeting those needs and
interests.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                b.  The
franchisee and the cable office shall be afforded fair opportunity for full
participation in the proceeding.  At the completion of the proceeding, the hearing
examiner shall issue a written final decision granting or denying the renewal
based upon the record of the proceeding, and transmit a copy to the franchisee;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              5.  Any
denial of a renewal shall be based on one or more adverse findings made with
respect to the factors described in subsection B.4.a(1) through (4) of this
section, under the record of proceeding under subsection B.4.a.(1) through (4)
of this section.  The county may not base a denial of renewal on conditions
listed in subsection B.4.a.(1) or (2) of this section unless the county has
provided the franchisee with notice and the opportunity to cure, or in any case
that the county has waived its right to object or has effectively acquiesced;
and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              6.  Any
franchisee whose renewal proposal has been denied by a final decision of the
county made in accordance with this subsection B. or has been adversely
affected by a failure of the county to act in accordance with procedural
requirements of this subsection B. may appeal such final decision or failure in
accordance with the Cable Act.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  Notwithstanding
subsection B. of this section, a franchisee may submit an informal renewal
application in accordance with this subsection at any time.  The following
procedure shall be used for all informal renewal applications:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  A
franchisee may submit a renewal application meeting the requirements of this
chapter.  Submission of a renewal application in accordance with this
subsection shall not invoke the formal application process contained in
subsection B. of this section;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Upon
submittal of a completed application, the county shall notify the public of the
application and solicit public comments;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  After
receiving the public comments and completing any other review, the county shall
either deny or grant the renewal.  In determining whether to grant or deny the
renewal, the county may consider whether:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                a.  the
franchisee has the technical, legal and financial ability to provide the
services, facilities and equipment as set forth in the franchisee's proposal;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                b.  the
franchisee has substantially complied with the material terms of the existing
franchise and with applicable law;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                c.  the
quality of the franchisee's service, including signal quality, response to
consumer complaints, billing practices, service mix or service level, has been
reasonable in light of community needs;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                d.  the
franchisee's proposal is reasonable to meet the future cable-related community
needs and interests, taking into account the cost of meeting those needs and
interests; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                e.  such
other factors consistent with the intent of this chapter and the Cable Act; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  The
denial of a renewal under this subsection shall not affect action on a renewal
application that is submitted in accordance with subsection B. of this section
(<span style='color:black'>Ord. 18230 § 83, 2016:  </span>Ord. 11075 § 1,
1993:  10159 § 8, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.070  Notices.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
All notices from a franchisee to the county pursuant to this chapter and the
cable rules shall be filed with the cable office.  A franchisee shall maintain
with the cable office, throughout the term of the franchise, an address for
service of notices by mail.  (Ord. 10159 § 9, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.080  Insurance
requirements.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  For any
franchise agreement entered into after December 2, 1991, a franchisee must
carry commercial general liability, automobile liability and stop gap or
employers liability coverage, each in minimum limits of not less than one
million dollars ($1,000,000.00), in an amount approved by the King County
office of risk management.  All policies must name King County as an additional
named insured.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  All
policies shall be placed with insurers having a Bests' rating of no less than
A:VIII or, if not rated by Bests, with surpluses equivalent to or greater than
Bests' A:VIII rating.  A franchisee shall send copies of certificates,
endorsements or other adequate evidence of compliance with this section to the
cable office prior to the county's execution of the franchise agreement.  (Ord.
10159 § 10, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.090  Liability
and indemnification.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  All
franchise agreements shall contain the following provision:  a franchisee shall
have no recourse whatsoever against the county or its officials, boards,
commissions, agents, or employees for any loss, costs, expenses, or damages
arising out of any provision or requirement of the franchise, franchise
agreement, or this chapter because of the enforcement of the franchise,
franchise agreement, or this chapter except if such loss, costs, expenses or
damages are the result of the sole negligence or misconduct on the part of the
county or its agents.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  All
franchise agreements shall contain the following provision:  to the extent
permitted by law, a franchisee shall, at its sole cost and expense, indemnify,
hold harmless, and defend the county and its officers, boards, commissions,
agents and employees, against any and all claims, including but not limited to
third-party claims, suits, causes of action, proceedings and judgments for
damages or equitable relief arising out of the construction, repair,
maintenance or operation of its cable system, or in any way arising out of the
franchisee's enjoyment or exercise of a franchise granted pursuant, or
otherwise subject, to this chapter, regardless of whether the act or omission
complained of is authorized, allowed or prohibited by this chapter, the cable
rules, or a franchise agreement.  This provision includes, but is not limited
to, expenses for reasonable legal fees and for disbursements and liabilities
assumed by the county as follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  To
persons or property, in any way arising out of or through the acts or omissions
of the franchisee, its officers, employees, or agents or to which the
franchisee's negligence shall in any way contribute;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Arising
out of any claim for invasion of the right of privacy, for defamation of any
person, firm or corporation; or the violation or infringement of any copyright,
trademark, trade name, service mark or patent; or a failure by the franchisee
to secure consents from the owners, or authorized distributors of programs to
be delivered by the cable system; or of any other right of any person,
excluding claims arising out of or relating to programming provided by the
county;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  Arising
out of a franchisee's failure to comply with the provisions of any federal,
state or local statute, ordinance, rule, or regulation applicable to the
franchisee with respect to any aspect of its cable television business to which
this chapter, the cable rules, and/or franchise agreement apply.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  The county
shall give the franchisee timely written notice of the making of any claim or
the commencement of any action, suit or other proceeding covered by this
chapter.  In the event any such claim arises, the county or any other
indemnified party shall tender the defense thereof to the franchisee and the
franchisee shall have the right to defend, settle, or compromise any claims
arising hereunder and the county shall cooperate fully therein.  (Ord. 10159 §
11, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.100  Security
fund or letter of credit.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  An applicant for a grant of a
franchise or franchise renewal or transfer must provide the cable office, for
deposit with the King County office of financial management, in an amount
determined by the cable office, but not less than twenty-five thousand dollars
($25,000) either a cash security deposit or an irrevocable letter of credit
from a financial institution in a form satisfactory to the manager and the King
County office of financial management prior to the county's execution of the
franchise agreement.  The amount of the deposit shall be based on the scope of
the applicant's existing and proposed cable operations in the county, the
applicant's technical and financial qualifications, and the applicant's history
of compliance with its franchise agreements in the county and elsewhere.  A
security deposit or letter of credit may also be required or the amount of the
security deposit or letter of credit may be raised as a condition of a
modification.  The security deposit or letter of credit shall be used to ensure
the faithful performance of the franchise agreement; compliance with this
chapter, the cable rules, applicable federal, state, and local law, all orders
and permits; and the payment of any claims, liens, fees, or taxes due the
county that arise by reason of the construction, operation, repair or
maintenance of the cable system.  The county may withdraw funds from the
security deposit or make demand for payment upon the letter of credit for the
monetary amount of any remedy imposed pursuant to this chapter.  (Ord. 10159 §
12, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.110  Liquidated
damages.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  All franchise agreements entered into after December 2,
1991, may provide for liquidated damages to compensate the county for harm
caused by violation of this chapter, the cable rules, a franchise agreement, or
any applicable law in an amount which is a reasonable forecast of just
compensation for the harm caused by the violation.  (Ord. 10159 § 13, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.120  Nondiscrimination.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  A
franchisee or applicant for a franchise shall not deny cable service, or
otherwise discriminate against any subscriber, access programmer or resident on
the basis of one or more of the protected classes as defined in K.C.C. chapter
3.12D, political affiliation, or income of the residents of the area in which
the person resides.  The franchisee shall comply at all times with all other
applicable federal, state, and local laws, rules and regulations relating to nondiscrimination.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  A
franchisee shall not refuse to employ, nor discharge from employment, nor
discriminate against any person in compensation or in terms, conditions or
privileges of employment because of one or more of the protected classes as
defined in K.C.C. chapter 3.12D, political affiliation, or income.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  A
franchisee shall comply with all applicable federal, state and local equal
employment opportunity requirements.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  The
franchisee shall establish, maintain and execute an equal employment
opportunity plan and a minority/women's business procurement program, which
shall be consistent with the intent of the county's affirmative action and
minority/women's business procurement policies.  Upon request, the franchisee
shall file with the cable office a copy of their equal employment opportunity
report submitted annually to the FCC and shall file with the executive's office
an annual compliance report detailing its progress with its minority/women's
business procurement program during the previous year.  The franchisee must
also provide the cable office, upon request, copies of all other reports and
information filed with federal, state, or local agencies concerning equal
employment opportunity or employment discrimination laws.  This subsection
shall apply only to franchise agreements entered into after December 2, 1991.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  Despite
the other provisions of this section, no provision of this section shall
invalidate any other section of this chapter.  (Ord. 20082 § 44, 2026:  Ord.
19977 § 9, 2025:  Ord. 19541 § 5, 2022:  Ord. 19047 § 17, 2019 [did not take
effect]:  Ord. 19026 § 3, 2019:  Ord. 10159 § 14, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.130  Privacy.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
A franchisee must protect the privacy of all subscribers pursuant to the Cable
Act.  A franchisee may not condition subscriber service on the subscriber's
grant of permission to disclose information which, pursuant to federal law,
cannot be disclosed.  (Ord. 10159 § 15, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.140  Rates.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.1.  A
franchisee must charge uniform prices throughout the geographic area in which
cable service is provided over its cable system, except that different rates
may be offered to commercial rate subscribers, and provided further that
reduced rates may be offered to:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                a.  new
subscribers,</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                b.  subscribers
adding a service that they have not previously received, or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                c.  disabled,
senior citizen, low income or bulk rate subscribers.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  To the
extent provided by federal law, a franchisee may change its rates and charges
only if it has given a minimum of thirty calendar days prior written notice to
subscribers and the cable office.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The county
may regulate rates except to the extent it is prohibited from doing so by state
or federal law.  Any regulated rate shall be adopted by ordinance and shall be
processed in accordance with the provisions of K.C.C. 20.22.060.  The cable
office shall promptly notify the hearing examiner of any proposed rate
changes.  The director of the department of information technology is
authorized to issue an order to toll the effective date of proposed rates in
accordance with the provisions of the FCC rules and to take any other action
necessary to implement rate regulation.  The director of the department of information
technology shall adopt rules governing the regulation of rates that:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  Are
consistent with the FCC's regulations;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Provide
a reasonable opportunity for consideration of the views of interested parties; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  Establish
procedures analogous to those set forth by the FCC governing requests that
proprietary information produced in the course of a rate proceeding be treated
as confidential, to the extent permitted by law.  (<span style='color:black'>Ord.
18230 § 84, 2016:  </span>Ord. 17142 § 19, 2011:  Ord. 14199 § 118, 2001:  Ord.
11075 § 2, 1993:  Ord. 10159 § 16, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.150  Customer
service standards.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Under
normal operating conditions a franchisee shall comply with the customer service
standards established under this chapter, the cable rules and its franchise. 
Such standards shall include, but need not be limited, to the following:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  The
franchisee shall have a local or toll-free telephone number.  The franchisee
shall have a location and procedure approved by the cable office to ensure that
subscribers can conveniently make payments, exchange or accept equipment,
receive responses to inquiries and schedule appointments during normal business
and evening hours and at least one-half a business day during the weekend.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Under
normal operating conditions, telephone answer time by the franchisee shall not
exceed thirty (30) seconds, average speed of answer, and busy signals shall not
occur more than three percent of the time.  This requirement shall be met at
least ninety (90) percent of the time, measured over any consecutive ninety
(90) day period.  The franchisee shall use an answering service or be capable
of receiving service complaints and system malfunction reports when the
business office is closed.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  Installation
work shall be performed in a timely manner.  The franchisee shall offer a
choice of morning or afternoon appointments within a four (4) hour time period
and may offer all day appointments for service, installation, or disconnection
if it is necessary to enter the subscriber's residence.  If the franchisee
fails to keep two (2) or more consecutive scheduled appointments with a
subscriber, and fails to give notice to the subscriber at least two (2) hours
prior to the scheduled appointment time, the franchisee shall give a service
credit to that subscriber.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  A
franchisee must have available twenty-four (24) hours a day, seven (7) days a
week, personnel and equipment capable of locating and correcting major cable
system outages.  A major cable system outage is an outage which results in the
loss of cable service to ten (10) or more subscribers on fifty (50) percent or
more of the subscribers' channels or picture impairment visible to ten (10) or
more subscribers on fifty (50) percent or more of the subscribers' channels. 
Major cable system outages must be corrected without delay.  Corrective action
for other cable system outages must be initiated by the franchisee not later
than one (1) business day after the customer service call is received and must
be completed as promptly as possible.  Corrective action for all other service
problems must be initiated by the franchisee not later than two (2) business
days after the customer service call is received and must be completed as
promptly as possible.  A franchisee may intentionally interrupt service on the
cable system only for good cause and for the shortest time possible.  Upon
request of a subscriber, the franchisee shall provide a rebate to subscribers,
pro-rated, for any service problem cause by the franchisee that exceeds
twenty-four (24) hours. </span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              5.  A
franchisee shall provide each subscriber at the time cable service is
installed, and upon request, with written subscriber information, which
includes procedures for handling complaints and a schedule of service rates and
charges as well as credits required by law.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              6.  All
subscriber bills must clearly indicate charges, broken down to indicate the
charge for each service, or group of services charged as a unit, equipment, and
any other fees included on the bill.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              7.  A
franchisee is prohibited from offering any service by a negative option.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              8.  A
subscriber may voluntarily disconnect service at any time; however, voluntary
disconnection does not excuse a subscriber from fulfilling its contract
obligations.  A franchisee may disconnect service to a subscriber for cause or
if at least thirty (30) days have elapsed after the due date for payment of a
bill and the franchisee has provided written notice that service will be
disconnected if the bill is not paid in full by a specific date.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              9.  A
franchisee may not refer, or cause to be entered, a negative report to any
consumer credit reporting agency, association or business unless thirty (30)
days have elapsed after sending notice to the customer at the last service
address or billing address of record after disconnection has occurred.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The
transmission of obscene programming is prohibited.  The county expressly
reserves the right to restrict or condition the provision of cable services
that are otherwise constitutionally unprotected.  (Ord. 10159 § 17, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.160  Technical
standards.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  A franchisee shall comply with all applicable technical
standards including, but not limited to, the National Electrical Safety Code,
the National Electric Code, and standards established by the FCC, the National
Television Systems Committee and the county.  (Ord. 10159 § 18, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.170  Minimum
facilities and services.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Consistent
with the Cable Act every cable system constructed, reconstructed or upgraded
after December 2, 1991:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  shall
have a two-way capability;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  shall
provide PEG access facilities, equipment, and/or channels; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  may be
required to provide an institutional network.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The county
may require, in the franchise agreement, a franchisee to interconnect its
system with any or all of the other cable systems in areas of King County so as
to enable each such system to carry and cablecast the public, educational and
government access programming carried on each system and on institutional
networks with channel capacity designated for educational and governmental
use.  Interconnection may be done by direct cable connection, microwave link,
satellite or other appropriate method.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  A
franchisee must make cable service available for the standard installation
charge to all persons within its franchise area who request cable service and
agree to subscribe for a minimum period of one year if, using the most direct
route, the distance the distribution line would be extended to provide service
divided by the number of people requesting service is not more than three
hundred (300) feet from the cable system, and the drop distance is not more
than one hundred fifty (150) feet from the cable system.  Cable service shall
be provided to all persons who are not within these distances if the person
agrees to pay the full cost to provide cable service beyond these distances.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  The
franchisee shall provide, at a minimum, the mix quality and level of services
listed in the franchise agreement.  Those services within the franchisee's
control shall not be changed without thirty (30) days prior written notice to
subscribers and the cable office in a manner approved by the cable office,
which provides full and clear disclosure of the following:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  the
franchisee's proposed change;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  the
franchise agreement requires certain services; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  comments
made by subscribers to King County will be considered in evaluating any
proposed changes that requires county approval.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  All
franchisees shall provide for immediate access by King County in emergency
situations and must have the ability to override programming with emergency
programming provided by King County during these emergency situations.  (Ord.
10159 § 19, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.180  Local
origination.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  A franchisee may be required in the franchise agreement
to produce up to two hours of local origination programming per day, seven days
per week, for viewing between 4:00 p.m. and 10:00 p.m.  It is the policy of the
county to encourage local origination programming, including programming of
interest and applicability to children, senior citizen, minority and disabled
residents.  This section shall not apply to franchises granted prior to December
2, 1991.  (10159 § 20, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.190  Reports
and records.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The county
and its representatives shall have the authority, upon reasonable notice, to
inspect a franchisee's books, records, facilities, and any other items and to
require a franchisee to keep, develop and produce books, records, reports,
summaries, tests, lists and other items regarding the franchisee's operations
in unincorporated King County that the county deems necessary to monitor a
franchisee's compliance, its franchise, this chapter, the cable rules, or
applicable law.  Such authority shall include, but not be limited to, the right
to audit a franchisee's books and records and to inspect and test a
franchisee's technical facilities.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  A
franchisee shall pay all of the county's costs associated with an audit,
reaudit, inspection, reinspection, test or retest if it is determined that the
franchisee has not materially complied with its franchise, this chapter, the
cable rules, or applicable law.  If the audit determines that the franchisee's
franchise fee payment was less than the amount owed to the county, the
franchisee shall pay to the county any deficiency plus interest on the
deficiency equal to twelve percent per annum interest compounded daily from the
date the franchise fee payment was due.  (Ord. 10159 § 21, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.200  Performance
evaluation.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The cable office may conduct such periodic performance
evaluations of a franchisee to ensure compliance with the franchise agreement
and all applicable laws and may conduct community needs assessments.  A
franchisee shall cooperate fully with these evaluations and assessments.  If
the cable office implements a survey of cable subscribers in connection with a
performance evaluation, the franchisee may be required to distribute the cable
office's survey to its subscribers at the county's expense.  (Ord. 10159 § 22,
1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.210  Revocation,
expiration or abandonment.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The county
executive may revoke the franchise and franchise agreement pursuant to the
notice and order procedure contained in this chapter if:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  a
franchisee has committed a material breach of the franchise agreement; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  there
has occurred an assignment for the benefit of creditors or the appointment of a
receiver or trustee to take over the business of the franchisee, whether in a
receivership, reorganization, bankruptcy assignment for the benefit of
creditors, or other action or proceeding, unless within that one hundred twenty
day period such assignment, receivership or trusteeship has been vacated; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  any part
of the franchise or cable system is foreclosed or sold at a judicial sale.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  Upon the
expiration or revocation of a franchise and franchise agreement or abandonment
of the cable system, the county may:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  require
the former franchisee to remove all portions of the cable system from all
streets and public property within the franchise area that are above ground or
are below ground and constitute a hazard to the health, welfare or safety of
county residents and restore county property to the county's reasonable
satisfaction.  If the former franchisee fails to comply within the time
specified, the county may remove any facilities and equipment, restore county
property to the county's satisfaction, and recover any costs incurred from the
franchisee or its assignees; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  require
transfer to an owner acceptable to King County or acquire ownership of the
cable system for an equitable price in the case of revocation, and at fair
market value in the case of any other franchise termination.  (Ord. 10159 § 23,
1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.220  Continuity
of service mandatory.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Subscriber
contracts shall give to subscribers the right to receive all available services
from the franchisee as long as their financial and other obligations to the
franchisee are satisfied.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The
franchisee must ensure that all subscribers receive continuous, uninterrupted
service.  In the event of a revocation of the franchise, expiration which
occurs without the franchisee having given notice pursuant to this section or
abandonment of the cable system, the franchisee shall continue to operate the
cable system for a period determined by the cable manager not to exceed
eighteen (18) months from the date of such revocation or expiration, in order
to provide for an orderly transition to another cable system operator without
interruption of service.  During such period the cable system must be operated
under the same terms and conditions as required by this chapter, the cable
rules, and the franchise agreement, except to the extent the county waives any
franchise condition.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  If the
franchisee elects not to renew a franchise, the franchisee shall notify the
county of its intent not less than twelve (12) months prior to the expiration
date of franchise.  Failure to provide this notification will subject the
franchisee to the continuity of service provision in this section of this
chapter.  (Ord. 10159 § 24, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.230  Enforcement
remedies.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The county
may seek legal and/or equitable relief from any court of competent jurisdiction
in the event a person violates this chapter, the cable rules, a franchise
agreement, or applicable federal, state or local law.  In addition, the county
has the right to impose any one or combination of the following remedies: 
collect liquidated damages as provided for in the franchise agreement, assess
civil penalties in an amount up to one hundred dollars per violation, require
corrective action to remedy the violation, and/or revoke the franchise and
franchise agreement.  Each day a violation continues may be considered an
additional violation.  Any remedy or remedies set forth in this section may be:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            1.  recovered
by legal action filed in King County superior court by the prosecuting attorney
on behalf of King County; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            2.  imposed by
an administrative notice and order issued pursuant to this chapter by the
director of the King County department of executive services, provided that
only the county executive shall have the authority to revoke a franchise and
franchise agreement.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  In
determining which remedy or remedies are appropriate, the county shall take
into consideration the nature of the violation and the harm caused by it, the
nature of the remedy required in order to remedy such harm and prevent further
violations, and such other matters as the cable office determines are
appropriate.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  Failure of
the county to enforce any requirements of this chapter, the cable rules, the
franchise agreement or applicable law shall not constitute a waiver of the
right to enforce that requirement, or subsequent violations of the requirement,
or to seek appropriate enforcement remedies, nor shall it relieve a franchisee
of the obligation to comply with any requirement.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  A person's
payment of liquidated damages or penalties or the county's imposition of any
remedy shall not relieve the person of the obligation to comply with the
requirements of this chapter, the cable rules, a franchise agreement, an order
of the county or applicable law.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  Any sum
recovered by the county from the required security fund or letter of credit
under the terms of this section shall not be a limitation upon the liability of
the franchise to the county and shall not constitute an election of remedies.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F.  In the
event of any dispute between the franchisee and the county arising out of this
chapter, the cable rules or the franchise agreement, the franchisee shall
pursue and exhaust all available administrative remedies pursuant to law prior
to pursuing any appropriate legal action.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            G.  The
revocation or forfeiture of any franchise shall not affect any of the county's
rights under the franchise or under any provision of law.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            H.  No
enforcement remedy shall be imposed except in accordance with due process of
law.  (Ord. 14199 § 119, 2001:  Ord. 10159 § 25, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.240  Notice
and order procedure.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Any remedy
imposed by administrative notice and order shall be imposed following the
procedure outlined in this section.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The notice
and order shall contain:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  A
statement that the county has found the person to be in violation of this
chapter, the cable rules, a franchise agreement or any applicable law, with a
brief and concise description of the conditions found to be in violation;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  A
statement of any corrective action required to be taken.  If the county has
determined that corrective action is required, the order shall require that all
corrective action commence within such time and be completed within such time
as the county determines is reasonable under the circumstances;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  A
statement specifying the amount of the civil penalty assessed, if any, on
account of the violation and, if applicable, the conditions on which assessment
of such civil penalty is contingent;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  A
statement advising that the order shall become final unless, after the notice
and order are served, any person aggrieved by the order files an appeal in
accordance with K.C.C. 20.22.080.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  Service of
the notice and order shall be made upon all persons identified in the notice
and order either personally or by mailing a copy of such notice and order by
certified mail, postage prepaid, return receipt requested.  If the address of
any such person cannot reasonably be ascertained, a copy of the notice and
order shall be mailed to such person at the address of the location of the
violation.  The failure of any such person to receive such notice shall not
affect the validity of any proceedings taken under this chapter.  Service by
certified mail shall be effective on the date of postmark.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  Any person
aggrieved by the order of the county may appeal that order in accordance with
K.C.C. 20.22.080.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.1.  The
appeal hearing shall be conducted on the record and the hearing examiner shall
have such rule-making and other powers necessary for conduct of the hearing as
specified by K.C.C. chapter 20.22.  The appeal hearing shall be conducted
within a reasonable time after receipt of the request for appeal.  Written
notice of the time and place of the hearing shall be given at least ten days
prior to the date of the hearing to each appealing party, to the cable manager
and to other interested person who have requested in writing that they be so
notified.  The county may submit a report and other evidence indicating the
basis for the enforcement order.  Each party shall have the following rights,
among others:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                a.  to
call and examine witnesses on any matter relevant to the issues of the hearing;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                b.  to
introduce documentary and physical evidence;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                c.  to
cross-examine opposing witnesses on any matter relevant to the issues of the
hearing;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                d.  to
impeach any witness regardless of which party first called the witness to
testify;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                e.  to
rebut evidence against the party; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                f.  to self-represent
or to be represented by anyone of the party’s choice who is lawfully permitted
to do so.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Following
review of the evidence submitted, the hearing examiner shall make written
findings and conclusions, and shall affirm or modify the order previously
issued if the hearing examiner finds that a violation has occurred.  The
hearing examiner shall reverse the order if the hearing examiner finds that no
violation occurred.  The written decision of the hearing examiner shall be
mailed by certified mail, postage prepaid, return receipt requested to all the
parties.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F.  Enforcement
of any notice and order of the county issued under this chapter shall be stayed
during the pendency of any appeal under this chapter. </span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            G.  An order that
is subjected to the appeal procedure shall become final twenty days after
mailing of the hearing examiner's decision unless within that time an aggrieved
person initiates review by writ of certiorari in King County superior court.  (Ord.
18728 § 43, 2018:  <span style='color:black'>Ord. 18230 § 85, 2016:  </span>Ord.
10159 § 26, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.250  Municipal
cable system ownership authorized.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The county
may construct, own, and/or operate a cable system.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  Nothing in
this chapter, the cable rules or a franchise agreement shall be interpreted to
affect the right of the county to acquire the property of the franchisee,
either by purchase or through the exercise of its right of eminent domain, for
an equitable price in the case of revocation, and at fair market value in the
case of any other form of franchise termination.  Further, nothing in this
chapter, the cable rules, or a franchise agreement shall be interpreted to
contract away, modify, or abridge, whether for a term or in perpetuity, the
county's right of eminent domain.  (Ord. 10159 § 27, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.260  Administration.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  This
chapter shall be implemented by means of administrative rules adopted by the
King County department of executive services in accordance with the provisions
of K.C.C. chapter 2.98.  These rules shall, at a minimum, contain requirements
for applications for new franchises and franchise renewals, modifications and
transfers, insurance coverage, security funds, letters of credit, restoration
bonds, minimum facilities, service and line extensions, payment of franchise
fees, reports and records, customer service, use of public rights-of-way,
technical standards, and price arbitration.  All rules shall comply with the
intent of this chapter and with applicable federal, state and local law. All
such rules shall have the force of law.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  This
chapter, the cable rules, and all franchise agreements shall be administered
and enforced by the cable office.  The functions of the cable office shall be
to:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  implement
cable policy, this chapter, the cable rules and franchise agreements;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  facilitate
the resolution of complaints received from any person;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  supervise
government programming with respect to PEG operations or coordinate with any
PEG access management authority designated by the county;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  provide
public information;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              5.  monitor
cable policy and related developments in other jurisdictions and make
recommendations for changes to county cable television policy;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              6.  develop
and maintain productive relationships with franchisees, other cable system
operators, and interested community groups to assure responsiveness to the
needs and interests of the community;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            7.  provide
staff assistance to any cable-related advisory committee or regulatory agency
hereafter established.  (Ord. 14199 § 120, 2001:  Ord. 10159 § 28, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.27A.270  Applicability
to current franchise agreements.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  This chapter and the
cable rules shall be applicable to all existing cable franchises and all
franchises issued in the county in the future.  (Ord. 10159 § 29, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc319998445"></a><a name="_Toc28263359">6.28      GO KART TRACKS</a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.010      Definitions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.020      License required &#8209; Fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.030      Renewal of license,
registration or permit &#8209; Late penalty.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.040      Compliance with zoning code.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.050      Liability insurance.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.060      Safety standards and
specifications.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.070      Reporting accidents and keeping
records.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.080      Telephone facilities.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.090      First&#8209;aid kit.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.100      Maintenance and inspections.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.110      Safety helmets.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.120      Penalty for violations.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.130      Civil penalty.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.140      Additional enforcement.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>6.28.010  Definitions.</b> 
For the purposes of this chapter, the words and phrases used herein shall have
the following meanings:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  &quot;Go
kart track&quot; means any place of business, whether open to the public or
operated on a private or semiprivate basis, whether or not operated for a
profit, wherein the use of karts for rides, rentals, demonstrations and/or
similar activities reasonably connected therewith and to only include herein
those operations commonly referred to as concession tracks.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  &quot;Go
kart&quot; means a miniature self-propelled vehicle designed to be
independently operated by the person riding therein and shall include the terms
&quot;cart,&quot; &quot;go cart&quot; or &quot;kart.&quot;  (Ord. 1888 Art. V §
22, 1974:  Res. 23509 § 1, 1961).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.020  License
required &#8209; Fee.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  It is unlawful to open, operate, conduct, manage,
maintain or control, or in any way be connected with the opening, operation,
conduct, management, maintenance or control of any go kart track without a
valid and subsisting license for each location.  The license shall be known as
a go kart track license, and the fee for the license is fixed in the sum of
$500.00 per year.  (Ord. 10170 § 8, 1991:  Res. 23509 § 2, 1961).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.030  Renewal
of license, registration or permit &#8209; Late penalty.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
A late penalty shall be charged on all applications for renewal of a license,
registration or permit received later than ten working days after the
expiration date of such license, registration or permit as set forth in the
respective resolution or ordinance establishing the expiration date of such
license, registration or permit.  The amount of such penalty is fixed as
follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            For a license,
registration or permit requiring a fee of fifty cents or more, but less than
fifty dollars &#8209; twenty percent of the required fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            For a license,
registration or permit requiring a fee of fifty dollars or more, but less than
one thousand dollars &#8209; ten percent of the required fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            For a license,
registration or permit requiring a fee of one thousand dollars or more &#8209;
five percent of the required fee.  (Ord. 1888 Art. IV § 3, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.040  Compliance
with zoning code.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  It is unlawful for any person to manage, conduct, carry
on or own the business of operating a go kart track unless the location and
establishment of such business complies with the provisions of the King County
zoning code or is deemed a nonconforming use thereunder.  (Res. 23509 § 3(1),
1961).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.050  Liability
insurance.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  It is unlawful for any person to manage, conduct, carry
on or own the business of operating a go kart track unless such person shall,
prior to the conducting, managing, carrying on or establishing of the go kart
track, obtain and maintain during the period of operation of the business
public liability insurance covering personal injuries, property damage and
medical expenses in limits of at least one hundred thousand dollars per
occurrence, with at least fifty thousand dollars for any one person per occurrence
and with at least five hundred dollars medical expense coverage per person per
occurrence.  Compliance with this section shall be deemed complete when the
person furnishes the director with proof of insurance coverage by a reputable
insurance carrier and with an endorsement to the effect that the director shall
receive at least ten days notice prior to the cancellation of such insurance
coverage of any such person governed by this chapter.  (Ord. 1888 Art. V § 23,
1974; Res. 23509 § 3(2), 1961).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.060  Safety
standards and specifications.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  All go kart tracks
regulated under the provisions of this chapter shall comply with the following
standards and specifications intended to protect and safeguard participants and
spectators at tracks:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The track
surface shall be a smooth, durable, nonskid material such as asphalt or
concrete.  Gravel or crushed rock surfaces are prohibited.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  Length of
tracks shall not exceed one-quarter mile.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  Length of
straight-of-ways on tracks shall not exceed three hundred feet.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  Width of
track shall be not less than sixteen feet on straight-of-ways and not less than
twenty feet on turns.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  Track may
have bank or super only on turns.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F.  Grades on
track shall not exceed five percent.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            G.  Track must
join with track edge smoothly to avoid a &quot;curb&quot; or drop-off hazard.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            H.  All tracks
must have a safety apron not less than fifteen feet wide between track and
fence on straight-of-ways and not less than twenty-five feet wide between the
track and fences on curves.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            I.  All tracks
shall be inside a fenced enclosure.  The fencing shall be chain link of No. 9
hogwire not less than four feet in height, with fence posts not less than five
and one-half feet in height and placed at intervals of not more than fifteen
feet.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            J.   Ingress
and egress to the track or pit areas shall be through gates which are kept
closed at all times when not in use.  Responsible supervision of participants
and spectators in the gate and pit areas must be provided at all times during
which the go kart track is in operation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            K.  Baled hay,
rubber tires or similar protective materials shall be placed on all turns or
curves at track and shall also be placed in a continuous ring two feet inside
chain link fence around the entire track.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            L.  Track pits
shall have separate entrance and exit lanes, shall have the same surface as
track, shall be fenced off from spectator areas and a responsible employee
shall supervise all pit activities.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            M.  No person
under the age of eight years shall be allowed to drive any go kart at speeds in
excess of twelve miles per hour.  No person under the age of eleven years shall
be allowed to drive any go kart at any speed in excess of twenty miles per
hour.  Under no circumstances shall go karts subject to the provisions hereof
be operated at speeds in excess of twenty miles per hour, except in connection
with sales demonstrations of single racing or competition go kart at any one
time.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            N.  Spectator
areas must be separated from track and pit areas by fencing as herein
provided.  Bleachers or grandstands, if any, shall be substantially constructed
and properly maintained.  Attendants must be on duty to control spectators and
parking.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            O.  All
attendants at a go kart track must at all times be under the direct control of
a responsible supervisor not less than eighteen years of age during all periods
of track use.  (Res. 23509 § 3(3), 1961).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>6.28.070  Reporting
accidents and keeping records.</b>  The manager or owner shall report in
writing all accidents of a nature to cause unconsciousness, broken or sprained
extremities or bones, removal, breaking or loosening of teeth, hemorrhaging or
lacerations which may require suturing or eye injuries to the director. 
Records thereof shall be maintained on the premises of all medical aid or care
administered.  (Ord. 1888 Art. V § 24, 1974; Res. 23509 § 4(a), 1961).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.080  Telephone
facilities.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Track owners shall provide a telephone facility
available for use on-site.  Telephone numbers of emergency medical services of
facilities should be conspicuously posted thereon.  Such telephone shall be
available for emergency use at all times during which the track is in
operation.  (Ord. 18728 § 44, 2018:  Res. 23509 § 4(b), 1961).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.090  First&#8209;aid
kit.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  A first-aid kit approved by the director shall be
maintained and be readily available on the track premises for emergency
treatment or care of a minor nature at all times during which the track is in
operation.  (Ord. 1888 Art. V § 25, 1974; Res. 23509 § 4(c), 1961).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.100  Maintenance
and inspections.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Go kart tracks and all related facilities and equipment
shall be maintained in good repair.  (Ord. 1888 Art. V § 26, 1974; Res. 23509 §
4(d), 1961).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.110  Safety
helmets.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  All persons riding go karts during periods of track
operation shall be required to wear standard safety or &quot;crash&quot;
helmets.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>(Res. 23509 § 4(e), 1961).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.120  Penalty
for violations.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Any person violating, or failing to comply with, any of
the provisions of this chapter shall be deemed guilty of a misdemeanor, and
upon conviction thereof shall be punished as prescribed by law.  (Res. 23509 §
7, 1961).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.130  Civil
penalty.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  In addition to or as an alternative to any other
penalty provided herein or by law any person who violates any provision of any
business license ordinance shall be subject to a civil penalty in an amount not
to exceed two hundred fifty dollars per violation to be directly assessed by
the director.  The director, in a reasonable manner, may vary the amount of the
penalty assessed to consider the appropriateness of the penalty to the size of
the business of the violator; the gravity of the violation; the number of past
and present violations committed and the good faith of the violator in
attempting to achieve compliance after notification of the violation.  All
civil penalties assessed will be enforced and collected in accordance with the
procedure specified under this title.  (Ord. 1888 Art. IV § 1, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.28.140  Additional
enforcement.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Notwithstanding the existence or use of any other
remedy, the director may seek legal or equitable relief to enjoin any acts or
practices which constitute or will constitute a violation of any business
license ordinance or other regulations herein adopted.  (Ord. 1888 Art. IV § 2,
1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc319998446"></a><a name="_Toc28263360">6.32      HEATING, AIR
CONDITIONING AND VENTILATION SYSTEMS INSTALLERS</a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.32.010      License required - fee - application
of chapter to manufacturers.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.32.020      Time limit for license
application - expiration date of license.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.32.030      Bond - Amount and terms - recovery
when more than one claim - suspension of license for reduction in amount of
bond.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.32.010  License
required - fee - application of chapter to manufacturers.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
It is unlawful for any person, firm or corporation to engage in the business
of, or to make representation as being engaged in the business of selling,
installing, altering or repairing heating, air-conditioning, ventilation and
exhaust systems equipment, without first procuring and being the holder of a
valid and subsisting license so to do, to be known as a &quot;HEATING, AIR-CONDITIONING,
VENTILATION SYSTEMS AND EQUIPMENT INSTALLERS LICENSE,&quot; the fee for which
is fixed in the sum of fifty dollars per year; provided, however that the terms
of this chapter shall not apply to the manufacture of heating, air-conditioning,
ventilation and exhaust systems as above defined.  (Ord. 780 (part), 1971: Ord.
205 § 1, 1969: Res. 16957 (part), 1957; Res. 12750 § 3, 1951).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.32.020  Time
limit for license application - expiration date of license.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  All
persons engaged in the business of selling, installing, altering or repairing
heating, air-conditioning, ventilation and exhaust systems equipment, at the
time this title takes effect, shall make application for a license hereunder
within ten days after this title takes effect.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            All heating,
air-conditioning, ventilation systems and equipment installers licenses shall
expire on June 30th of each year.  (Ord. 780 (part), 1971: Res. 16957 (part),
1957; Res. 13363 (part), 1952; Res. 12750 § 5, 1951).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.32.030  Bond
- Amount and terms - recovery when more than one claim - suspension of license
for reduction in amount of bond.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  No
heating, air-conditioning, ventilation systems and equipment installers license
shall be granted until the applicant has furnished a good and sufficient bond,
in a form approved by the director, in the penal sum of one thousand dollars,
executed by the applicant for license as principal and by a surety company
authorized to do business in this state running to the county of King, state of
Washington, and conditioned on the following:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  That the
principal will abide by the terms of this title and ordinances relating to the
sale, installation, alteration or repair of heating, air-conditioning,
ventilation and exhaust systems equipment;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  To save
harmless and indemnify King County from all and any loss, damages, actions and
claims of any kind or character that may accrue to or be suffered by any person
by reason of failure of the principal or the principal's servants and agents to
abide by the terms of this title and all ordinances relating to the sale,
installation, alteration or repair or heating, air-conditioning, ventilation
and exhaust systems equipment.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  To save
harmless and indemnify all persons for damages sustained on account of the
failure of the principal of such bond to comply with the terms of this title
and all ordinances relating to the sale, installation, alteration or repair of
heating, air-conditioning, ventilation and exhaust systems equipment;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  Claims
shall be maintained under the bond only if the claimant serves upon the surety
and King County notice of the amount of such claim and the nature thereof within
six months after the principal on the bond is completed or abandoned the work
giving rise to the claim, whereupon any bona fide payment of any such claim by
the surety, with prompt notice thereof to King County, shall reduce the amount
of the bond by the amount so provided, that if there is at one time more than
one unliquidated claim under the bond, of which notice has been given as herein
provided, and the total of such unliquidated claims exceeds the amount of the
bond at that time, the recoveries shall be prorated so that the totals of
recoveries against the surety under any circumstances shall not exceed one
thousand dollars, except as the bond may be reinstated with King County.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  In the
event any such bond or extension thereof is terminated or the amount thereof
reduced, any license granted under K.C.C. 6.32.010 shall be suspended until
such time as there is filed with King County a consent of the surety to the
restoration of the amount of the bond to the full sum of one thousand dollars
or until the filing of a new bond in the sum of one thousand dollars, any such
consent of surety or new bond is approved as provided for a new bond.  (Ord. 18728
§ 45, 2018:  Ord. 780 (part), 1971:  Res. 16957 (part), 1957;  Res. 12750 § 4,
1951).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc319998447"></a><a name="_Toc28263361">6.36      JUNK DEALERS</a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.010      License required.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.020      Definitions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.030      License fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.040      Application for license.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.050      Renewal of license,
registration or permit &#8209; Late penalty.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.060      Personal property tax return.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.070      Vehicle markings.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.080      Records required.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.090      Compliance required.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.100      Records and articles to be
available for inspection.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.110      Seller to give true name.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.120      Certain transactions
prohibited.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.130      No sale within ten days.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.140      Police officers to be admitted.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.150      Violation a misdemeanor.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.160      Civil penalty.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.170      Additional enforcement.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.010  License
required.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Junk Shop
License:  It is unlawful for any person, firm, or corporation to operate or
maintain a junk shop without first obtaining a &quot;junk shop license&quot;
pursuant to the provisions of this chapter.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  Junk Wagon
License:  It is unlawful for any person, firm, or corporation to operate or
maintain a junk wagon without first obtaining and displaying a valid and
subsisting &quot;junk wagon license&quot; pursuant to the provisions of this
chapter.  (Res. 36055 § 1, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.020  Definitions.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Junk:  The
word &quot;junk&quot; as used in this chapter shall be deemed to include and
mean old rope, old iron, brass, copper, tin, lead, rags, empty bottles, paper,
bagging, scrap metals of all kinds, and other worn out or discarded material.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  &quot;Junk
shop&quot; means any storeroom, building, yard, enclosure, or other place where
junk is sold, bought, received or stored shall be deemed to be a JUNK
&quot;junk shop&quot; within the meaning of this chapter; provided, however,
that such definition shall not apply where junk is:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  Purchased
from a source other than a junk wagon and is in prepared form by baling,
pressing, or otherwise; or in carload lots; or cut to specifications; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Purchased
from a licensed junk shop; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  Purchased
directly from the industrial producer of scrap metals, by the consumer there;
or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  Purchased
by automobile wreckers where automobiles are purchased and a certificate of
title furnished.</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>            C.  &quot;Junk
wagon&quot; means any vehicle used for the purpose of going from house to
house, place to place, buying or offering to buy, picking up or collecting junk
and transporting such junk, wholly or in part, within King County, regardless
of where the junk has been bought or collected, other than a vehicle used by a
regularly licensed junk shop in disposition of its own junk, is declared to be
a &quot;junk wagon&quot; within the meaning of this chapter.  (Res. 36055 § 2,
1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.030  License
fee.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Junk Shop
License:  The fee for a junk shop license shall be three hundred dollars per
year payable on the thirty-first of December preceding the year for which the
license is issued.  Fees becoming due for less than one year shall be prorated
on a quarterly basis.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  Junk Wagon
License Fee:  The fee for a junk wagon license shall be forty dollars per year
payable on the thirty-first of December preceding the year for which the
license is issued.  Fees becoming due for less than one year shall be prorated
on a quarterly basis.  (Ord. 10170 § 9, 1991:  Ord. 5799 § 5, 1981:  Res. 36055
§ 3, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.040  Application
for license.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  All applications for issuance or renewal of a junk shop
license or a junk wagon license shall be made to and be filed with the director
on forms furnished for such purpose.  This application shall state the true
name of the applicant, who shall not be less than eighteen years of age, the
names of all persons having a financial, proprietary, or other interest in such
junk shop together with such other information as the director deems
appropriate.  The application shall then be referred to the Department of
Public Safety for investigation, report and recommendation.  If from the
reports and other information available, the director deems the applicant to be
a fit and proper person, the director shall issue or renew the license applied
for.  (Ord. 1888 Art. V § 27, 1974:  Res. 36055 § 4, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.050  Renewal
of license, registration or permit &#8209; Late penalty.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
A late penalty shall be charged on all applications for renewal of a license,
registration or permit received later than ten working days after the
expiration date of such license, registration or permit as set forth in the
respective resolution or ordinance establishing the expiration date of such
license, registration or permit.  The amount of such penalty is fixed as
follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            For a license,
registration or permit requiring a fee of fifty cents or more but less than
fifty dollars &#8209; twenty percent of the required fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            For a license,
registration or permit requiring a fee of fifty dollars or more, but less than
one thousand dollars &#8209; ten percent of the required fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            For a license,
registration or permit requiring a fee of one thousand dollars or more &#8209;
five percent of the required fee.  (Ord. 1888 Art. IV § 3, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.060  Personal
property tax return.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No renewal license shall issue to any junk shop owner
or to any junk wagon owner until the applicant shall show that the owner has
made a return to the King County assessor of the property in the owner's
possession or ownership and the value thereof for tax assessment purposes and
has paid the tax due.  (Ord. 18728 § 46, 2018:  Res. 36055 § 5, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.070  Vehicle
markings.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Every licensee operating a junk wagon shall obtain from
the director two junk wagon vehicle licenses for each vehicle to be so used. 
On each license there shall be stamped or painted the word &quot;junk&quot; and
the license number of the licensee.  Each license shall be securely fastened to
each outer side of the vehicle.  In addition, such vehicle shall also be
prominently and plainly marked with the name of the licensee and the street
address of the licensee's place of business.  The vehicle marking license shall
remain the property of King County, and it is unlawful for any person other
than the licensee to whom the plates were issued to possess or use any such
plate.  Plates possessed or used in violation of this section, or used after
the junk wagon license has expired or been suspended, or if by a dealer, after the
dealer's junk shop license has expired or been suspended, shall be taken up by
any sheriff's deputy or the director.  (Ord. 18728 § 47, 2018:  Ord. 1888 Art.
V § 28, 1974:  Res. 36055 § 6, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.080  Records
required.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Every person who maintains or operates a junk shop
and/or a junk wagon shall provide and keep a book in which shall be plainly
written in ink, in the English language, at the time of every purchase, a
description of the article purchased, the printed name, signature, age, street
and house number, the general description of the dress, complexion, color and
appearance of the person from whom such purchase is made, and the day and hour
of such purchase.  All such records shall be present at the junk shop or junk
wagon, and shall be at all times available for inspection by officers of the
Department of Public Safety.  (Ord. 1888 Art. V § 29, 1974:  Res. 36055 § 7,
1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.090  Compliance
required.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  It is unlawful for any junk shop or junk wagon owner,
or any clerk, agent, or employee of such junk shop or junk wagon to fail,
neglect or refuse to make any material entry in the records required herein, or
to make any false entry therein, or to obliterate, destroy or remove from the
place of business such record within five years from the date of transaction. 
(Ord. 18728 § 48, 2018:  Res. 36055 § 8, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.100  Records
and articles to be available for inspection.</span></b><span style='font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  All books and
other records of any junk shop operator or any junk wagon operator relating to
the purchase or receipt of any goods, wares, merchandise, junk, or other
articles or things of value, shall be at all times open for inspection by the sheriff
or deputy; and all junk wagon operators shall at any time allow inspection of
their license and junk or other articles contained in the junk wagon.  (Ord. 18728
§ 49, 2018:  Ord. 1888 Art. V § 30, 1974:  Res. 36055 § 9, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.110  Seller
to give true name.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Anyone who sells or otherwise gives any property to a
junk shop operator or junk wagon operator shall sign the records required to be
kept by such operator with the person's true name and shall include the
person's correct residence address.  (Ord. 18728 § 50, 2018:  Res. 36055 § 10,
1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.120  Certain
transactions prohibited.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  It is
unlawful for any person to purchase any junk from any person under the age of
eighteen years, without receiving from such person a written authority from the
person owning such junk, authorizing the person selling the junk to sell the junk. 
Such a written authority shall be placed on file by the person receiving such
junk.  It is unlawful for any junk shop operator or junk wagon operator to
receive any article or thing known by the operator to be stolen, any article or
thing from any person who is under eighteen years of age; intoxicated; an
habitual drunkard; addicted to the use of drugs; or from any person who is
known to be a thief or a receiver of stolen property, or from any person who the
operator has reason to suspect or believe to be such.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  It is
unlawful for any operator of a junk shop, or person operating a junk wagon to
purchase any junk between the hours of seven p.m. and seven a.m. of the
following day.  (Ord. 18728 § 51, 2018:  Ord. 624 § 1, 1970:  Res. 36055 § 11,
1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.130  No
sale within ten days.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No junk shop operator or junk wagon operator shall sell
or otherwise dispose of any article received or purchased by the operator, or
remove or permit the same to be removed from the operator's place of business
within ten days after receipt of the articles have been reported to the sheriff's
office as herein provided, except when the articles have been inspected by a
regular member of the sheriff's office, and the operator has been authorized to
dispose of such goods within a lesser time.  (Ord. 18728 § 52, 2018:  Ord. 1888
Art. V § 31, 1974:  Res. 36055 § 12, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.140  Police
officers to be admitted.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  It is unlawful for any operator of a
junk shop or a junk wagon to refuse to allow any sheriff's deputy to inspect the
operator's place of business or the operator's junk wagon, and all articles of
junk kept therein, or to conceal or hide away any article or thing bought or
received by the operator.  (Ord. 18728 § 53, 2018:  Res. 36055 § 13, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.150  Violation
a misdemeanor.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Any violation of the provisions of this chapter shall
constitute a misdemeanor.  (Res. 36055 § 14, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.160  Civil
penalty.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  In addition to or as an alternative to any other
penalty provided herein or by law any person who violates any provision of any
business license ordinance shall be subject to a civil penalty in an amount not
to exceed two hundred fifty dollars per violation to be directly assessed by
the director.  The director, in a reasonable manner, may vary the amount of the
penalty assessed to consider the appropriateness of the penalty to the size of
the business of the violator; the gravity of the violation; the number of past
and present violations committed and the good faith of the violator in
attempting to achieve compliance after notification of the violation.  All
civil penalties assessed will be enforced and collected in accordance with the
procedure specified under this title.  (Ord. 1888 Art. IV § 1, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.36.170  Additional
enforcement.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Notwithstanding the existence or use of any other
remedy, the director may seek legal or equitable relief to enjoin any acts or
practices which constitute or will constitute a violation of any business
license ordinance or other regulations herein adopted.  (Ord. 1888 Art. IV § 2,
1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc319998448"></a><a name="_Toc28263362">6.40      MASSAGE
PARLORS AND PUBLIC BATHHOUSES</a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.010      Definitions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.020      General provisions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.030      License required.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.040      License application and
issuance.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.050      Standards for denial of
license.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.060      Expiration of license &#8209;
due date for license fees.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.070      License fees.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.080      Requirements for
licensing/operation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.090      Transfer of licenses and change
of location.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.100      Safety and sanitation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.110      Standards of conduct.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.120      Standards for suspension or
revocation of license.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.130      Violation &#8209; penalties.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.010 
Definitions.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  For the purpose of this chapter, the following terms,
words and phrases shall have the following meanings:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  &quot;Massage
business&quot; means the operation of a business where massages are given.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  &quot;Public
bathhouse&quot; means any place where baths or facilities for baths of any kind
whatever are given or furnished and the term shall include but not be limited
to:  Finnish baths; Russian baths; Sauna baths; Swedish baths; Turkish baths;
hot tubs; baths by hot air, steam, vapor, water or electric cabinet; provided,
that such term shall not include ordinary tub or shower baths where attendant
is not required.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  &quot;Massage
practitioner&quot; means a person engaged in the practice of massage.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  &quot;Genitals&quot;
includes genitals, pubic area, anus, or perineum of any person, or the vulva or
breasts of a female.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  &quot;Massage&quot;
means the treatment of a human body by another by the external manipulation or
pressure of soft tissue.  Massage includes rubbing, kneading, touching,
stroking, or tapping by manual means as they relate to massage with or without
the aids of superficial heat, cold, water, lubricants, or salts.  (Ord. 7919 §
2, 1987).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.020 
General provisions.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Unless otherwise specified, the general licensing
provisions, contained in King County Code, Chapter 6.01, shall apply to this
license section.  (Ord. 7919 § 3, 1987).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.030 
License required.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Massage
business &#8209; public bathhouse.  It is unlawful to conduct, operate or
maintain a massage business or public bathhouse unless such establishment or
premises is licensed as hereinafter provided.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  Massage
practitioner.  It is unlawful for any person to give a massage without a
massage practitioner license.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  Exemptions. 
This chapter shall not apply to:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  An
individual giving massage in their home to members of their immediate family;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Physicians,
surgeons, chiropractors, osteopaths, acupuncturists, or physical therapists who
are duly licensed or certified to practice their respective professions in the
State of Washington;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  Persons
practicing massage under the direct supervision of physicians, surgeons,
chiropractors, osteopaths, or physical therapists duly licensed by the State of
Washington.  Direct supervision shall mean that the massage is given on the
premises of or in the presence of such physicians, surgeons, chiropractors,
osteopaths, or physical therapists;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  Nurses
who are registered as such under the laws of the State of Washington and who
act under the direction and control of a duly licensed physician;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              5.  Persons
authorized by the laws of this state as barbers and cosmetologists, provided
that such massage as is practiced is within their authorized scope of practice;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              6.  Massage
practiced at the athletic department of any institution maintained by the
public funds of the state, or any of its political divisions; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              7.  Massage
practiced at the athletic department of any school or college accredited by the
northwest association of secondary and higher schools.  (Ord. 7919 § 4, 1987).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.040 
License application and issuance.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  All
applications for a massage business/public bathhouse shall be submitted in the
name of the person or entity proposing to conduct such massage business/public
bathhouse on the business premises and shall be signed by the person or the
person's agent and notarized or certified as true under penalty of perjury. 
All applications shall be submitted on a form supplied by the director, which
shall require the following information:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  The
name, home address, home telephone number, date and place of birth and social
security number of the applicant if the applicant is an individual;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  The
business name, address and telephone number of the establishment;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  The
names, addresses, telephone numbers, and social security numbers of any
partners, corporate officers, shareholders who own ten percent or more of the
business, or other persons who have a substantial interest or management
responsibilities in connection with the business, specifying the interest or
management responsibility of each.  For the purpose of this subsection
&quot;substantial interest&quot; shall mean ownership of ten percent or more of
the business, or any other kind of contribution to the business of the same or
greater size; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>              4.  Terms of
any loans, leases, secured transactions and repayments therefor relating to the
business;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  All
applications for a massage practitioner's license shall be signed by the
applicant and notarized or certified to be true under penalty of perjury.  All
applications shall be submitted on a form supplied by the director, which shall
require, at a minimum, the following information:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  The
applicant's name, home address, home telephone number, date and place of birth;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  A letter
from the owner of the business indicating intent to employ the applicant; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>              3.  Written
proof that the applicant is eighteen years of age or older.  Written proof
shall mean the following:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                a.  a
motor vehicle operator's license issued by any State bearing the applicant's
photograph and date of birth;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                b.  an
identification card issued by the state of Washington which bears the
applicant's photograph and date of birth; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                c.  a
passport.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  Applications
will be submitted to a background check in accordance with the procedures of
the sheriff's office.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  A license
shall be issued within four weeks of receipt if there are no grounds to deny
the license pursuant to the sections of this code.  (Ord. 18728 § 54, 2018:  Ord.
7919 § 5, 1987).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.050 
Standards for denial of license.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Massage
business or public bathhouse license.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  The
director shall deny any massage business/public bathhouse license applied for
under this chapter if the director determines that the applicant has:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                a.  made
any material misstatement in the application for a license;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                b.  proposed
a place of business or an establishment to be licensed which would not comply
with all applicable requirements of this code including but not limited to the
zoning, building, health or fire codes of King County; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                c.  not
complied with the operating requirements set out in Section 6.40.080 of this
chapter.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  The
director may deny any massage business/public bathhouse license applied for
under this chapter if the director determines that the applicant has, within
three years prior to the date of application:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                a.  had
any convictions or bail forfeitures that have a direct connection with the
licensed activity including, but not limited to, theft, controlled substances,
prostitution, promoting or permitting prostitution, sexual offenses, consumer
fraud, or obscenity; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                b.  had a
massage business/bathhouse license denied or revoked by this county or any
other jurisdiction.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  Massage
practitioner license.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  The
director shall deny any massage practitioner license if the director determines
that the applicant/licensee has:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                a.  made
any material misstatement in the application for a license; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                b.  not
complied with the operating requirements set out in K.C.C. 6.40.080.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  The
director may deny any massage practitioner's license if the director determines
that the applicant/licensee has:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                a.  had
any convictions or bail forfeitures which have a direct connection with the
licensed activity including, but not limited to, theft, controlled substances,
prostitution, sexual offenses, consumer fraud or obscenity, within three years
prior to the date of application; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                b.  had a
massage practitioner license revoked or suspended by the county or any other
jurisdiction within one year prior to the date of application.</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>            C.  If any
applicant has the applicant's license denied under K.C.C. 6.40.050 A.2.a. or
B.2.a., a license may not be granted within three years from the date of the
denial, if the denial was based on a conviction classified as a felony.  All
other convictions under K.C.C. 6.40.050 A.2.a. or B.2.a. will preclude the
issuance of a license under this chapter for a period of at least one year from
the date of such denial.  All applicants must comply with all application
procedures, pursuant to this chapter.  (<span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Ord.
18728 § 55, 2018:  </span>Ord. 7919 § 6, 1987).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.060  Expiration
of license &#8209; due date for license fees.</span></b><span style='font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Every license
issued or renewed pursuant to this chapter shall expire on the thirtieth of
November.  All license fees, set out in Section 6.40.070 of this chapter, are
payable to the director at least four weeks prior to the opening of any massage
business or public bathhouse, or the performance of massage in any massage
business or public bathhouse.  (Ord. 7919 § 7, 1987).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.070  License
fees.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The following fees are applicable to the licensing of
massage businesses, public bathhouses and massage practitioners in King County
as required in this chapter:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Massage
business                                                                     $150.00
per year</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  Public
bathhouse                                                                       $150.00
per year</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  Massage
practitioner                                                                 $  50.00
per year</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  Late
penalty &#8209; A late penalty shall be charged on all applications for renewal
of a license received later than ten working days after the expiration date of
such license.  The amount of such penalty is fixed as follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  Massage
business.                                                                  $  15.00</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Public
bathhouse                                                                      $ 
15.00</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  Massage
practitioner                                                               $   5.00</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>(Ord. 7919 § 8, 1987).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.080  Requirements
for licensing/operation.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The
director shall refer applications for massage business - public bathhouse to
the Seattle-King County department of public health and the King County fire
marshal with a request to inspect the premises or proposed premises and submit
a written report as to its sanitary and safety conditions.  An application for
a massage business conducted in the applicant's home shall not be referred to
the King County fire marshal.  All licensees shall:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  Comply
with the applicable safety and sanitation requirements of K.C.C. 6.40.100;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Keep
business receipts showing the date of service or services given, the type of
service or services rendered and the name and license number of the employee
rendering the service or services.  These business receipts shall be retained
for a period of three years after the date of the service or services, and
shall be open to inspection by the director and the King County department of
public safety;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  Allow
any police officer, the director or a representative from the Seattle-King
County department of public health or the King County fire marshal entry to the
premises during the hours the massage business or public bathhouse is open for
business, upon presentation of proper identification, for purposes of
inspecting the premises;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  Provide
that all doors in the premises, excluding doors in office and storage rooms,
unless the doors provide access to service areas, are so equipped that they may
not be fastened shut so as to prevent reasonable access by authorities listed
in subsection A.2 or 3. of this section who announce their authority to enter
prior to inspection of the premises;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              5.  Comply
with the applicable standards of conduct requirements set out in K.C.C. 6.40.110;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              6.  Comply
with the applicable provisions of the King County building, fire and zoning
codes;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              7.  Submit
proof of a current Washington State massage business license;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              8.  Shall
post in a prominent place a list of all services offered with a brief
description of what the service entails along with the costs for such
services.  All business transactions with customers must be conducted in
accordance with said posted list; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              9.  Shall
not distribute or consume liquor or controlled substances on licensed premises.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  All
applicants for a massage practitioner's license or license renewal shall:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  Be at
least eighteen years of age;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Submit
to a background check in accordance with the procedures of the King County
department of public safety;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  Submit
proof of a current Washington State massage license;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  Comply
with the applicable standards of conduct requirements of K.C.C. 6.40.110; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              5.  Comply
with the applicable safety and sanitation requirements of K.C.C. 6.40.100.  (Ord.
15319 § 2, 2005:  Ord. 9508, 1990:  Ord. 7919 § 9, 1987).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.090  Transfer
of licenses and change of location.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  No massage
business or public bathhouse license issued under this chapter shall be
transferable from one person to another.  Upon the sale or transfer of any
substantial interest in a massage business/public bathhouse, the license
therefore shall be null and void.  A new application shall be made by any
person desiring to operate or maintain the establishment and shall include a
release of interest statement from the previous licensee and/or a signed lease
or rental agreement for the establishment.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The
massage practitioner license, when issued, shall be valid only for the massage
establishment listed on the license.  However, if the practitioner provides
massage solely in the client's home, the license will so note and will be valid
for such purpose.  Before commencing work as a massage practitioner for a new
employer, a massage practitioner shall submit a letter from the new employer
indicating intent to employ the applicant and must have the massage
practitioner's license amended by the director for a fee of two dollars.  (Ord.
18728 § 56, 2018:  Ord. 7919 § 10, 1987).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.100  Safety
and sanitation.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Health and sanitary requirements may include, but are
not necessarily limited to, the following:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Each room
or enclosure where massage services are performed on patrons shall be provided
with adequate lighting in accordance with the building code, and in addition,
at least one artificial light of not less than forty watts shall be provided in
each room or enclosure where services are performed on patrons and shall be in
operation when such services are performed;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The
premises shall have equipment for disinfecting and cleaning non-disposable
instruments and materials used in administering massage services.  Such
materials and instruments shall be cleaned after each use;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  Hot and
cold running water shall be provided at all times;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  Closed
cabinets shall be provided and used for the storage of all equipment, supplies
and clean linens.  All used disposable materials and soiled linens and towels
shall be kept in covered containers or cabinets, which containers or cabinets
shall be kept separate from clean storage cabinets;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  Clean
linen and towels shall be provided for each massage patron.  No common use of
towels or linens shall be permitted;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F.  All
massage tables, bathtubs, shower stalls, sauna baths, steam or bath areas and
all floors shall have surfaces which may be readily cleaned;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            G.  Oils,
creams, lotions or other preparations used in administering massages shall be
kept in clean containers or cabinets;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            H.  Shower or
bathtub, dressing, locker and toilet facilities shall be provided upon request
for all patrons served at any given time.  Upon the request of a patron, the
licensee shall provide the patron with facilities to lock or secure personal
property.  Patrons of different genders shall not simultaneously use common
shower or bathtub, dressing, toilet and massage room facilities;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            I.  All walls,
ceilings, floors, pools, showers, bathtubs, steam rooms and all other physical
facilities shall be in good repair and maintained in a clean and sanitary
condition.  Wet and dry heat rooms, steam or vapor rooms, or steam or vapor
cabinets, shower compartments, and toilet rooms shall be thoroughly cleaned
each day the business is in operation.  Bathtubs and showers shall be
thoroughly cleaned after each use;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            J.  Each
massage practitioner shall wash the massage practitioner's hands in hot running
water using soap or disinfectant before and after administering a massage to
each patron;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            K.  No person
shall consume food or beverages in massage work areas;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            L.  Animals,
except for seeing-eye dogs, shall not be permitted in massage establishments;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            M.  A person
suffering from infectious or contagious disease or diseases shall not be
treated by any licensed massage business or public bathhouse or massage
practitioner.  A massage practitioner who is suffering from infectious or
contagious disease or diseases shall not administer massage services; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            N.  All
massage establishments shall continuously comply with all applicable building,
fire or health ordinances and regulations.  (Ord. 18728 § 57, 2018:  Ord. 7919
§ 11, 1987).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.110 
Standards of conduct.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The
following standards of conduct and operation must be adhered to by the owner,
proprietor, manager or person in charge of any massage business or public
bathhouse:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  Any
person who is employed to give a massage in such establishment must be at least
eighteen years of age and be validly licensed as a massage practitioner;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  At all
times during the hours held open for business or during the presence of
patrons, or both, at least one validly licensed massage practitioner must be on
the premises.  Public bathhouses must have a manager or supervisor on the
premises at all times during the hours held open for business and/or during the
presence of patrons; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  Any
person who is employed by such establishment must present documentation that the
employee has attained the age of eighteen years when an inspection pursuant to
this chapter is conducted.  Any of the following shall be accepted as
documentation of age:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                a.  a
motor vehicle operator's license issued by any state bearing the applicant's
photograph and date of birth;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                b.  an
identification card issued by the state of Washington bearing the applicant's photograph
and date of birth; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                c.  a
passport.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  It shall
be unlawful for any employee or agent or any massage business or public
bathhouse to:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  Intentionally
touch or manipulate the genitals of a massage patron;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Masturbate
or fondle the genital area of a massage patron;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  Administer
a massage to a massage patron unless such massage practitioner's sexual and
genital body parts are completely covered by opaque clothing; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  Administer
a massage to massage patrons in the same room or enclosure at the same time.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  Any
violation of this section shall be grounds for revocation or suspension of the
license.  (Ord. 18728 § 58, 2018:  Ord. 7919 § 12, 1987).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.120  Standards
for suspension or revocation of license.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.1.  The
director shall revoke or suspend a massage business/public bathhouse license if
the director determines that the licensee has:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                a.  failed
to comply with the applicable safety and sanitation requirements in K.C.C.
6.40.100;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                b.  failed
to comply with the applicable standards of conduct in K.C.C. 6.40.110;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                c.  failed
to comply with the applicable building, fire and zoning code provisions; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                d.  employed
persons who, within one year, have been convicted of prostitution or consumer
fraud stemming from activities conducted on the licensed premises, or who have
been arrested for such offenses and that lead to such convictions, but only if
there are two or more such convictions within one year, or two or more arrests
leading to such convictions within one year.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  The
director may revoke or suspend a massage business/public bathhouse license if
he determines that the licensee has:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                a.  failed
to comply with any of the operating requirements in K.C.C. 6.40.080 of this
chapter;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                b.  had
any convictions or bail forfeitures which have a direct connection with the
licensed activity, including, but not limited to, consumer fraud, theft,
controlled substances, prostitution, permitting or promoting prostitution,
sexual offenses or obscenity; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                c.  failed
to comply with or done anything which constitutes a basis for denying a
license.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  If the
director determines during an inspection that the condition of any massage
business needs correction, a  written notice of violation shall be issued to
the supervisor, manager, owner or person in charge specifying such violations. 
Those same violations shall be remedied immediately or by a later date
determined by the director.  Failure to comply with any written notice of
violation by the director to make corrections may result in suspension or
revocation of the massage business.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.1.  The
director shall suspend or revoke any massage practitioner's license if the director
determines that the licensee has failed to comply with the applicable standards
of conduct in K.C.C. 6.40.110.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  The
director may suspend or revoke any massage practitioner's license if the director
determines that the licensee has:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                a.  failed
to comply with any of the operating requirements in K.C.C. 6.40.080;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                b.  had
any convictions or bail forfeitures which have a direct connection with the
licensed activity including, but not limited to, theft, controlled substances,
prostitution, consumer fraud, obscenity or sexual offenses; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                c.  failed
to comply with or done anything which constitutes a basis for denying a
license.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  If any
applicant under this chapter has the applicant's license revoked, a license
shall not be granted under this chapter for a period of at least one year from
the date of such revocation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  The
director may suspend a license for no more than six months.  (Ord. 18728 § 59, 2018: 
Ord. 7919 § 13, 1987).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.40.130  Violation
&#8209; penalties.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A. 
Misdemeanor.  Every person as principal, agent or otherwise, failing,
neglecting or refusing to comply with any provision of this chapter, or
violating the same, shall be guilty of a misdemeanor.  Each day of such
failure, neglect or refusal to comply with the provision of this chapter or the
violation of same shall constitute a separate offense hereunder.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  Civil
penalty.  In addition to or as an alternative to any other penalty provided
herein or by law any person who violates any provision or any business license
ordinance shall be subject to a civil penalty in an amount not to exceed
two-hundred-fifty dollars per violation to be directly assessed by the
director.  The director, in a reasonable manner, may vary the amount of the
penalty assessed to consider the appropriateness of the penalty to the size of
the business of the violator; the gravity of the violation; the number of past
and present violations committed and the good faith of the violator in
attempting to achieve compliance after notification of the violation.  All
civil penalties assessed will be enforced and collected in accordance with the
procedure specified under this title.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  Additional
enforcement.  Notwithstanding the existence or use of any other remedy, the
director may seek legal or equitable relief to enjoin any acts or practices
which constitute a violation of any business license ordinance or other
regulations herein adopted.  (Ord. 7919 § 14, 1987).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc319998449"></a><a name="_Toc28263363">6.52      OUTDOOR
MUSICAL ENTERTAINMENTS</a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.52.010      Permit required.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.52.020      Application for permit.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.52.030      Permit fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.52.040      Submission of plans for
approval &#8209; Approving agencies.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.52.050      Conditions for permit issuance.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.52.060      Hours of operation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.52.070      Renewal of license,
registration or permit &#8209; Late penalty.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.52.080      Violation &#8209; Misdemeanor.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.52.090      Failure to comply.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.52.100      Civil penalty.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.52.110      Additional enforcement.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.52.010  Permit
required.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  It is unlawful for any person, persons, corporation,
organization, landowner, or lessor to allow, encourage, organize, promote,
conduct, permit or cause to be advertised an entertainment, amusement, or
assembly of persons wherein the primary purpose will be the presentation of
outdoor, live or recorded musical entertainment which the person, persons, or
corporation, organization, landowner or lessor believes or has reason to
believe will attract two hundred fifty or more persons and where a charge or contribution
is required for admission unless a valid county permit has been obtained for
the operation of the assembly; provided, however, that the assembly may be
advertised by the sponsors and/or organizers thereof after application for such
permit has been made.  (Ord. 187 § 1, 1969).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.52.020  Application
for permit.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Written application for outdoor musical amusements,
entertainments or assembly permits shall be made to the director forty or more
days prior to the date upon which such assembly is scheduled to be held. 
Written notice of approval or disapproval of the application shall be given to
the applicant no later than fifteen days after the application has been filed. 
Permits shall not be denied providing the conditions enumerated in Section
6.52.020 are met by the applicant.  Provided that no permit may be granted to
anyone who has been convicted of a felony or a crime involving moral
turpitude.  Provided further that each application shall be accompanied by the
fingerprints and a three by five inch photograph of each and every person
having any proprietary interest in the licensed activity.  The director shall
be empowered to obtain adequate photographs of all persons having any proprietary
interest.  (Ord. 1888 Art. V § 48, 1974:  Ord. 187 § 2, 1969).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.52.030  Permit
fee.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The basic fee required shall be seven hundred fifty
dollars for each event.  (Ord. 10451 § 2, 1992:  Ord. 10469 § 2, 1992:  Ord.
10170 § 12, 1991:  Ord. 1888 Art. V § 49, 1974:  Ord. 187 § 3, 1969).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.52.040  Submission
of plans for approval &#8209; Approving agencies.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
Whenever approval by a governmental agency other than the director is required
hereunder, the applicant for such approval shall be required to cooperate fully
with such agencies to insure that full review of the proposals may be
accomplished by the agencies within the fifteen day time limit set out in
Section 6.52.020.  When any type of physical facility is required or subject to
approval hereunder preliminary approval may be granted based upon specific
plans proposed and submitted by the applicant.  All such facilities shall be in
existence five or more days before the event for which an application is
submitted and shall be subject to inspection by the approving agencies or
departments.  Should the actual facility or construction fail to meet the standards
approved in the proposed plans such preliminary approval may be withdrawn and
any and all permits granted subject to such approval may be withdrawn.  (Ord.
1888 Art. V § 50, 1974:  Ord. 187 § 4, 1969).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.52.050  Conditions
for permit issuance.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  No permit
for an outdoor musical assembly shall be granted unless the assembly is to be
held in those areas of unincorporated King County that have been zoned for
parks and recreation.  However, a permit may be granted for other areas if a
zoning variance has been granted in advance by the executive department for the
location.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  No permit
shall be granted unless the applicants obtain the written approval of public
health – Seattle &amp; King County indicating that the applicants for the
permit have complied with the health requirements of the department for like or
similar facilities.  The approval shall indicate the type and adequacy of water
supply to be provided, the type and adequacy of toilet, waste collection and
washing facilities to be provided, and if there is to be food served on the
premises the type and adequacy of food preparation and food service facilities
to be provided.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  No permit
shall be granted hereunder unless the applicant has shown that the King County
fire marshal has approved fire protection devices and equipment available at
such assembly.  Fire prevention standards shall be as set out in K.C.C. chapter
17.04.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  No permit
shall be issued hereunder unless the applicant has on deposit with the director
of finance and business operations a cash bond in the amount as set out below
to save and protect the streets, pavements, bridges, road signs and other
property in the county from any and all damage that may be caused by vehicles,
employees, or participants in such outdoor musical assembly and to be used, if
necessary, to restore the ground where such assembly is held to a sanitary
condition and pay all charges and losses of the county for damages to the
streets, pavements, bridges and other property.  Further, any extraordinary law
enforcement costs incurred by the county which are the result of the activity
shall be met by the cash bond.  The amount of such a bond shall be determined
as follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            For gatherings
of 0 to 10,000 persons, a $5,000 cash bond;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            For gatherings
of 10,000 to 20,000 persons, a cash bond of $7,500;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            For gatherings
of 20,000 to 30,000 persons, a cash bond of $10,000;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            And a cash
bond shall be raised in increments of $2,500 for each additional 10,000 persons
expected.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            The deposit or
its balance to be returned when the director certifies to the King County
comptroller that no damage has been done or that the cost of making the above
mentioned repairs was less than the cash bond amount and that the balance
thereof should be returned.  Further, the sponsors shall be required to furnish
evidence of a liability insurance policy providing for a minimum of one hundred
thousand dollars bodily injury coverage per person; three hundred thousand
dollars bodily injury coverage per occurrence and one hundred thousand dollars
property damage covering, naming King County as an additional insured.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  No permit
shall be granted hereunder unless the applicant obtained the written approval
of the sheriff's office indicating that the following conditions have been
complied with by the applicant:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  That
adequate traffic control and crowd protection policing have been contracted for
or otherwise provided by the applicant;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  That
traffic control and crowd control personnel shall be licensed private patrol
persons or named persons meeting the department's requirements for becoming private
patrol persons;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  That
there shall be provided one traffic control person for each four hundred
persons expected or reasonably to be expected to be in attendance at any time
during the event; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  Further
that there shall be provided one crowd control person for each four hundred
persons expected or reasonably expected to be in attendance at any time during
the event; provided that if at any time during the event the size of the crowd
exceeds by twenty percent the number of persons represented by the sponsors to
be expected to be in attendance the sheriff's office shall have the discretion
to require the sponsor to limit further admissions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Any person
with more than a ten percent proprietary interest in the event shall be
required to be in attendance at the activity and shall be responsible for
insuring that no person shall be allowed to remain on the premises if the
person is violating state or county laws.  Any such person having a duty to
remove law violators who willfully fails to do so shall be deemed to be an
aider or abettor of such violation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F.  Application
for a permit hereunder shall be accompanied by a scale drawing showing adequate
parking facilities have been made available within or adjacent to the location
for which the permit is requested.  Such parking facilities shall provide
parking space for one vehicle for every four persons expected or reasonably to
be expected.  Adequate ingress and egress shall be provided to or from such
parking area to facilitate the movement of any vehicle at any time to or from
the parking area.  If any nonadjacent parking facilities are approved, shuttle
buses shall be used to transport the public to the event on a no-charge basis. 
(Ord. 18728 § 60, 2018:  Ord. 1888 Art. V § 51, 1974:  Ord. 187 § 5, 1969).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.52.060  Hours
of operation.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No outdoor musical assembly shall be conducted in the
unincorporated areas of King County during the hours of 12:01 a.m. and 9:00
a.m.; provided, that no license shall be issued for more than one forty-eight
hour period ending at midnight.  The participants shall be required to have
cleared the licensed area and its immediate environs no later than one a.m. of
each day of the licensed event.  (Ord. 10451 § 3, 1992:  Ord. 187 § 6, 1969).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.52.070  Renewal
of license, registration or permit &#8209; Late penalty.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
A late penalty shall be charged on all applications for renewal of a license,
registration or permit received later than ten working days after the
expiration date of such license, registration or permit as set forth in the
respective resolution or ordinance establishing the expiration date of such
license, registration or permit.  The amount of such penalty is fixed as
follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            For a license,
registration or permit requiring a fee of fifty cents or more, but less than
fifty dollars &#8209; twenty percent of the required fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            For a license,
registration or permit requiring a fee of fifty dollars or more, but less than
one thousand dollars &#8209; ten percent of the required fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            For a license,
registration or permit requiring a fee of one thousand dollars or more &#8209;
five percent of the required fee.  (Ord. 1888 Art. IV § 3, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.52.080  Violation
&#8209; Misdemeanor.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Any person who violates or fails to comply with any
provision of this chapter, who, having obtained a permit hereunder, willfully
fails to continue to comply with the terms and conditions hereunder, or who
counsels, aids or abets such a violation or failure to comply is guilty of a
misdemeanor.  (Ord. 187 § 7, 1969).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.52.090  Failure
to comply.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Compliance with the terms and conditions of this
chapter constitutes the minimum health, sanitation and safety provisions and
failure to comply with the terms and conditions constitutes a public nuisance
and the sponsors of the event shall be subject to all criminal and civil
remedies as such.  (Ord. 187 § 8, 1969).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.52.100  Civil
penalty.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  In addition to or as an alternative to any other
penalty provided herein or by law any person who violates any provision of any
business license ordinance shall be subject to a civil penalty in an amount not
to exceed two hundred fifty dollars per violation to be directly assessed by
the director.  The director, in a reasonable manner, may vary the amount of the
penalty assessed to consider the appropriateness of the penalty to the size of
the business of the violator; the gravity of the violation; the number of past
and present violations committed and the good faith of the violator in
attempting to achieve compliance after notification of the violation.  All
civil penalties assessed will be enforced and collected in accordance with the
procedure specified under this title.  (Ord. 1888 Art. IV § 1, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.52.110  Additional
enforcement.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Notwithstanding the existence or use of any other
remedy, the director may seek legal or equitable relief to enjoin any acts or
practices which constitute or will constitute a violation of any business
license ordinance or other regulations herein adopted.  (Ord. 1888 Art. IV § 2,
1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc28263364"></a><a name="_Toc319998450">6.56      PAWNBROKERS</a>*</h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.010      License required.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.020      Pawnbroker and pawnshop
defined.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.030      License fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.040      Application for license.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.050      Personal property tax return.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.060      Limitations on licensing.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.070      Renewal of license,
registration or permit &#8209; Late penalty.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.080      Records required.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.090      Compliance required.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.100      Transcript to be furnished.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.110      Records and articles to be
available for inspection.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.120      Seller or consignee to give
true name and address.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.130      Authorized rate of interest &#8209;
Penalty for violation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.140      Prima facie evidence of
violation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.150      Period of redemption.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.160      Certain transactions
prohibited.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.170      Pawnshop to be closed during
certain hours.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.180      Violation &#8209; Misdemeanor.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.190      Civil penalty.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.200      Additional enforcement.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*For statutory provisions
regarding business regulations of pawnbrokers, see chapter 19.60 RCW.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.010 
License required.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  It is unlawful for any person, firm, or corporation to
engage in the business of pawnbroker, or to conduct a pawnshop without first
obtaining a &quot;pawnbroker's license&quot; pursuant to the provisions of this
chapter.  (Res. 36053 § 1, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.020 
Pawnbroker and pawnshop defined.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The term
&quot;pawnbroker&quot; as used in this chapter, means and includes every person
who takes or receives by way of pledge, pawn, or exchange goods, wares, or
merchandise or any kind of personal property whatever, for the repayment of
security of any money loaned thereon, or to loan money on deposit of personal
property, or who makes a public display of any sign indicating that the pawnbroker
has money to loan on personal property on deposit or pledge.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The term
&quot;pawnshop&quot; means and includes every place at which the business of
pawnbroker is being carried on.  (Ord. 18728 § 61, 2018:  Res. 36053 § 2,
1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.030 
License fee.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The fee for such license shall be five hundred dollars
per year, payable on the thirty-first of December preceding the year for which
the license is issued.  Fees becoming due for less than one year shall be
prorated on a quarterly basis.  (Ord. 10170 § 13, 1991:  Res. 36053 § 3, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.040 
Application for license.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  All applications for issuance or
renewal of a pawnbroker's license shall be made to and be filed with the
director on forms furnished for such purpose.  This application shall state the
true name of the applicant, who shall not be less than eighteen years of age,
the names of all persons having a financial, proprietary, or other interest in
such pawnshop, together with such other information as the license division
deems appropriate.  The application shall then be referred to the Department of
Public Safety for investigation, report and recommendation.  If, from the
reports and other information available, the director deems the applicant to be
a fit and proper person, the director shall issue or renew the license applied
for.  (Ord. 1888 Art. V § 52, 1974;  Ord. 1005 § 2, 1971:  Res. 36053 § 4,
1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.050  Personal
property tax return.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No renewal license shall be issued to any pawnbroker
until the applicant returns to King County assessor of the property in the
applicant's possession or ownership and the value thereof for tax assessment
purposes and has paid the tax due.  (Ord. 18728 § 62, 2018:  Res. 36053 § 5,
1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.060  Limitation
on licensing.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No pawnbroker's license shall be issued which would
increase the number of holders of such licenses to more than one for every
fifteen thousand of population, according to the last preceding federal census,
provided that this population limitation shall not operate to prohibit the
licensing of any pawnbroker duly licensed prior to the enactment of this
chapter, if such pawnbroker is otherwise duly qualified.  (Res. 36053 § 6,
1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.070  Renewal
of license, registration or permit &#8209; Late penalty.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
A late penalty shall be charged on all applications for renewal of a license,
registration or permit received later than ten working days after the
expiration date of such license, registration or permit as set forth in the
respective resolution or ordinance establishing the expiration date of such
license, registration or permit.  The amount of such penalty is fixed as
follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            For a license,
registration or permit requiring a fee of fifty cents or more, but less than
fifty dollars &#8209; twenty percent of the required fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            For a license,
registration or permit requiring a fee of fifty dollars or more, but less than
one thousand dollars &#8209; ten percent of the required fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            For a license,
registration or permit requiring a fee of one thousand dollars or more &#8209;
five percent of the required fee.  (Ord. 1888 Art. IV § 3, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.080  Records
required.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Every pawnbroker shall maintain at the pawnbroker's
place of business a book in which the pawnbroker shall at the time of such
loan, purchase or sale, enter, in the English language, written in ink, the
following information:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The date
of the transaction;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The name
of the person conducting the transaction and making the entries required
herein;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  The
printed name, signature, age, street and house number, the general description
of the dress, complexion, color of hair and facial appearance of the person
with whom the transaction is had, including the identification which the
customer shall present to verify the customer's identity, and the account or
other number of such identification;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  The name
and street and house number of the owner of the property bought or received in
pledge;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  The street
and house number of the place from which the property bought or received in
pledge was last removed;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F.  A
description of the property bought or received in pledge, which shall include
the name of the maker of such property or manufacturer thereof and the serial
number, if the article has such marks on it, or any other inscriptive or
identifying marks; provided, that when the article received is furniture or the
contents of any house or room, actually inspected on the premises where the
sale is made, a general description of the property shall be sufficient;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            G.  The price
paid or the amount loaned; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            H.  The number
of any pawn tickets issued therefor.  (Ord. 18728 § 63, 2018:  Res. 36053 § 7,
1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.090  Compliance
required.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  It is unlawful for any pawnbroker or any clerk, agent,
or employee of such pawnbroker to fail, neglect or refuse to make any material
entry in this record, as required by this chapter, or to make any false entry
therein, or to obliterate, destroy or remove from the pawnbroker's place of
business such record within five years from date of transaction.  (Ord. 18728 §
64, 2018:  Res. 36053 § 8, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.100  Transcript
to be furnished.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  It is the
duty of every pawnbroker to deliver to the sheriff's office at the close of
every business week a full, true and correct transcript of the record of all
transactions occurring during the preceding week.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  It is also
the duty of any pawnbroker having good cause to believe any property in the
pawnbroker's possession has been previously lost or stolen, to report such fact
to the sheriff immediately, together with the name of the owner, if known, and
the date and name of the person from whom the same was received by such
pawnbroker.  (Ord. 18728 § 65, 2018:  Ord. 1888 Art. V § 75, 1974; Res. 36053 §
9, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.110  Records
and articles to be available for inspection.</span></b><span style='font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  All books and
other records of any pawnbroker relating to purchase, pledge, exchange, order
or receipt of any goods, wares, merchandise, or other articles or things of
value, shall at all times be open for inspection by the King County Department
of Public Safety; and all articles or things received, purchased or left in
pledge with the pawnbroker shall at all times be open to a like inspection. 
(Ord. 1888 Art. V § 76, 1974; Res. 36053 § 10, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.120  Seller
or consignee to give true name and address.</span></b><span style='font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Anyone who
pledges, sells, or consigns any property to or with a pawnbroker shall sign the
records required to be kept by such pawnbroker with the seller or consignee's
true name and shall include the seller or consignee's correct residence
address.  (Ord. 18728 § 66, 2018:  Res. 36053 § 11, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.130  Authorized
rate of interest &#8209; Penalty for violation.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
All pawnbrokers are authorized to charge and receive interest at the rate of
three percent per month, for any loan on the security of personal property
actually received in pledge, and every person who asks or receives a higher
rate of interest or discount on any such loan, or on any actual or pretended
sale, shall, on redemption of such personal property, be deemed guilty of a
violation of this chapter.  (Res. 36053 § 12, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.140  Prima
facie evidence of violation.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The fact of loaning
money upon or purchasing goods from any of the classes enumerated in K.C.C.
6.56.130 shall be prima facie evidence of an intent on the part of such
pawnbroker, the pawnbroker's agent or employee, to violate this chapter.  (Ord.
18728 § 67, 2018:  Res. 36053 § 13, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.150  Period
of redemption.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No pawnbroker shall sell any property held by the
pawnbroker as security for a loan until ninety days after the period for
redemption shall have expired.  (Ord. 18728 § 68, 2018:  Res. 36053 § 14,
1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.160  Certain
transactions prohibited.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  It is
unlawful for any pawnbroker, the pawnbroker's clerk or employee to receive in
pledge, or purchase, any article or thing known to the pawnbroker or the
pawnbroker's clerk or employee to be stolen, any article or thing from any
person who is under eighteen years of age; intoxicated; addicted to the use of
drugs; or from any person who is known to be a thief, or a receiver of stolen
property, or from any person who the pawnbroker or the pawnbroker's clerk or
employee has reason to suspect or believe to be such.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  It is
unlawful for any pawnbroker, the pawnbroker's clerk or employee, to refuse to
return property which has been identified as stolen or pawned without
authorization, to any person the pawnbroker, the pawnbroker's clerk or employee
knows to be the rightful owner, or to charge a fee for the return of such
property to the rightful owner.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  &quot;Identified
as stolen or pawned without authorization&quot; shall mean any property which
has been reported by the rightful owner to legitimate authority as missing or
stolen.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  &quot;The
rightful owner,&quot; unless otherwise proven, shall be considered to be the
person having possession of the property prior to the theft or removal without
authorization.  (Ord. 18728 § 69, 2018:  Ord. 6383 § 1, 1983:  Ord. 521 § 1,
1970: Res. 36053 § 15, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.170  Pawnshop
to be closed during certain hours.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  It is unlawful for any
pawnbroker to conduct or carry on the business of the pawnbroker, in whole or
in part, directly or indirectly, or to open or keep open, the pawnshop for the
transaction of any business whatsoever therein, between the hours of eight p.m.
and seven a.m., except that from December 1 to December 24 of each year, when
pawnbrokers may remain open until ten p.m. (Ord. 18728 § 70, 2018:  Res. 36053
§ 16, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.180  Violation
&#8209; Misdemeanor.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Any violation of the provisions of this chapter
constitutes a misdemeanor.  (Res. 36053 § 17, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.190  Civil
penalty.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  In addition to or as an alternative to any other
penalty provided herein or by law any person who violates any provision of any
business license ordinance shall be subject to a civil penalty in an amount not
to exceed two hundred fifty dollars per violation to be directly assessed by
the director.  The director, in a reasonable manner, may vary the amount of the
penalty assessed to consider the appropriateness of the penalty to the size of
the business of the violator; the gravity of the violation; the number of past
and present violations committed and the good faith of the violator in
attempting to achieve compliance after notification of the violation.  All
civil penalties assessed will be enforced and collected in accordance with the
procedure specified under this title.  (Ord. 1888 Art. IV § 1, 1973).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.56.200  Additional
enforcement.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Notwithstanding the existence or use of any other
remedy, the director may seek legal or equitable relief to enjoin any acts or
practices which constitute or will constitute a violation of any business
license ordinance or other regulations herein adopted.  (Ord. 1888 Art. IV § 2,
1973).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><a
name="SECONDHAND_DEALERS"><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>6.60    SECONDHAND DEALERS*</span></b></a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.010      License required.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.020      Secondhand dealer and
secondhand goods defined.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.030      License fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.040      Application for a license.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.050      Renewal of license,
registration or permit &#8209; late penalty.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.060      Personal property tax return.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.070      More than one shop - change of
location.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.080      Records required.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.090      Compliance required.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.100      Transcript to be furnished.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.110      Records and articles to be
available for inspection.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.120      Seller to give true name and
address.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.130      No sale within ten days.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.140      Certain transactions
prohibited.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.150      Violation a misdemeanor.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.160      Civil penalty.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.170      Additional enforcement.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*For statutory provisions
regulating secondhand dealers, see chapter 19.60 RCW.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.010  License
required.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  It is unlawful for any person, firm or corporation to
engage in the business of buying, selling, or trading in secondhand goods in
King County without first obtaining a &quot;secondhand dealer's license&quot;
pursuant to the provisions of this chapter.  (Res. 36054 § 1, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.020  Secondhand
dealer and secondhand goods defined.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The term
&quot;secondhand dealer&quot; as used in this chapter, means and includes every
person who as a business engages in the purchase, sale, trade, barter, auction,
sale on consignment, or otherwise exchanges secondhand goods, or who keeps a
store, shop, room or other place where secondhand goods of any kind or
description are bought, sold, traded, bartered, pledged, pawned, auctioned,
sold on consignment, or otherwise exchanged, including dealers in used or
remanufactured automobile tires or parts; provided, however, that this term
shall not apply to those persons engaged in the business of selling used or
secondhand motor vehicles or boats.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The term
&quot;secondhand goods&quot; when used in this chapter means and includes any
and all used, remanufactured, or secondhand goods purchased or kept for sale by
a dealer in secondhand goods; provided however, such term shall not be
construed to include junk as defined in Section 6.36.020, or used or secondhand
motor vehicles or boats.  (Ord. 623 § 1, 1970:  Res. 36054 § 2, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.030  License
fee.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The fee for such license shall be forty dollars per
year, payable on the thirty&#8209;first of December preceding the year for
which the license is issued.  Fees becoming due for less than one year shall be
prorated on a quarterly basis.  (Ord. 10170 § 14, 1991:  Ord. 5799 § 7, 1981: 
Res. 36054 § 3, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.040  Application
for a license.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  All applications for issuance or renewal of secondhand
dealer's license shall be made to and be filed with the director on forms
furnished for such purpose.  This application shall state the true name of the
applicant, who shall not be less than eighteen years of age, the names of all
persons having a financial, proprietary, or other interest in such secondhand
dealer's shop, together with such other information as the director deems
appropriate.  The application shall then be referred to the King County Department
of Public Safety for investigation, report, and recommendation.  If, from the
reports and other information available, the license division deems the
applicant to be a fit and proper person, the director shall issue or renew the
license applied for.  (Ord. 1888 Art. V § 77, 1974; Ord. 1005 § 3, 1971: Res.
36054 § 4, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.050  Renewal
of license, registration of permit - late penalty.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
A late penalty shall be charged on all applications for renewal of a license,
registration or permit received later than ten working days after the
expiration date of such license, registration or permit as set forth in the
respective resolution or ordinance establishing the expiration date of such
license, registration or permit.  The amount of such penalty is fixed as
follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            For a license,
registration or permit requiring a fee of fifty cents or more, but less than
fifty dollars &#8209; twenty percent of the required fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            For a license,
registration or permit requiring a fee of fifty dollars or more, but less than
one thousand dollars &#8209; ten percent of the required fee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            For a license,
registration or permit requiring a fee of one thousand dollars or more &#8209;
five percent of the required fee.  (Ord. 1888 Art. IV § 3, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.060  Personal
property tax return.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No renewal license shall be issued to any secondhand
dealer until the applicant returns to the King County assessor of the property
in the applicant's possession or ownership and the value thereof for tax
assessment purposes and has paid the tax due.  (Ord. 18728 § 71, 2018:  Res.
36054 § 5, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.070  More
than one shop - change of location.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Any person having more
than one place of business where secondhand goods are bought, sold, traded,
bartered, or exchanged, shall be required to procure a separate license for
each and every such place of business.  A secondhand dealer's license shall not
be transferable from one person to another, but the licensee may have the
license transferred to a new location by the director, and the change of
address shall be noted on the license, together with the date of which the
change was made.  (Ord. 18728 § 72, 2018:  Ord. 1888 Art. V § 53, 1974; Res.
36054 § 6, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.080  Records
required.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Every secondhand dealer shall maintain at the
secondhand dealer's place of business a book in which the secondhand dealer shall
at the time of purchase of any secondhand goods enter, in the English language,
written in ink, the following information:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The date
of the transaction;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The name
of the person conducting the transaction and making the entries required
herein;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  The
printed name, signature, age and address of the person with whom the
transaction is had;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  The
address of the place from which the property was last removed;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  An
accurate description of the property bought, which shall include the name of
the maker of such property or manufacturer thereof and the serial number, if
the article has such marks on it, or any other inscriptive or identifying
marks, except that when the article received is furniture or the contents of
any house or room, actually inspected on the premises where the sale is made,
the general description of the property shall be sufficient; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F.  An
itemized statement of the price or amount paid for the property purchased.  (Ord.
18728 § 73, 2018:  Res. 36054 § 7, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.090  Compliance
required.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  It is unlawful for any secondhand dealer, or any clerk,
agent, or employee of such secondhand dealer to fail, neglect, or refuse to
make any material entry in this record, as required by this chapter, or to make
any false entry therein, or to obliterate, destroy, or remove from the
secondhand dealer's place of business such record within five years from the
date of the transaction.  (Ord. 18728 § 74, 2018:  Res. 36054 § 8, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.100  Transcript
to be furnished.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  It is the
duty of every secondhand dealer to deliver to the sheriff's office at the close
of every business week a full, true and correct transcript of the record of all
transactions occurring during the preceding week.  Secondhand goods taken on
consignment or trade-in will be recorded in the same manner as goods purchased
outright.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  It is also
the duty of any secondhand dealer having good cause to believe any property in the
secondhand dealer's possession has been previously lost or stolen, to report
such act to the sheriff immediately, together with the name of the owner, if
known, and the date and name of the person from whom the same was received by
such secondhand dealer.  (Ord. 18728 § 75, 2018:  Ord. 1888 Art. V § 55, 1974; 
Res. 36054 § 9, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.110  Records
and articles to be available for inspection.</span></b><span style='font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  All books and
other records of any secondhand dealer relating to purchase or receipt of any
goods, wares, merchandise, or other things of value, shall at all times be open
for inspection by the King County Department of Public Safety; and all articles
or things received or purchased shall at all times be open to a like
inspection.  (Ord. 1888 Art. V § 55, 1974; Res. 36054 § 10, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.120  Seller
to give true name and address.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Anyone who sells or
otherwise leaves any property with a secondhand dealer shall sign the records
required to be kept by such dealer with the seller's or leaver's true name and
shall include the seller's or leaver's correct residence address.  (Ord. 18728
§ 76, 2018:  Res. 36054 § 11, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.130  No
sale within ten days.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No dealer in secondhand goods shall sell or dispose of
any article received or purchased by the secondhand dealer or permit the same
to be removed from the secondhand dealer's place of business within ten days
after the receipt of the goods has been reported to the sheriff as provided
herein, except when the goods have been inspected by regular members of the appropriate
sheriff personnel, and they have authorized the secondhand dealer to dispose of
such goods within a lesser period of time, except that consigned property sold
at auction need only be held for three days prior to sale.  (Ord. 18728 § 77, 2018: 
Ord. 623 § 2, 1970:  Res. 36054 § 12, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.140  Certain
transactions prohibited.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  It is
unlawful for any secondhand dealer, the secondhand dealer's clerk or employee,
to purchase or receive any article or thing known by the secondhand dealer or
the secondhand dealer's clerk or employee to be stolen, any article or thing
from a person who is under eighteen years of age, intoxicated, addicted to the
use of drugs, or from any person who is known to be a thief, or a receiver of
stolen property, or from any person who the secondhand dealer or the secondhand
dealer's clerk or employee has reason to suspect or believe to be such.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  It is
unlawful for any secondhand dealer, the secondhand dealer's clerk or employee
to refuse to return property which has been identified as stolen or sold
without authorization, to any person the secondhand dealer, the secondhand
dealer's clerk or employee, knows to be the rightful owner, or to charge a fee
for the return of such property to the rightful owner.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  &quot;Identified
as stolen or sold without authorization&quot; shall mean any property which has
been reported by the rightful owner to legitimate authority as missing or
stolen.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  &quot;The
rightful owner,&quot; unless otherwise proven, shall be considered to be the
person having possession of the property prior to the theft or removal without
authorization.  (Ord. 18728 § 78, 2018:  Ord. 6383 § 2, 1983:  Ord. 623 § 3,
1970:  Res. 36054 § 13, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.150  Violation
a misdemeanor.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Any violation of the provisions of this chapter shall
constitute a misdemeanor.  (Res. 36054 § 14, 1968).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.160  Civil
penalty.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  In addition to or as an alternative to any other
penalty provided herein or by law any person who violates any provision of any
business license ordinance shall be subject to a civil penalty in an amount not
to exceed two hundred fifty dollars per violation to be directly assessed by
the director.  The director, in a reasonable manner, may vary the amount of the
penalty assessed to consider the appropriateness of the penalty to the size of
the business of the violator, the gravity of the violation, the number of past
and present violations committed and the good faith of the violator in
attempting to achieve compliance after notification of the violation.  All
civil penalties assessed will be enforced and collected in accordance with the
procedure specified under this title.  (Ord. 1888 Art. IV § 1, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.60.170  Additional
enforcement.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Notwithstanding the existence or use of any other
remedy, the director may seek legal or equitable relief to enjoin any acts or
practices which constitute or will constitute a violation of any business
license ordinance or other regulations herein adopted.  (Ord. 1888 Art. IV § 2,
1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc28263365"></a><a name="_Toc319998451">6.64      </a>FOR-HIRE
TRANSPORTATION - TRANSPORTATION NETWORK COMPANIES, VEHICLES, AND DRIVERS</h1>

<h1>(Formerly FOR-HIRE TRANSPORTATION - TAXICABS, FOR-HIRE VEHICLES, FOR-HIRE
DRIVERS AND TRANSPORTATION NETWORK COMPANIES)</h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.005      Application of chapter -
resolution of conflicts with K.C.C. chapter 6.65.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.010      Definitions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.015      Interlocal agreements.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.021      Rules adoption.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.026      Fees – procedure for setting –
notice – effective date – posting – approval of new fees by ordinance.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.111      Fee surcharge for taxicab
licensees, for-hire vehicle licensees and transportation network companies –
use of fee surcharge – rules adoption.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.201      Transportation network company
– license required – application dispatch system unlawful except if licensed
transportation network company or used exclusively for certain taxicabs or
for-hire vehicles.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.211      Transportation network company
– license requirements.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.221      Transportation network company
- annual application – notice of changes – expiration – lease, transfer or
assignment prohibited.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.231      Transportation network company
license not a right – denial of application or renewal.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.241      Transportation network company
- revocation or suspension.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.251      Transportation network company
– other requirements.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.261      Transportation network company
– drivers active on dispatch system must have for-hire driver's license –
required vehicles for drivers active on dispatch system.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.271      Transportation network company
vehicle endorsement – requirements of persons, vehicles.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.281      Transportation network company
vehicle endorsement – annual filing – certificate and decal – expiration –
lease, transfer or assignment prohibited.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.291      Transportation network company
vehicle endorsement – denial of application.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.295      Transportation network company
vehicle endorsement – suspension – ceasing operation and surrender of decal.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.300      Transportation network company
endorsed vehicle - vehicle endorsement required.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.360      Certificate of safety –
maintenance and service records retention – maintenance of vehicles –
certification required of vehicles previously determined to be total wrecks or
total losses – factory specifications required for rebuilt or significantly
altered vehicles – ensurance of safety compliance and maintenance by vehicle
owner – placement of vehicles out of service if determined to be immediate
safety hazards.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.500      For-hire driver's license
required.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.510      For-hire driver's license -
initial and annual application.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.520      For-hire driver's license –
investigation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.530      For-hire driver's license –
qualifications.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.540      For-hire's driver's license –
temporary permit.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.550      For-hire driver's license –
application null and void if applicant fails or neglects to complete the
application process or obtain a license.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.560      For-hire driver – certification
of being physically and mentally fit – medical examination upon appearance of
incapacitation rendering licensee unfit.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.570      For-hire driver – required
training.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.580      For-hire driver – examination.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.590      For-hire driver – driving
abstract.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.595      For-hire license – pick up
directly from director – &quot;for-hire permit&quot; display for applicant affiliated
with transportation network company - form of license – determined by director
– placement.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.600      For-hire driver license –
denial of application.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.610      For-hire driver's license –
suspension or revocation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.620      For-hire driver – additional
requirements for license issuance.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.630      For-hire driver – license
expiration.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.640      For-hire driver – operating
standards.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.650      Driver – vehicle safety
standards.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.660      Driver – conduct standards.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.665      Transportation network
company's driver – additional standards.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.680      Driver-passenger relations
standards.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.690      Driver – soliciting and
cruising standards.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.740      Director – annual report.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.760      Rates - requirements.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.780      Reports by transportation
network companies and for-hire drivers.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.790      Licensees – protection of
information that is confidential, proprietary or business secrets – procedures
for disclosure and release of materials subject to disclosure.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.800      Penalties.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.830      Notice and order of denial,
suspension, revocation of license or assessment of civil penalty.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.900      Consumer complaint hotline.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-99.0pt'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.910      Passenger complaint process.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:1.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:
-1.5in'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>CROSS REFERENCE:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Taxicab operating
agreement at airport, see K.C.C. chapters 15.48 and 15.80.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.005  Application
of chapter - resolution of conflicts with K.C.C. chapter 6.65.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  This
chapter applies to transportation network companies, transportation network
company drivers, and transportation network company endorsed vehicles.  K.C.C.
chapter 6.65 applies to taxicab associations, for-hire vehicle companies,
taxicabs, for-hire vehicles, and the drivers of those vehicles.  References to
taxicab associations, for-hire vehicle companies, taxicabs, for-hire vehicles,
and the drivers of those for-hire vehicles remain in this chapter because RCW
46.72B.190 constrains the county from amending ordinances or regulations
related to transportation network companies, transportation network company
drivers, or transportation network company endorsed vehicles after January 1,
2022.  In the event of a conflict between this chapter and K.C.C. chapter 6.65
related to taxicab associations, for-hire vehicle companies, taxicabs, for-hire
vehicles, and the drivers of for-hire vehicles, K.C.C. chapter 6.65 controls. 
(Ord. 19699 § 1, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.010  Definitions.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The
definitions in this section apply throughout this chapter unless the context
clearly requires otherwise.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A. 
&quot;Active on a transportation network company dispatch system&quot; or
&quot;active on the transportation network company dispatch system&quot;
includes, but is not limited to:  when the driver is logged onto the
transportation network company application dispatch system showing that the
driver is available to pick up passengers; when a passenger is in the vehicle;
when transportation network company dispatch records show the vehicle is
dispatched; or when the driver has accepted a dispatch and is en route to
provide transportation services to a passenger.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B. 
&quot;Application dispatch system&quot; means technology that allows consumers
to directly request dispatch of for-hire drivers for trips via the Internet
using mobile interfaces such as smartphone applications.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  &quot;Approved
mechanic &quot; means mechanic or technician who:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  Has successfully
passed the examinations of, and met the experience requirements prescribed by, the
National Institute for Automotive Service Excellence; </span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Has been
awarded a certificate in evidence of competence satisfactory to the director;
and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  Is not the
owner, lessee or driver of a taxicab, for-hire vehicle or transportation
network company endorsed vehicle.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  &quot;Director&quot;
means the director of the department of executive services or the director's
designee.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  &quot;Engage
in the business of operating a taxicab or vehicle for hire&quot; means the
pickup and transportation of any fare paying passenger from a point within the
geographical confines of unincorporated King County, whether or not the vehicle
is dispatched from a taxicab stand or office within any other municipal
corporation, and whether or not the ultimate destination or route of travel is
within the confines of unincorporated King County.  A transportation network
company is engaged in the business of operating a vehicle for hire if it
provides application dispatch services via an application dispatch system to
any transportation network company driver at any time for the transport of any
passenger for a fare from a point within unincorporated King County.  However, nothing
in this chapter shall be construed to apply to taxicabs or for-hire vehicles
licensed by any other municipal corporation and transporting passengers from a
point within the licensing municipality to a destination outside the
municipality, whether or not the ultimate destination or route traveled is
within unincorporated King County.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F. 
&quot;Fare&quot; means anything of economic value that is provided, promised or
donated primarily in exchange for services rendered.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            G.  &quot;For-hire
driver&quot; means any person in control of, operating or driving a taxicab, for-hire
vehicle or transportation network company endorsed vehicle.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            H.  &quot;For-hire
vehicle&quot; means a motor vehicle used for the transportation of passengers
for hire and not operated exclusively over a fixed and definite route, except:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  Taxicabs;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2. 
Transportation network company endorsed vehicles;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3. 
Passenger vehicles carrying passengers on a noncommercial enterprise basis;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  Vehicles
or operators expressly exempt by state law from county regulation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            I. 
&quot;For-hire vehicle company&quot; has the same meaning as &quot;for-hire
vehicle company&quot; in K.C.C. 6.65.040.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            J.  &quot;Lessee&quot;
has the same meaning as &quot;lessee&quot; in K.C.C. 6.65.040.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            K.  &quot;Licensee&quot;
means all persons, including for-hire drivers, vehicle owners, taxicab
associations and transportation network of companies required to be licensed under
this chapter.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            L. 
&quot;Medallion&quot; has the same meaning as &quot;medallion&quot; in K.C.C.
6.65.040.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            M. 
&quot;Medallion system&quot; has the same meaning as &quot;medallion
system&quot; in K.C.C. 6.65.040.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            N.  &quot;Motor
vehicle&quot; means every motorized vehicle by or upon which any person may be
transported or carried upon a public street, highway or alley, though vehicles
used exclusively upon stationary rail tracks or propelled by use of overhead
electric wires shall not come under this chapter.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            O. 
&quot;Person&quot; means any individual, partnership, association, corporation,
firm, institution or other entity, whether or not operated for profit. 
&quot;Person&quot; does not include:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  A
governmental unit of or within the United States;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  An
entity operating exclusively under contract with a government entity; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  That
portion of an entity that is operating exclusively under contract with a
government entity.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            P. 
&quot;Personal vehicle&quot; means a motor vehicle that is not a taxicab or
for-hire vehicle.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Q.  &quot;Special
rate&quot; means discounted rates for senior citizens and disabled persons.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            R.  &quot;Taxicab&quot;
has the same meaning as &quot;taxicab&quot; in K.C.C. 6.65.040.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            S. 
&quot;Taxicab association&quot; has the same meaning as &quot;taxicab
association&quot; in K.C.C. 6.65.040.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            T. 
&quot;Taxicab license&quot; has the same meaning as &quot;taxicab license&quot;
in K.C.C. 6.65.040.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            U.  &quot;Taximeter&quot;
has the same meaning as &quot;taximeter&quot; in K.C.C. 6.65.040.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            V. 
&quot;Trade dress&quot; means the unique visual element associated with a
transportation network company that is attached to a transportation network
company endorsed vehicle.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            W. 
&quot;Transportation network company&quot; means a person licensed under this
chapter that provides application dispatch services via an application dispatch
system to connect drivers with passengers for the transportation of passengers
for fares. </span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            X. 
&quot;Transportation network company driver&quot; means a licensed for-hire
driver affiliated with a licensed transportation network company in order to
provide transportation to passengers by an application dispatch system. </span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Y. 
&quot;Transportation network company endorsed vehicle&quot; means a vehicle
with a transportation network company vehicle endorsement.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Z. 
&quot;Transportation network company representative&quot; means a person who a
transportation network company has authorized to: </span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  File
applications and other documents on behalf of the company; </span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Receive
and accept all correspondence and notices from the county pertaining to the
company or its drivers.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            AA. 
&quot;Transportation network company vehicle endorsement&quot; means an
endorsement on a for-hire driver's license that allows the for-hire driver to
use the driver's personal vehicle to affiliate with a transportation network
company to provide transportation to passengers by an application dispatch
system.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            BB. 
“Wheelchair accessible taxicab” or “wheelchair accessible for-hire vehicle” or
“wheelchair accessible transportation network company endorsed vehicle” means a
taxicab, for-hire vehicle or transportation network company endorsed vehicle
designed or modified to transport passengers in wheelchairs or other mobility
devices and conforming to the requirements of the Americans with Disabilities
Act and inspected and approved by the director.  (Ord. 19699 § 3, 2023:  Ord.
18338 § 1, 2016:  Ord. 17892 § 2, 2014:  Ord. 17665 § 1, 2013:  Ord. 15263 § 1,
2005:  Ord. 14199 § 121, 2001:  Ord. 10498 § 1, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.015  Interlocal
agreements.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The executive may execute an interlocal agreement with either
the city of Seattle or the Port of Seattle, or both, for the purposes of
coordinating and consolidating for-hire driver administration and enforcement,
reducing duplication of licensing functions and a sharing of license fees as
agreed to by the city and county.  (Ord. 19699 § 4, 2023:  Ord. 17892 § 3,
2014:  Ord. 17665 § 2, 2013:  Ord. 10498 § 5, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            <b>6.64.021 
Rules adoption.</b>  The director is authorized to adopt rules under the
procedures specified in K.C.C. chapter 2.98 for the purpose of implementing
this chapter.  (Ord. 17892 § 4, 2014).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=DE>            6.64.026
 </span></b><b>Fees – procedure for setting – notice – effective date – posting
– approval of new fees by ordinance.*</b></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            A.  The
director shall set fees in K.C.C. 4A.750.100, in accordance with this section.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            B.  The
director shall make available to the public a description of the director's
procedures for setting fees.  The description shall include information on how
to inquire about the director's proposed and adopted fees and public comment
opportunities.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            C.1.  The
director shall give at least twenty days' notice of the director's intention to
set fees by providing notice:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                a.  in
writing or by electronic format, to:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                  (1) 
the clerk of the council;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                  (2) 
all council members; </span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                  (3) 
all persons who have made a timely request for advance notice of fee setting;
and</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                  (4) 
all existing fee payers; and</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                b.  by
publishing in the official county newspaper a summary of the notice of the
proposed action, including the information in subsection C.2. a. through e. of
this section.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              2.  The
notice made in subsection C.1. of this section shall:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                  a. 
include a reference to this section;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                  b. 
include a reference to the fee type to which the fee will be applied;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                  c. 
include a date and place by which comments must be submitted;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                  d. 
specify whether the proposal is a change or an elimination of a fee;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                  e. 
if the proposal is to change a fee, indicate both the amount of the existing
fee and the proposed fee; and</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                  f. 
state the reason for and methodology used to determine the proposed new fee.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              3.  The
director shall consider all comments received by the prescribed date for
comment before the fee is set.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            D.  A fee
is set when signed by the director.  A fee takes effect ten<i> </i>days after
it is set.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            E.  Once a
fee is set, the director shall post the amount of the fee in both written and
electronic form for inspection, review and copying by the public, including
providing a copy, in writing or by electronic format, of the fee to the clerk
of the county council and each member of the county council and posting the fee
on the Internet.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            F.  A new
fee may not be established unless the fee is approved by the council by
ordinance.  (Ord. 17892 § 5, 2014).</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>*Reviser's note:  The dollar amounts of the
fees are set under K.C.C. 4A.750.100.  In accordance with K.C.C. 4A.750.100.B.,
the director of the department of executive services has adjusted the dollar
amounts for the fees listed in K.C.C. 4A.75.100.A.  The current fee amounts may
be obtained through the records and licensing services division (RALS) of the
department of executive services, and may be found at the web site
https://www.kingcounty.gov/depts/records-licensing/licensing/taxi-for-hire-transportation-networks/notices-regulations.aspx</span></b></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><u><span lang=DE><span
 style='text-decoration:none'>&nbsp;</span></span></u></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=DE>            6.64.111 
</span></b><b>Fee surcharge for taxicab licensees, for-hire vehicle licensees
and transportation network companies – use of fee surcharge – adoption of rules.</b></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            A.  Each
taxicab licensee, for-hire vehicle licensee or transportation network company
shall pay a fee surcharge of the amount in K.C.C. 4A.750.100.C. and D. for all
rides originating in:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              1. 
Unincorporated King County; or</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              2.  Any
municipality that contracts with the county for the county to license taxicabs,
for-hire vehicles or transportation network companies that operate in the
municipality.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            B.  The
fee surcharge in subsection A. of this section shall be used to offset the
operational costs incurred by owners and operators of wheelchair accessible
taxi, wheelchair accessible for-hire vehicle or wheelchair accessible
transportation network company endorsed vehicle services including, but not
limited to, the costs associated with purchasing and retrofitting an accessible
vehicle, fuel and maintenance costs and the time involved in providing
wheelchair accessible trips.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            C.  The
director shall adopt rules to establish the conditions and procedure for
distributing funds to wheelchair accessible taxicab, wheelchair accessible
for-hire vehicle or wheelchair accessible transportation network company
endorsed vehicle owners and drivers, including the maximum amount of
reimbursement.  (Ord. 17892 § 10, 2014).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=DE>            6.64.201 
</span></b><b>Transportation network company – license required – application
dispatch system unlawful except if licensed transportation network company or
used exclusively for certain taxicabs or for-hire vehicles.</b></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            A.  It is
unlawful for a person to operate as a transportation network company without
first having obtained a transportation network company license under this
chapter.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            B.  It is
unlawful for a person to operate an application dispatch system unless:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              1.  The
person is a licensed transportation network company; or</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              2.  The
person uses the application dispatch system exclusively for taxicabs or
for-hire vehicles consistent with K.C.C. 6.64.760.  (Ord. 17892 § 19, 2014).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=DE>            6.64.211
</span></b><b>Transportation network company – license requirements.</b>  <span
lang=DE>    The director shall not issue a transportation network company
license unless the person meets the following requirements:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            A. 
Requires that drivers who affiliate with the company:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              1. 
Possess a for-hire driver's license; and</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              2.  When
active on the company's dispatch system, operate a vehicle that is a taxicab,
for-hire vehicle or transportation network company endorsed vehicle; and</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            B.  Files
with the director on behalf of the registered owners of endorsed vehicles, or
ensures that the registered owners have filed, an insurance policy, and any
related driver contracts if applicable, demonstrating that each endorsed
vehicle has insurance that complies with state insurance requirements effective
at that time.  The transportation network company shall provide evidence that
each vehicle affiliated with a transportation network company has insurance in
an amount no less than required by RCW 46.72.050 and minimum underinsured
motorist coverage of one hundred thousand dollars per person and three hundred
thousand dollars per accident or in an amount no less than required by RCW 46.72B.180,
at any time while active on the transportation network company dispatch system. 
The insurance policy shall:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              1.  Be
issued by an admitted carrier in the state of Washington with an A.M. Best
Rating of not less than B VII, or show evidence that an exemption has been met
allowing for the use of a surplus line insurer with an A.M. Best Rating of not
less than B+ VII.  However, the director may temporarily suspend any or all of
these requirements if no other viable insurance options are available to the
industry;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              2.  Name
King County, its officers, officials, agents and employees as an additional
insured on the insurance policy;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              3.  Provide
that the insurer will notify the director in writing of any cancellation or
nonrenewal at least thirty days before cancellation or nonrenewal of the
policy; and</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              4.  Not
include aggregate limits, or named driver requirements or exclusions.  Other
limitations or restrictions beyond standard insurance services office business
auto policy form are subject to approval by the director.  (Ord. 19699 § 5,
2023:  Ord. 18338 <span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span> 2, 2016:  Ord.
17892 § 20, 2014).</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=DE>            6.64.221 
</span></b><b>Transportation network company - annual application – notice of
changes – expiration – lease, transfer or assignment prohibited.</b></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            A.  A
person desiring to operate as a transportation network company shall file
annually with the director a signed transportation network company license
application on a form provided by the director.  The application shall include
the following:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              1.  The
applicant's:  name, business street address and post office box address,
business telephone number and business email address at which the
transportation network company representative can generally be reached between
9 a.m. and 5 p.m. on all nonholiday weekdays;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              2.  The
form of business entity under which the applicant will operate;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                a.  if
the applicant is an individual:  the information in subsection A.1. of this
section if not already provided and the date of birth of the owner; or</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                b.  if
the applicant is a corporation, partnership or other business entity:  the
names, home and business addresses, telephone numbers and of all officers,
directors, general and managing partners, registered agents, the company
representative and all other persons vested with authority to manage or direct
the affairs of the entity or to bind the entity in dealings with third parties;
the entity's legal name and state of incorporation; registration, if any, with
the Secretary of State of the state of Washington; and state of Washington
business license number;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              3.  The
trade dress, if any, the applicant intends to use for each endorsed vehicle,
with a photo of the trade dress;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              4. 
Evidence of the insurance required by K.C.C. 6.64.211;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              5. 
Documentation of the company's application dispatch rate structure as required
by K.C.C. 6.64.760.C.; and</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              6. 
Other information as the director may reasonably require.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            B.  The
applicant shall inform the director in writing within seven days if there is
any change to the information provided under subsection A. of this section.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            C.  A
transportation network company license is valid for not more than one year.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            D.  A
transportation network company license shall not be leased, transferred or
assigned.  (Ord. 17892 § 21, 2014).</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=DE>            6.64.231 
</span></b><b>Transportation network company license not a right – denial of
application or renewal.</b></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            A.  The
transportation network company's ability to satisfy stated criteria for a
transportation network license does not create a right to a license.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            B.  The
director shall deny any company license application if the director determines
that:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              1.  The
applicant provides access to its application dispatch system to drivers who do
not meet the requirements in K.C.C. 6.64.211.A.;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              2.  The
applicant fails to submit evidence of the insurance required by K.C.C. 6.64.211;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              3.  The
application is incomplete or has a misstatement or omission of material fact;
or</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              4.  The
rate structure is not transparent as required by K.C.C. 6.64.760.C.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            C.  The
director may deny an annual application for license renewal if the applicant:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              1.  Has
failed to pay all outstanding penalties assessed against the company;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              2.  Has
failed within five years of the date of application to meet any of the
requirements in K.C.C. 6.64.251.  (Ord. 17892 § 22, 2014).</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><u><span lang=DE><span
 style='text-decoration:none'>&nbsp;</span></span></u></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=DE>            6.64.241 
</span></b><b>Transportation network company - revocation or suspension.  </b><span
lang=DE>The director may revoke or suspend a transportation network company
license if during the license period the transportation network company fails
to meet any of the requirements in K.C.C. 6.64.251.  In determining whether to
suspend or revoke the license, the director shall consider the gravity of the
association's noncompliance and whether suspension is appropriate to allow the
company time to correct the noncompliance.  (Ord. 17892 § 23, 2014).</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><u><span lang=DE><span
 style='text-decoration:none'>&nbsp;</span></span></u></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=DE>            6.64.251 
</span></b><b>Transportation network company – other requirements.  </b><span
lang=DE>In addition to meeting the license application requirements in K.C.C.
6.64.211, a transportation network company shall:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            A. 
Maintain a mailing address and email address where the company's representative
will accept mail;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            B.  When
required by the director, forward correspondence from the director to a driver
within five business days after receiving the correspondence by first class
mail or email and keep a record of the mailings;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            C.  Retain
company records, including:  copies of drivers' for-hire drivers licenses;
copies of drivers' vehicle endorsements; copies of for-hire vehicle licenses or
taxicab licenses; vehicle insurance policies; passenger complaints; and
dispatch records.  Records may be maintained electronically;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            D. 
Collect, retain and report the information required under K.C.C. 6.64.780;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            E.  Permit
the director to carry out inspections with reasonable notice of all records
required to be kept under this chapter;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            F. 
Provide secure storage for all items left in a company's driver's vehicle by a
passenger and turned in by the driver;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            G. 
Require that a passenger be able to view a picture of the driver and vehicle
license plate number on the passenger's smart phone, tablet or other mobile
device used to connect with the company's dispatch application before the trip
is initiated;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            H. 
Maintain a nondiscrimination policy that complies fully with all applicable
federal, state and local laws that prohibit discrimination;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            I.  Allow
any passenger to indicate the need for a wheelchair accessible vehicle and
connect the passenger to an accessible vehicle service via an internet link,
application or telephone number;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            J.  Notify
the director within two working days of having knowledge of the following:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              1.  A
conviction or bail forfeiture received by any of the company's drivers for any
criminal offense or traffic violation that occurs during or arises out of the
driver's operation of a vehicle while active on the company's dispatch system;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              2.  A
conviction or bail forfeiture received by any of the company's drivers for any
criminal offense reasonably related to the driver's honesty and integrity or
ability to operate a vehicle in a safe manner;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              3.  A
vehicle accident required by law to be reported to a state agency that involves
any of the company's drivers; and</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              4.  A
restriction, suspension or revocation of a valid driver's license issued to any
of the company's drivers;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            K. 
Terminate a driver's access to the company's dispatch system immediately upon:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              1. 
Receiving notification from the director that the driver does not meet the
requirements of K.C.C. 6.64.211.A.; or</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              2. 
Having knowledge that a driver meets the criteria for the driver's license to
be immediately suspended under K.C.C. 6.64.610;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            L. 
Maintain a policy that prohibits the company's drivers while active on the
company's dispatch system from being under the influence of any alcohol,
narcotics, drugs, or prescription or over-the-counter medication that might
impair their performance or in any way jeopardize the safety or security of
passengers or the public.  Provide notice of the policy on the company's
website, mobile application and passenger trip confirmations and include in the
notice a telephone number, web site link and email address for a passenger to
report to the company a driver who the passenger suspects was in violation of
the policy during a trip;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            M. 
Maintain the rate structure documented with the application or file with the
director for approval the documentation required by K.C.C. 6.64.760.C.;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            N. 
Require the company's drivers to comply with K.C.C. 6.64.665.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            O. 
Provide a written insurance disclosure to the company's drivers that includes
the following language: &quot;[insert name of company] confirms that while
driver [insert driver's full name] is active on the application dispatch
system, the driver's vehicle is insured as required by K.C.C. chapter
6.64&quot;; and</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            P.  Pay
all penalties assessed against the company.  (Ord. 19699 § 6, 2023:  Ord. 17892
§ 24, 2014).</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><u><span lang=DE><span
 style='text-decoration:none'>&nbsp;</span></span></u></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=DE>            6.64.261 
</span></b><b>Transportation network company – drivers active on dispatch
system must have for-hire driver's license – required vehicles for drivers
active on dispatch system.</b></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            A.  It is
unlawful for a driver to be active on a transportation network company's
dispatch system without a for-hire driver's license.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            B.  It is
unlawful for a driver while active on a transportation network company's
dispatch system to operate a vehicle other than a taxicab, for-hire vehicle or
transportation network company endorsed vehicle.  (Ord. 17892 § 25, 2014).</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><u><span lang=DE><span
 style='text-decoration:none'>&nbsp;</span></span></u></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=DE>            6.64.271 
</span></b><b>Transportation network company vehicle endorsement – requirements
of persons, vehicles.</b></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            A.  The
director shall not issue a transportation network company vehicle endorsement
unless the person meets the following requirements:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              1.  Has
a for-hire driver's permit, as described in K.C.C. 6.64.595.B., or a transportation
network company license under this chapter; and</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              2.  Is
affiliated with a licensed transportation network company.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            B.  The
director shall not issue a transportation network company vehicle endorsement
unless the vehicle meets the following requirements:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              1.  Has
insurance that complies with K.C.C. 6.64.211 and state law;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              2.  Has
a certificate of safety as required by K.C.C. 6.64.360; and</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              3.  The
vehicle's model year is no more than fifteen years old.  (Ord. 19699 § 7,
2023:  Ord. 18874 § 1, 2019:  Ord. 17892 § 26, 2014).</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><u><span lang=DE><span
 style='text-decoration:none'>&nbsp;</span></span></u></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=DE>            6.64.281 
</span></b><b>Transportation network company vehicle endorsement – annual
filing – certificate and decal – expiration – lease, transfer or assignment
prohibited.</b></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            A.  An
applicant for a transportation network company vehicle endorsement, or a
transportation network company on behalf of the applicant, shall file annually
with the director a signed application on a form provided by the director to
include the following information about the applicant:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              1. 
Name, aliases, residence or business address and residence and business
telephone numbers;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              2.  If
the applicant is an individual, the date of birth, which shall be at least twenty
years before the date of application, height, weight, and color of eyes;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              3.  If
the applicant is an individual, a valid driver's license number.  The applicant
shall present the applicant's valid driver's license or a copy at the time of
application;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              4.  If
the applicant is an individual, evidence of a for-hire driver's license or
permit, or an approved application for a for-hire driver's license or permit;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              5. 
Vehicle information including vehicle identification number or numbers and valid
license plate number or numbers;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              6. 
Evidence of vehicle insurance as required in K.C.C. 6.64.211;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              7. 
Vehicle certificate of safety required by K.C.C. 6.64.360;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              8. 
Whether any of the circumstances in K.C.C. 6.64.291.B. apply to the applicant;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              9. 
Evidence that the applicant is affiliated with a transportation network
company; and</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              10. 
Other information as reasonably determined by the director.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            B.  The
transportation network company vehicle endorsement consists of a certificate and
an endorsement decal affixed to the vehicle.  The certificate shall include the
following:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              1. 
Vehicle identification number;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              2. 
Vehicle registered owner's full legal name;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              3. 
Vehicle license plate number;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              4. 
Endorsement expiration date;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              5. 
Unique number; and</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              6. 
Other information the director may reasonably require.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            C.  A
transportation network company vehicle endorsement is valid for not more than
one year.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            D.  A
person shall not lease, transfer or assign a transportation network company
vehicle endorsement.  (Ord. 19699 § 8, 2023:  Ord. 18874 § 2, 2019:  Ord. 17892
§ 27, 2014).</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><u><span lang=DE><span
 style='text-decoration:none'>&nbsp;</span></span></u></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=DE>            6.64.291 
</span></b><b>Transportation network company vehicle endorsement – denial of
application.</b></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            A.  The
director shall deny any transportation network company vehicle endorsement
application if the director determines that:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              1.  The
applicant has failed to affiliate with a licensed transportation network
company;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              2.  The
applicant fails to meet one or more of the applicant or vehicle requirements
under K.C.C. 6.64.271.A. or B.; or</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              3.  The
application is incomplete or has a misstatement or omission of material fact.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            B.  The
director may deny any transportation network company vehicle endorsement
application if the director determines that any one or more of the following
apply:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              1. 
Within two years of the date of application, the applicant has engaged in the
business of operating in unincorporated King County a taxicab or for-hire
vehicle for which a license is required while unlicensed or while such license
was suspended or revoked;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              2. 
Within twelve months of the date of application, the applicant has violated any
city of Seattle, Port of Seattle or King County ordinance or regulation
pertaining to the operation of licensed taxicabs or licensed for-hire vehicles
while in those jurisdictions, if such a violation would constitute grounds for
license revocation or denial if occurring within King County; and</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              3. 
Within twelve months of the date of application, the applicant has its King
County taxicab or for-hire vehicle license revoked.  (Ord. 17892 § 28, 2014).</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><u><span lang=DE><span
 style='text-decoration:none'>&nbsp;</span></span></u></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=DE>            6.64.295 
</span></b><b>Transportation network company vehicle endorsement – suspension –
ceasing operation and surrender of decal.</b></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            A.  A
transportation network company endorsement shall be immediately suspended if:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              1.  At
any time the insurance required by K.C.C. 6.64.211 expires, lapses or is
cancelled or revoked; or</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              2.  The
director places the vehicle out-of-service for a violation of a vehicle
standard that is found to be an immediate safety hazard and immediate
suspension is necessary to prevent a clear, substantial and imminent hazard to
life, safety or property.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            B.  When
an endorsement has been suspended under subsection A. of this section, the
operation of the vehicle on a transportation network company dispatch system
must cease and the endorsement decal surrendered immediately to the director. 
(Ord. 17892 § 29, 2014).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.300  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Transportation network
company endorsed vehicle - vehicle endorsement required. <span
style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'> </span></span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>It is unlawful to own or
operate, advertise or engage in the business of operating a transportation
network company endorsed vehicle [in unincorporated King County]* without first
having obtained, for each and every vehicle so used, a transportation network
company vehicle endorsement issued under K.C.C. 6.64.281.  (Ord. 19699 § 9,
2023:  Ord. 17892 § 30, 2014:  Ord. 10498 § 10, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Reviser's note:  Not
included in Ordinance 17892 and Ordinance 19699, but not deleted as required in
K.C.C. 1.24.075.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.360  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Certificate of safety –
maintenance and service records retention – maintenance of vehicles –
certification required of vehicles previously determined to be total wrecks or
total losses – factory specifications required for rebuilt or significantly
altered vehicles – ensurance of safety compliance and maintenance by vehicle
owner – placement of vehicles out of service if determined to be immediate
safety hazards.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The
certificate of safety required by K.C.C. 6.64.271 shall be provided by an
approved mechanic and shall certify that the following items are mechanically
sound and fit for driving:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  Foot
brakes;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2. 
Emergency brakes;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  Steering
mechanism;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4. 
Windshield;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              5.  Rear
window and other glass;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              6. 
Windshield wipers;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              7. 
Headlights;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              8.  Tail
lights;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              9.  Turn
indicator lights;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              10.  Stop
lights;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              11.  Front
seat adjustment mechanism;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              12.  Doors,
including that doors properly open, close and lock;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              13.  Horn;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              14. 
Speedometer;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              15. 
Bumpers;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              16.  Muffler
and exhaust system;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              17. 
Condition of tires, including tread depth;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              18. 
Interior and exterior rear view mirrors;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              19.  Safety
belts and air bags for driver and a passenger or passengers; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              20.  Other
items reasonably required by the director.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The
vehicle owner shall keep all maintenance and service records for all vehicles
for three years.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  Vehicles
shall be maintained following the service standards recommended by the vehicle
manufacturer.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  A vehicle
that has been in a collision and determined by the insurance adjuster to be a
total wreck or total loss shall not be placed back in service until an approved
mechanic with a current certification in structural analysis and damage repair
has verified that there is no damage to the vehicle frame.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  A vehicle
shall not be rebuilt or significantly modified from factory specifications.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F.  Each
vehicle owner shall ensure that the safety standards, conditions and
requirements in this section are met and continually maintained.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            G.  The
director shall place a vehicle out of service if the director determines that a
violation of this section is an immediate safety hazard and immediate
suspension is necessary to prevent a clear, substantial and imminent hazard to
life, safety or property.  (Ord. 19699 § 10, 2023:  Ord. 17892 § 36, 2014: 
Ord. 17665 § 5, 2013:  10498 § 16, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.500 
For-hire driver's license required.  </span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>It is unlawful for any
person to drive, be in control of, or operate a transportation network company
endorsed vehicle in the unincorporated areas of King County without first
having obtained a valid for-hire driver's license.  K.C.C. 6.64.510 through K.C.C.
6.64.690 apply to drivers of endorsed vehicles unless the context clearly
requires otherwise.  (Ord. 19699 § 11, 2023:  Ord. 17892 § 46, 2014:  Ord.
17665 § 15, 2013:  Ord. 10498 § 27, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.510  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>For-hire driver's
license - initial and annual application.</span></b><span style='font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  For an initial
for-hire driver's license and annually thereafter, the applicant, or
transportation network company on behalf of the applicant, shall file a signed application
on a form approved by the director.  The application may be filed online, by
email, by United States mail or in person,  The application shall include the
following:  name; height; weight; and eyes; residence address; place and date
of birth; social security number; driver's license number; aliases; consent to
a background check or a copy of a background check as required by K.C.C.
6.64.520; whether the applicant has ever had a license suspended, revoked or
denied and for what cause; the information required in K.C.C. 6.64.530 and
6.64.590; and any other information as the director may reasonably require.  (Ord.
19699 § 12, 2023:  Ord. 17892 § 47, 2014:  Ord. 17665 § 16, 2013:  Ord. 10498 §
28, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.520  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>For-hire driver's
license – investigation.  </span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>All applicants for a for-hire driver's
license shall:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Be
referred for fingerprinting, and all applications shall be referred for a state
and federal background investigation under RCW 36.01.300 to regulate the
issuance of licenses of those engaged in the taxicab and for-hire occupations
and activities; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  Have a
copy of a criminal background check provided directly from a third party
approved by the director.  The director shall annually issue the list of third
parties that are approved to conduct background checks.  Approved third parties
shall at a minimum:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  Include
local, state and national databases;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Access
at least five years of database history; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3. 
Demonstrate competency in providing accurate information.  (Ord. 17892 § 48,
2014:  Ord. 17665 § 17, 2013:  Ord. 10680 § 1, 1992:  Ord. 10498 § 29, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.530  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>For-hire driver's
license – qualifications<span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>.</span></span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The
director shall not issue a for-hire driver's license to a person unless the following
requirements about the person are met:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Must be twenty
years old or older;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  Must
possess a valid driver's license;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  Must
submit a certificate of fitness;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  Must have
completed the training program required by K.C.C. 6.64.570; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  Must
successfully complete the examination required by K.C.C. 6.64.580.  (Ord. 19699
§ 13, 2023:  Ord. 17892 § 49, 2014:  Ord. 17665 § 18, 2013: Ord. 10498 § 30,
1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.540  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>For-hire's driver's
license – temporary permit.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Pending
final action on a for-hire driver's license application, the director shall
issue a temporary permit within two business days to an applicant who has:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  Filed a
complete application as required by K.C.C. 6.64.510 that has been reviewed
under K.C.C. 6.64.600; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Passed
the examination required by K.C.C. 6.64.580.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The
temporary permit is valid for a period not to exceed sixty days from the date
of the application.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  The
temporary permit shall not be transferable or assignable.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  The
temporary permit shall be immediately null and void if at any time the
applicant's valid driver's license is no longer valid, or following the denial
of an application.  (Ord. 19699 § 14, 2023:  Ord. 17892 § 50, 2014:  Ord. 15263
§ 6, 2005:  Ord. 10498 § 31, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.550  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>For-hire driver's
license – application null and void if applicant fails or neglects to complete
the application process or obtain a license.<span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
</span></span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>An application for a for-hire driver's license shall
become null and void after sixty days from the date of filing if the applicant,
for any reason, fails or neglects to complete the application process or obtain
a license. (Ord. 17892 § 51, 2014:  Ord. 10498 § 32, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.560  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>For-hire driver –
certification of being physically and mentally fit – medical examination upon
appearance of incapacitation rendering licensee unfit.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The
applicant shall certify on a form prescribed by the director that the applicant
is physically and mentally fit to be a for-hire driver.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The
director may at any time require any for-hire licensee or applicant to be
medically examined if it appears that the licensee has become physically or
mentally incapacitated to such a degree as to render the applicant or licensee
unfit for a for-hire driver.  The examination shall be performed by a physician
licensed to practice in the state of Washington.  The director shall prescribe
the scope of the examination and provide a certificate form for the physician
to complete.  (Ord. 17892 § 52, 2014:  Ord. 10498 § 33, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.570  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>For-hire driver –
required training.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  An initial
for-hire driver applicant is required to complete:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  Before
filling an application, a training program providing information about defensive
driving, use of emergency procedures and equipment for the driver’s personal
safety, risk factors for crimes against for-hire drivers, enhancement of driver
and passenger relations, professional conduct and communication skills; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Before
the end of the temporary permit period under K.C.C. 6.64.540, the National
Safety Council Defensive Driving Course. </span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  A
currently licensed for-hire driver shall satisfy the requirements of subsection
A. of this section if:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  A
transportation network company with which the driver is affiliated requests
that the driver receive a refresher course; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  The
director has reasonable grounds, based on documented complaints or violations,
to believe that a refresher course is necessary.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  The
director shall assure that this training is offered by the county or offered by
another public or private entity, or offered by both.  The director shall
annually approve the content and testing process for training offered by a noncounty
entity.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  A for-hire
driver who operates a wheelchair accessible taxicab must successfully complete
a separate training program for the special needs of passengers in wheelchairs
including, but not limited to, loading and tie-down procedures and door-to-door
service.  (Ord. 19699 § 15, 2023:  Ord. 17892 § 53, 2014:  Ord. 15263 § 7,
2005:  Ord. 10498 § 34, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.580  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>For-hire driver –
examination.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  An
applicant for an initial for-hire driver's license shall be required to
successfully complete an examination.  </span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The
examination shall test the applicant's knowledge of the requirements dealing
with fare determination, driver-passenger relations, conduct including the
applicant's ability to understand oral and written directions in the English
language, vehicle safety requirements, transportation network company vehicle
endorsement and driver regulations, risk factors for crimes against for-hire
drivers, emergency procedures and equipment for driver’s personal safety.  The
examination shall also test the applicant’s geographical knowledge of King
County and surrounding areas and local public and tourist destinations and
attractions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  The
examination is not required for the renewal of a for-hire driver's license
unless the applicant's license has remained expired for more than one year.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  The
director shall assure that these examinations are offered by the county or
offered by another public or private entity, or offered by both.  The director
shall annually approve the content and procedures for examinations offered by a
noncounty entity.  (Ord. 19699 § 16, 2023:  Ord. 17892 § 54, 2014:  Ord. 17665
§ 19, 2013:  Ord. 15263 § 8, 2005:  Ord. 10498 § 35, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.590  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>For-hire driver –
driving abstract.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>
<span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'> Each applicant for a for-hire driver's
license shall provide a current copy, or authorize the director to obtain a
current copy, of the applicant's driving abstract from the Washington state
Department of Licensing.  (Ord. 17892 § 55, 2014:  Ord. 10498 § 36, 1992).</span></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.595  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>For-hire license – pick
up directly from director – &quot;for-hire permit&quot; display for applicant
affiliated with transportation network company - form of license – determined
by director – placement.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  A for-hire
license that has been approved from an application filed online, by email or by
United States mail shall be picked up directly from the director, and the
applicant shall show photo identification.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The
for-hire driver's license shall be in a form as determined by the director. 
When issued to an applicant who is affiliated with a transportation network
company, the license shall display &quot;for-hire permit.&quot;  A copy shall
be placed inside each transportation network company endorsed vehicle so that
the license is clearly visible from the passenger compartment at all times that
the licensee is operating, driving or using the vehicle.  (Ord. 19699 § 17,
2023:  Ord. 17892 § 56, 2014:  Ord. 17665 § 20, 2013).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.600  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>For-hire driver license
– denial of application<span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>.</span></span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The
director shall deny any initial or renewal application for a for-hire driver
license if the director determines that the applicant:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  Has made
a misstatement or omission of material fact in the application;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Fails to
meet any of the qualifications of a for-hire driver;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  Has had,
within five years of the date of application, a criminal conviction or a bail
forfeiture for a crime pertaining to hit-and-run, reckless driving, attempting
to elude an officer by using a vehicle, vehicular assault, vehicular homicide,
reckless endangerment or driving under the influence of alcohol or a controlled
substance, or has been found to be a habitual traffic offender;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  Is
required to register as a sex offender; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              5.  Has been
convicted of a sex offense or kidnapping offense against a minor.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The
director may deny any for-hire driver license application if the director
determines that the applicant:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  Has had,
within five years of the date of application, a criminal conviction or a bail
forfeiture involving a crime pertaining to prostitution, gambling, physical
violence or other crimes reasonably related to the applicant's honesty and
integrity, including, but not limited to, fraud, larceny, burglary or extortion
or reasonably related to the person’s ability to operate as a for-hire driver;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Has been
found through a criminal conviction, bail forfeiture, judgment in a civil suit
or decision in an administrative proceeding, or has been proven by a
preponderance of the evidence regardless of whether the same act was charged as
a civil infraction or a crime, to have exhibited past conduct in driving or
operating as a for-hire driver that would lead the director to reasonably
conclude that the applicant will not comply with the provisions of the chapter
related to driver and operator conduct and the safe operation of the vehicle;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3. Has been
found through a criminal conviction, bail forfeiture, judgment in a civil suit
or decision in an administrative proceeding, or has been proven by a
preponderance of the evidence regardless of whether the same act was charged as
a civil infraction or a crime, to have exhibited a past driving or criminal record
that would lead the director to reasonably conclude that the applicant would
not operate a vehicle in a safe manner; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  Has a
felony conviction or bail forfeiture related to a felony under the laws of
Washington, another state or under federal law.  (Ord. 17892 § 57, 2014:  Ord.
17665 § 21, 2013:  Ord. 13984 § 1, 2000:  Ord. 10498 § 37, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.610  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>For-hire driver's
license – suspension or revocation.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  A for-hire
driver's license shall be immediately suspended and is null and void if:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  At any
time the driver no longer possesses a valid driver's license;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  The
director obtains information after license issuance that the driver fails to
meet the qualifications of a for-hire driver; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  The
driver is found to be in possession of controlled substances or alcohol while
in control of or while operating a vehicle as a for-hire driver;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The
director may suspend or revoke a for-hire driver's license if the director
determines that the licensee has:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  Received
a conviction or bail forfeiture for a crime that would be grounds for denial as
set forth in K.C.C. 6.64.600;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Failed
to comply with the driver standards as set forth in this chapter; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  A
driving record that leads the director to reasonably conclude that the
applicant would not operate a vehicle in a safe manner.  (Ord. 19699 § 18,
2023:  Ord. 17892 § 58, 2014:  Ord. 17665 § 22, 2013:  Ord. 10498 § 38, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.620  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>For-hire driver –
additional requirements for license issuance.</span></b><span style='font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  In addition to
the application requirements in this chapter, the director may obtain other
information concerning the applicant's character, integrity, personal habits,
past conduct and general qualifications that shows the applicant's ability and
skill as a for-hire driver and the applicant's honesty, integrity and character
for the purposes of determining whether the applicant is a suitable person to
drive as a for-hire driver.  If the director is satisfied that the applicant
possesses the qualifications and is a suitable person to drive as a for-hire
driver under this chapter, the director shall issue the applicant a for-hire
driver's license.  (Ord. 17892 § 59, 2014:  Ord. 10498 § 39, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.630  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>For-hire driver –
license expiration<span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>.</span></span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  A
for-hire driver's license shall expire one year from the date of application. 
A licensee shall secure a renewal of the license no later than one month before
the license expiration date.  (Ord. 17892 § 60, 2014:  Ord. 10498 § 40, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.640  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>For-hire driver –
operating standards.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  A driver shall not operate a vehicle in violation of
any of the for-hire driver standards in this chapter.  (Ord. 17892 § 61, 2014: 
Ord. 10498 § 41, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.650  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Driver – vehicle safety
standards.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  A driver,
before starting each shift, shall check the lights, brakes, tires, steering,
seat belts, and other vehicle equipment to see that they are working properly. 
The driver shall also ensure that the transportation network company vehicle
endorsement certificate, vehicle registration and proof of insurance card are
in the vehicle.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  A driver
shall maintain the interior and the exterior of the vehicle in a clean condition
and good repair.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  A driver
shall neither transport more passengers than the number of seat belts available
nor more luggage than the vehicle capacity will safely and legally allow.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  A driver
shall not drive, be in control of or operate a vehicle that does not meet the
applicable vehicle standards as set forth in this chapter.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  A driver
shall allow the director to inspect the vehicle at any reasonable time or
place.  (Ord. 19699 § 19, 2023:  Ord. 17892 § 62, 2014:  Ord. 10498 §§ 42-46,
1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.660  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Driver – conduct
standards.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  A driver
shall not operate a vehicle under the influence of any alcohol, narcotics,
drugs, or prescription or over-the-counter medication that might impair the
driver's performance or in any way jeopardize the safety or security of
passengers or the public.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  A driver
shall, at the end of each trip, check the driver's vehicle for any article that
is left behind by any passenger.  The articles must be reported as found
property on the hotline number, as well as to the transportation network
company, and the articles are to be returned to the transportation network
company at the end of the shift or sooner.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  A driver
shall have in the driver's possession and posted as required in K.C.C. 6.64.595
a valid for-hire driver's license at any time the driver is driving, in control
of or operating a vehicle and the license shall be displayed as prescribed by
the director.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  A driver
shall comply with any written notice and order by the director.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  A driver
shall not operate a vehicle when the vehicle has been placed out-of-service by
order of the director.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F.  A driver
shall immediately surrender the vehicle license plate or decal to the director
upon written notice that the vehicle is out-of-service.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            G.  A driver
shall not be in control of a vehicle for more than fourteen consecutive hours
in any twenty-four-hour period.  Thereafter, the driver shall not drive a
vehicle until eight consecutive hours have elapsed.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            H.  A driver
shall operate the vehicle with due regard for the safety, comfort and
convenience of passengers.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            I.  A driver
shall neither solicit for prostitution nor allow the vehicle to be used for prostitution.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            J.  A driver
shall not knowingly allow the vehicle to be used for the illegal solicitation,
transportation, sale or any other activity related to controlled substances.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            K.  A driver
shall deposit all refuse appropriately and under no circumstances may litter.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            L.  A driver
shall not use offensive language, expressions or gestures to any person while
the driver is driving, operating or in control of a vehicle.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            M.  A driver
shall not operate a wheelchair accessible taxicab unless the driver has
successfully completed the special training requirements in K.C.C. 6.64.570.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            N.  A driver
shall not use a mobile phone unless in hands-free mode, consistent with RCW
46.61.667.  (Ord. 19699 § 20, 2023:  Ord. 17892 § 63, 2014:  Ord. 17665 § 23,
2013:  Ord. 15971 § 48, 2007:  Ord. 15263 § 9, 2005: Ord. 10498 §§ 47 - 60,
1992).</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=DE>&nbsp;</span></b></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=DE>            6.64.665 
</span></b><b>Transportation network company's driver – additional standards.</b></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            In
addition to meeting the for-hire driver standards in this chapter, a
transportation network company's driver shall meet the following standards:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            A.  When
active on a transportation network company's application dispatch system, shall
drive only the vehicle for which the driver has an endorsement; and</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            B.  When
driving an endorsed vehicle, shall only provide rides to fare-paying passengers
that are booked through a transportation network company's application dispatch
system.  (Ord. 17892 § 64, 2014).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.680  Driver-passenger
relations standards.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  When
wearing a costume a driver shall display a photograph of the driver dressed in
the costume along with the driver's for-hire license.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  A driver
shall provide a customer with professional and courteous service at all times.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  A driver
shall at all times assist a passenger by placing luggage or packages that are under
fifty pounds in and out of the vehicle.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  A driver
shall not refuse to transport in the vehicle:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  Any
passenger's wheelchair that can be folded and placed in either the passenger,
driver or trunk compartment of the vehicle;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  An
assist dog or guide dog to assist the disabled or handicapped; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  Groceries,
packages or luggage when accompanied by a passenger.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E.  A driver
shall provide each passenger an electronic or paper receipt upon payment of the
fare.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F.  A driver
shall use the most direct available route on all trips unless the passenger
specifically requests to change the route.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            G.  A driver
shall not smoke in the vehicle.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            H.  If
operating a wheelchair accessible transportation network company endorsed
vehicle, a driver shall provide priority service to private pay passengers in
wheelchairs or other mobility devices.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            I.  A driver
must be clean and neat in dress and person and present a professional
appearance to the public.  (Ord. 19699 § 21, 2023:  Ord. 17892 § 66, 2014:  Ord.
17665 § 25, 2013:  Ord. 15263 § 10, 2005:  Ord. 10498 §§ 69-79, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.690  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Driver – soliciting and
cruising standards.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  A driver
shall load or unload passengers at Sea-Tac airport only as permitted by the
Sea-Tac International Airport Schedule of Rules and Regulations.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  A driver shall
not drive, be in control of or operate a vehicle to pick up passengers at
Sea-Tac airport without having on display a Port of Seattle authorized permit.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  A driver
shall not solicit on Sea-Tac property.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  A driver
shall not hold out for designated destinations.  (Ord. 19699 § 22, 2023:  Ord. 18728
§ 79, 2018:  Ord. 17892 § 67, 2014:  Ord. 10498 §§ 80 - 85, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.740  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Director – annual
report.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  On or
before April 30 of each year, the director shall file an annual report with the
council for January 1 through December 31 of the preceding calendar year.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The report
shall include, but not be limited to:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  Number
of transportation network company endorsed vehicles in King County, in Seattle
only and in both King County and Seattle during the reporting period and during
the preceding year;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Number
of drivers licensed in King County only, Seattle only and in both King County
and Seattle during the reporting period and during the preceding year;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  Numbers
and nature of complaints;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  Any
other recommendations deemed appropriate by the director.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  The report
required by this section shall be filed in the form of a paper original and an
electronic copy with the clerk of the council, who shall retain the paper
original and distribute electronic copies to all councilmembers.  (Ord. 19699 §
23, 2023:  Ord. 17892 § 72, 2014:  Ord. 17665 § 27, 2013:  Ord. 10498 § 93,
1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.760  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Rates - requirements.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.1. 
Transportation network companies that use an application dispatch system shall
file with the director documentation or provide a physical demonstration of the
application dispatch rate structure that is visible to a passenger before the
passenger confirms a ride.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  The
director shall approve the rate structure as transparent if, when a passenger
requests a ride but before the passenger accepts the ride, the application
clearly displays:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                a.  the
total fare or fare range;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                b.  the
rate by distance or time; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                c.  any
variables that may result in a higher fare or additional charges; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  the cost
of the ride is made clear to the passenger before the passenger confirms the
ride through an alternative method approved by the director.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The rates
specified in this section shall not apply to transportation of persons provided
pursuant to a written contract that establishes a fare at a different rate for
specified transportation and that has been previously filed with the director. 
No contract may include any provision that directly or indirectly requires
exclusive use of the transportation services of the contracting taxicab or
for-hire vehicle.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  It is
unlawful to make any discriminatory charges to any person or to make any rebate
or in any manner reduce the charge to any person, unless the charge conforms to
the discounts or surcharges contained in the filed rates.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  A
transportation network company may not impose additional charges for providing
services to persons with disabilities because of those disabilities, consistent
with RCW 46.72B.110.  (Ord. 19699 § 24, 2023:  Ord. 17892 § 73, 2014:  Ord.
17404 § 3, 2012:  Ord. 16234 § 1, 2008:  Ord. 15132 § 1, 2005:  Ord. 10498 §
95, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=DE
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>            6.64.780  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Reports by
transportation network companies and for-hire drivers.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE style='font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>            A.  A transportation network
company shall:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              1. 
Submit quarterly the following reports in an electronic format approved by the
director:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                a. 
total number of rides provided by each transportation network company;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                b. 
type of dispatch for each ride, including whether by hail, telephone or
application dispatch;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                c. 
percentage or number of rides picked up in each ZIP code;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                d. 
pickup and drop off ZIP codes of each ride; </span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                e. 
percentage by ZIP code of rides requested by telephone or application dispatch
that are requested but not provided;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                f. 
vehicle collisions, including the name of the driver, identification of the
vehicle, collision fault, injuries and estimated damage;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                g. 
number of requested rides for an accessible vehicle; </span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                h. 
crimes against drivers;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                i. 
passenger complaints; and</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                j. 
other information reasonably determined by the director as necessary to ensure
compliance with this chapter by transportation network companies;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              2. 
Retain for at least two years records related to the reports required under
subsection A. of this section.  Records may be maintained electronically; and</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              3. 
Provide instructions to its for-hire drivers for weekly reporting to the
company or association the information needed for the reports in subsection
A.1. of this section.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            B. 
For-hire drivers comply with the reporting requirements in subsection A.3. of
this section.  (Ord. 17892 § 74, 2014).</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><u><span lang=DE><span
 style='text-decoration:none'>&nbsp;</span></span></u></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=DE>            6.64.790 
</span></b><b>Licensees – protection of information that is confidential,
proprietary or business secrets – procedures for disclosure and release of
materials subject to disclosure.</b>  <span lang=DE>If a licensee considers any
portion of any record provided to the county under this chapter, whether in
electronic or hard copy form, to be protected under law, the licensee shall
clearly identify each such portion with words such as &quot;confidential,&quot;
&quot;proprietary&quot; or &quot;business secret.&quot;  If a request is made
for disclosure of such portion under the state Public Records Act, the county
will determine whether the material should be made available.  If the county
determines that the material is subject to disclosure, the county will notify
the licensee of the request and allow the licensee ten business days to take
whatever action it deems necessary to protect its interests.  If the licensee
fails or neglects to take such action within ten days, the county will release
the portions of records deemed by the county to be subject to disclosure. 
(Ord. 17892 § 75, 2014).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.800  </span></b><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Penalties<span
style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>.</span></span></b></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            A.1.  The
director may assess the following civil penalties:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                a.  up
to ten thousand dollars for each violation of the following:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                  (1) 
K.C.C. 6.64.201; and</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                  (2) 
K.C.C. 6.64.251;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                b.  up
to one thousand dollars for a violation of any of the following:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                  (1) 
K.C.C. 6.64.261;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                  (2) 
K.C.C. 6.64.300;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                  (3) 
K.C.C. 6.64.360;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                  (4) 
K.C.C. 6.64.500;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                  (5) 
K.C.C. 6.64.640;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                  (6) 
K.C.C. 6.64.650;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                  (7) 
K.C.C. 6.64.660;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                  (8) 
K.C.C. 6.64.665;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                  (9) 
K.C.C. 6.64.680; and</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>                  (10) 
K.C.C. 6.64.690.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              2.  In
determining a penalty under subsection A.1. of this section, the director shall
consider:  the size of the business of the violator; the gravity of the
violation; the number of past and present violations committed; and the good
faith of the violator in attempting to achieve compliance after notification of
the violation.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>            B.  As an
alternative to the civil penalties in subsection A. of this section:</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              1.  A
violation of K.C.C. 6.64.300, K.C.C. 6.64.500 or K.C.C. 6.64.261 is a Class 1
civil infraction and shall subject the violator to a maximum monetary penalty
and default amount of one thousand dollars, inclusive of statutory
assessments.  An infraction under this subsection shall be initiated and
processed under the Infraction Rules for Courts of Limited Jurisdiction, and
the director is the enforcement officer under RCW 7.80.040.  A person who is
issued a notice of infraction shall not be assessed a civil penalty under
subsection A. of this section for the same violation.  In determining whether
to issue a notice of infraction instead of a civil penalty under subsection A.
of this section, the director shall consider whether it would be a more
efficient method of providing notice to persons who are in violation.</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=DE>              2.  Each
subsequent violation of K.C.C. 6.64.300, K.C.C. 6.64.500 or K.C.C. 6.64.261 within
five years of the prior violation is a misdemeanor.  A person who is prosecuted
for the misdemeanor in this subsection shall not be issued a notice of civil
infraction or assessed a civil penalty for the same violation.  In determining
whether to refer a person for prosecution for a misdemeanor, the director shall
consider whether it would be a deterrent to future violations.  (</span><span
style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Ord. 19699 § 26, 2023:  </span><span lang=DE>Ord.
17892 § 76, 2014:  Ord. 10498 § 97, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=DE>            6.64.830 
</span></b><b>Notice and order of denial, suspension, revocation of license or
assessment of civil penalty.</b>  <span lang=DE>If the director denies,
suspends or revokes a license or assesses a civil penalty under this chapter,
the director shall issue a notice and order under K.C.C. 6.01.130.  (Ord. 17892
§ 77, 2014).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.900  Consumer
complaint hotline.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The director may establish, in conjunction with the city
of Seattle and the Port of Seattle, a shared consumer complaint telephone
number and complaint process.  (Ord. 17892 § 78, 2014:  Ord. 10498 § 100,
1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            6.64.910  Passenger
complaint process.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Upon
receiving a written complaint involving the conduct of a for-hire driver, the
route of transportation, the rate charged for the transportation or passenger
injury or property damage not arising from a vehicle accident, the director
shall:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  Issue a
notice of complaint to the for-hire driver and vehicle owner, taxicab
association or transportation network company, as applicable, advising them of
the allegations made in the complaint;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Require
the for-hire driver and vehicle owner, association or company, as applicable,
to respond, in writing, to the allegations in the notice of complaint within
ten days of receipt of the notice of complaint;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  Investigate
the allegations in the written complaint and the response submitted by the
for-hire driver and vehicle owner, association or company, as applicable; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4.  Make a
finding as to the validity of the allegations in the written complaint.  If it
is found to be a valid complaint the director shall issue a notice and order under
K.C.C. 6.01.130.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  Failure to
respond in writing to a notice of complaint within ten days shall constitute a
waiver of the for-hire driver's, vehicle owner's, association's or company's right
to contest the allegations in the written complaint and shall be prima facie
evidence that the allegations are valid.  The director shall issue a notice and
order under K.C.C. 6.01.130 if there is a failure to respond in writing.  (Ord.
17892 § 79, 2014:  Ord. 10498 § 101, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

